(173, 'Auto Post for facebook at 14:00', 'The iconic Barbie doll. Created by Ruth Handler and launched by Mattel, Inc. in 1959, Barbie has become a cultural phenomenon and a staple in many children\'s toy collections.\n\n**History of Barbie**\n\nThe idea for Barbie was born when Ruth Handler, the co-founder of Mattel, observed her daughter playing with paper dolls. Handler realized that there was a gap in the market for a doll that allowed children to engage in imaginative play and explore different roles and careers. The first Barbie doll was launched at the American International Toy Fair in New York City on March 9, 1959. The doll was named after Handler\'s daughter, Barbara.\n\n**Characteristics and Features**\n\nBarbie dolls are known for their distinctive physical characteristics, including:\n\n* A slender, curvaceous figure\n* Long hair, often styled in a variety of ways\n* A wide range of skin tones, hair colors, and eye colors\n* A variety of outfits and accessories, from casual wear to formal gowns\n\nOver the years, Barbie has undergone many changes, including the introduction of new body types, skin tones, and hairstyles. In 2016, Mattel launched a new line of Barbie dolls with more diverse body types, including curvy, tall, and petite.\n\n**Impact and Controversy**\n\nBarbie has had a significant impact on popular culture, with many children growing up with the dolls and using them to explore their creativity and imagination. However, Barbie has also been the subject of controversy, with some critics arguing that the dolls promote unrealistic beauty standards and reinforce negative stereotypes about women.\n\n**Collectibility and Cultural Significance**\n\nBarbie dolls have become highly collectible, with rare and vintage dolls selling for thousands of dollars. The dolls have also been the subject of numerous exhibitions and artworks, including a 2015 exhibition at the Musée des Arts Décoratifs in Paris.\n\n**Fun Facts**\n\n* The first Barbie doll wore a black and white striped swimsuit and high heels.\n* Barbie has had over 150 careers, including astronaut, doctor, and rock star.\n* The most expensive Barbie doll ever sold was a 1959 Barbie doll that sold for $27,450 in 2010.\n* Barbie has been inducted into the National Toy Hall of Fame.\n\nOverall, Barbie is an iconic and enduring symbol of childhood imagination and creativity, with a rich history and cultural significance that continues to inspire and fascinate people around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-17 14:00:00', '2025-12-17 14:00:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Barbie_Doll?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 25, '2025-12-17 14:00:26', '2025-12-17 14:00:26'),
