(227, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:39', 'Here\'s a relatable caption for Roddies Fashion on Facebook:\n\n\"Stay on top of your fashion game with Roddies! Here\'s why you\'ll love us:\n* Trendy and affordable clothing for all occasions\n* High-quality materials that will make you feel confident and stylish\n* New arrivals every week to keep your wardrobe fresh\n* Easy returns and exchanges for a hassle-free shopping experience\n\nFollow us for the latest fashion updates and get ready to elevate your style! #RoddiesFashion #TrendingNow #FashionForward #StyleInspo #NewArrivals #FashionLover #MustHaves #TrendyClothing #AffordableFashion #QualityMatters\"\n\nThis caption is professional, relatable, and includes trending hashtags to increase visibility and engagement on Facebook.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-19 11:39:00', '2025-12-19 11:39:09', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Umbrella?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 35, '2025-12-19 11:39:09', '2025-12-19 11:39:09'),
(228, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:50', 'Jewellery, also known as jewelry, is a form of personal adornment that has been a part of human culture for thousands of years. It is typically made from precious metals, gemstones, and other materials, and is used to add beauty, elegance, and style to an individual\'s appearance.\n\nTypes of Jewellery:\n\n1. **Fine Jewellery**: Made from precious metals like gold, silver, and platinum, and featuring gemstones like diamonds, rubies, and emeralds.\n2. **Fashion Jewellery**: More affordable and trendy, often made from base metals and synthetic materials.\n3. **Costume Jewellery**: Designed to make a statement, often featuring bold designs and bright colors.\n4. **Bridal Jewellery**: Specialized jewellery for weddings and engagements, often featuring diamonds and other precious stones.\n5. **Ethnic Jewellery**: Inspired by traditional cultures and folklore, often featuring unique materials and designs.\n\nPopular Jewellery Items:\n\n1. **Rings**: Engagement rings, wedding bands, signet rings, and more.\n2. **Earrings**: Studs, drops, hoops, and dangling earrings.\n3. **Necklaces**: Pendants, chains, and collars.\n4. **Bracelets**: Bangles, cuffs, and charm bracelets.\n5. **Brooches**: Decorative pins and clasps.\n\nMaterials Used in Jewellery:\n\n1. **Precious Metals**: Gold, silver, platinum, and palladium.\n2. **Gemstones**: Diamonds, rubies, emeralds, sapphires, and more.\n3. **Base Metals**: Copper, brass, and zinc.\n4. **Synthetic Materials**: Plastic, glass, and ceramic.\n5. **Organic Materials**: Pearls, ivory, and wood.\n\nJewellery Making Techniques:\n\n1. **Casting**: Molten metal is poured into a mold to create a shape.\n2. **Forging**: Metal is heated and shaped using a hammer and anvil.\n3. **Soldering**: Metal pieces are joined together using a torch and solder.\n4. **Enameling**: Glass or ceramic is applied to metal using heat and chemicals.\n5. **Setting**: Gemstones are secured into metal using prongs, claws, or bezels.\n\nFamous Jewellery Designers:\n\n1. **Tiffany & Co.**: Known for their iconic blue boxes and elegant designs.\n2. **Cartier**: Renowned for their luxurious and sophisticated jewellery.\n3. **David Yurman**: Famous for their cable motif and stylish designs.\n4. **Bulgari**: Italian luxury brand known for their bold and colorful jewellery.\n5. **Van Cleef & Arpels**: French jewellery house famous for their poetic and whimsical designs.\n\nOverall, jewellery is a unique and personal way to express oneself, and with so many different styles, materials, and techniques to choose from, there\'s something for everyone.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-19 11:50:00', '2025-12-19 11:50:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://picsum.photos/seed/947/1024/1024', NULL, 'pending', 36, '2025-12-19 11:50:24', '2025-12-19 11:50:24'),
(229, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:50', 'Jewellery, also spelled jewelry, is a form of personal adornment that has been a part of human culture for thousands of years. It is typically made from precious metals, gemstones, and other materials, and is worn for a variety of reasons, including:\n\n1. **Aesthetic appeal**: Jewellery is often worn to add beauty and style to an outfit.\n2. **Symbolism**: Jewellery can be used to convey meaning, such as a wedding ring symbolizing marriage or a cross symbolizing faith.\n3. **Status**: Jewellery can be used to display wealth and status, such as a diamond necklace or a gold watch.\n4. **Cultural significance**: Jewellery can be an important part of cultural and traditional practices, such as a henna tattoo or a bindi.\n\nTypes of Jewellery:\n\n1. **Fine jewellery**: Made from precious metals and gemstones, such as gold, silver, diamonds, and rubies.\n2. **Fashion jewellery**: Made from less expensive materials, such as base metals, plastics, and synthetic gemstones.\n3. **Costume jewellery**: Made from inexpensive materials, often used for decorative purposes.\n4. **Body jewellery**: Includes piercings, such as earrings, nose rings, and belly button rings.\n\nPopular Types of Jewellery:\n\n1. **Rings**: Engagement rings, wedding rings, signet rings, and cocktail rings.\n2. **Earrings**: Studs, drops, hoops, and chandeliers.\n3. **Necklaces**: Pendants, chains, and collars.\n4. **Bracelets**: Bangles, cuffs, and charm bracelets.\n5. **Brooches**: Used to fasten clothing or as a decorative piece.\n\nJewellery can be made from a variety of materials, including:\n\n1. **Metals**: Gold, silver, platinum, and copper.\n2. **Gemstones**: Diamonds, rubies, sapphires, emeralds, and pearls.\n3. **Plastics**: Acrylic, polyurethane, and polycarbonate.\n4. **Organic materials**: Wood, bone, and shell.\n\nThe history of jewellery dates back to ancient civilizations, with evidence of jewellery-making found in ancient Egypt, Greece, and Rome. Today, jewellery is a global industry, with designers and manufacturers creating a wide range of styles and pieces for different markets and cultures.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-19 11:50:00', '2025-12-19 11:50:38', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://picsum.photos/seed/947/1024/1024', NULL, 'pending', 36, '2025-12-19 11:50:38', '2025-12-19 11:50:38');
