(230, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:50', 'Jewellery, also spelled jewelry, is a form of personal adornment that consists of decorative items worn for personal or cultural significance. It can be made from a wide range of materials, including metals, gemstones, beads, and other substances.\n\nTypes of Jewellery:\n\n1. **Fine Jewellery**: High-end jewellery made from precious metals like gold, silver, and platinum, often featuring diamonds and other gemstones.\n2. **Fashion Jewellery**: Trendy and affordable jewellery made from base metals, plastics, and other materials, often featuring bold designs and bright colors.\n3. **Costume Jewellery**: Theatrical and dramatic jewellery made for stage or screen performances, often featuring oversized or elaborate designs.\n4. **Ethnic Jewellery**: Traditional jewellery from specific cultures or regions, often featuring unique materials and designs.\n5. **Body Jewellery**: Jewellery designed to be worn on or in the body, such as piercings, implants, or other forms of body modification.\n\nPopular Types of Jewellery:\n\n1. **Rings**: Worn on the fingers, often featuring gemstones or other decorative elements.\n2. **Necklaces**: Worn around the neck, often featuring pendants, beads, or other decorative elements.\n3. **Earrings**: Worn on the ears, often featuring drops, studs, or other decorative elements.\n4. **Bracelets**: Worn on the wrists, often featuring charms, beads, or other decorative elements.\n5. **Brooches**: Worn on clothing, often featuring pins, clasps, or other decorative elements.\n\nMaterials Used in Jewellery:\n\n1. **Gold**: A precious metal often used in fine jewellery, available in various colors like yellow, white, and rose.\n2. **Silver**: A precious metal often used in fine jewellery, known for its bright white color and affordability.\n3. **Platinum**: A rare and durable metal often used in high-end jewellery, known for its strength and white color.\n4. **Gemstones**: Precious or semi-precious stones like diamonds, rubies, emeralds, and sapphires, often used in fine jewellery.\n5. **Beads**: Small, decorative elements made from materials like glass, ceramic, or metal, often used in fashion jewellery.\n\nJewellery has been a part of human culture for thousands of years, with various civilizations using it to express social status, wealth, and personal style. Today, jewellery is a global industry, with designers and manufacturers creating a wide range of pieces to suit different tastes, budgets, and occasions.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-19 11:50:00', '2025-12-19 11:50:52', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://picsum.photos/seed/947/1024/1024', NULL, 'pending', 36, '2025-12-19 11:50:52', '2025-12-19 11:50:52'),
(231, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-fitted suit in black, navy, or gray is a classic choice for formal parties.\n2. **Tuxedos**: A tuxedo is perfect for black-tie events and can be paired with a bow tie or a long tie.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A crisp, white dress shirt with a wingtip collar is a versatile choice that can be paired with a suit or a blazer.\n4. **Blazers**: A navy or charcoal gray blazer can add a touch of sophistication to a dress shirt and trousers.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Dress Pants**: Dark-washed dress pants can be paired with a dress shirt and a blazer for a semi-formal look.\n2. **Button-Down Shirts**: A button-down shirt in a bold color or pattern can add a touch of personality to a semi-formal outfit.\n3. **Sports Coats**: A sports coat in a bold color or pattern can add a touch of elegance to a semi-formal outfit.\n4. **Dark Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans can be paired with a dress shirt and a blazer for a semi-formal look.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Polos**: A polo shirt in a bold color or pattern can be a great choice for a casual party.\n2. **T-Shirts**: A plain or graphic T-shirt can be paired with jeans or trousers for a casual look.\n3. **Chinos**: Light-washed chinos can be paired with a polo or T-shirt for a casual look.\n4. **Jackets**: A leather jacket or a denim jacket can add a touch of edge to a casual outfit.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Ties**: A tie can add a touch of elegance to a formal or semi-formal outfit.\n2. **Pocket Squares**: A pocket square can add a touch of personality to a formal or semi-formal outfit.\n3. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to a formal outfit.\n4. **Shoes**: Dress shoes, loafers, or boots can complete a party outfit.\n\n**Grooming:**\n\n1. **Hair**: Style your hair with a pomade or a hair gel to add a touch of sophistication.\n2. **Beard**: Trim your beard to add a touch of elegance to your outfit.\n3. **Fragrance**: Wear a fragrance that complements your outfit and personality.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Experiment with different styles and find what works best for you!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-19 12:40:00', '2025-12-19 12:40:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://picsum.photos/seed/1753/1024/1024', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2025-12-19 12:40:24', '2025-12-19 12:40:24'),
(232, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a point collar, spread collar, or a cutaway collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or button cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the chest and waist.\n5. **Button-front**: Formal shirts usually have a button-front closure.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a point collar and French cuffs.\n2. **Business shirt**: A formal shirt with a spread collar and button cuffs.\n3. **Wing-tip shirt**: A formal shirt with a wing-tip collar and French cuffs.\n4. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt with a starched front and a detachable collar.\n5. **Dress shirt with contrasting cuffs**: A formal shirt with contrasting cuffs and collar.\n\n**Colors and Patterns:**\n\n1. **White**: A classic choice for formal shirts.\n2. **Light blue**: A popular choice for business and formal events.\n3. **Pastel colors**: Soft pink, baby blue, and pale yellow are popular choices for spring and summer.\n4. **Stripes**: Thin stripes are a classic pattern for formal shirts.\n5. **Checks**: Small checks are a subtle pattern for formal shirts.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: Known for their high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand that offers luxurious, bespoke formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: An American brand that offers classic, formal shirts with a preppy twist.\n4. **Armani**: An Italian brand that offers stylish, modern formal shirts.\n5. **Hugo Boss**: A German brand that offers high-quality, fashion-forward formal shirts.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Choose a shirt that fits well**: A well-fitting shirt is essential for a formal look.\n2. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a shirt that is suitable for the occasion, such as a black-tie event or a business meeting.\n3. **Pay attention to details**: Make sure the shirt is well-made, with attention to details such as stitching and buttons.\n4. **Accessories matter**: Pair the shirt with a tie, pocket square, and cufflinks to complete the formal look.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-19 12:56:00', '2025-12-19 12:56:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://picsum.photos/seed/2021/1024/1024', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2025-12-19 12:56:23', '2025-12-19 12:56:23'),
