(455, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear**\n\n1. **Tuxedos**: A classic choice for formal parties, tuxedos are available in various styles, including single-breasted, double-breasted, and peak lapel.\n2. **Suits**: A well-fitted suit in navy, black, or gray is a versatile option for formal parties.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A crisp, white dress shirt with a wingtip collar is a timeless choice.\n4. **Bow Ties**: Add a touch of elegance with a bow tie in a bold color or pattern.\n5. **Cufflinks**: Complete the look with stylish cufflinks.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A navy or charcoal gray blazer with a dress shirt and dark jeans is a stylish option.\n2. **Dress Pants**: Dark-washed dress pants with a button-down shirt and a blazer create a sharp look.\n3. **Polo Shirts**: A high-quality polo shirt in a bold color or pattern can add a touch of sophistication.\n4. **Loafers**: Slip-on loafers or dress shoes in leather or suede are great options.\n5. **Accessories**: Add a pocket square, watch, or simple necklace to complete the look.\n\n**Casual Party Wear**\n\n1. **Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans with a stylish top and shoes can create a stylish, casual look.\n2. **Graphic T-Shirts**: A bold, graphic tee with a pair of distressed denim jeans is perfect for a casual party.\n3. **Hoodies**: A stylish hoodie with a pair of sweatpants or jeans is great for a relaxed party vibe.\n4. **Sneakers**: Sneakers in bold colors or stylish designs can add a fun touch to a casual outfit.\n5. **Hats**: A baseball cap or beanie can add a cool, casual touch to an outfit.\n\n**Trendy Party Wear**\n\n1. **Slim-Fit Suits**: A slim-fit suit in a bold color or pattern can create a stylish, modern look.\n2. **Patterned Shirts**: A bold, patterned shirt with a pair of dark-washed jeans can add a touch of personality to an outfit.\n3. **Monochromatic Outfits**: A monochromatic outfit in a bold color can create a stylish, cohesive look.\n4. **Statement Accessories**: A bold, statement piece of jewelry or a patterned scarf can add a touch of personality to an outfit.\n5. **Bold Colors**: Incorporate bold, bright colors into an outfit to create a fun, party-ready look.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing for a party is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Choose an outfit that reflects your personal style and the party\'s dress code, and don\'t be afraid to add your own unique touches to make your look stand out.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-31 12:40:00', '2025-12-31 12:40:13', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2025-12-31 12:40:13', '2025-12-31 12:40:13'),
(456, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key characteristics of a formal shirt for men:\n\n**Types of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress Shirt:** A classic dress shirt with a point or spread collar, French cuffs, and a fitted silhouette.\n2. **Business Shirt:** A shirt with a more relaxed fit, often with a button-down collar and button cuffs.\n3. **Tuxedo Shirt:** A special type of formal shirt designed to be worn with a tuxedo, typically with a wingtip collar and stud buttons.\n\n**Features of a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Collar:** A formal shirt typically has a point, spread, or wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuffs:** French cuffs or button cuffs are common on formal shirts.\n3. **Front:** A formal shirt usually has a placket front with buttons or studs.\n4. **Sleeves:** Long sleeves are typical, but some formal shirts may have short sleeves.\n5. **Fabric:** Formal shirts are often made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n6. **Buttons:** Mother-of-pearl or plastic buttons are commonly used on formal shirts.\n7. **Pockets:** Some formal shirts may have a pocket on the left side, but it\'s not a standard feature.\n\n**Popular Styles:**\n\n1. **Classic Fit:** A traditional fit with a relaxed silhouette.\n2. **Slim Fit:** A more modern fit with a narrower silhouette.\n3. **Tailored Fit:** A fitted silhouette with a nipped-in waist.\n4. **Cutaway Collar:** A collar style with a wider spread, often worn with a tie.\n\n**Colors and Patterns:**\n\n1. **White:** A classic choice for formal shirts.\n2. **Light Blue:** A popular alternative to white.\n3. **Pastel Colors:** Soft pink, baby blue, or pale yellow can add a touch of elegance.\n4. **Stripes:** Subtle stripes can add texture and interest to a formal shirt.\n5. **Checks:** Small checks or grids can add a touch of sophistication.\n\n**Brands and Prices:**\n\n1. **Luxury Brands:** Tom Ford, Ralph Lauren, and Burberry offer high-end formal shirts with prices ranging from $100 to $500.\n2. **Mid-Range Brands:** Calvin Klein, Hugo Boss, and Ted Baker offer high-quality formal shirts with prices ranging from $50 to $200.\n3. **Affordable Brands:** Uniqlo, H&M, and Zara offer budget-friendly formal shirts with prices ranging from $10 to $50.\n\nRemember, the key to a great formal shirt is a good fit, high-quality fabric, and attention to detail.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2025-12-31 12:56:00', '2025-12-31 12:56:13', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2025-12-31 12:56:13', '2025-12-31 12:56:13'),
