(511, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Party wear for men can vary depending on the type of party, the dress code, and personal style. Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Parties:**\n\n1. **Tuxedos**: A classic choice for black-tie events, tuxedos are sleek and sophisticated.\n2. **Suits**: A well-fitted suit in navy, black, or gray is a timeless choice for formal parties.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A crisp, white dress shirt with a wing-tip collar is a must-have for formal events.\n4. **Bow Ties**: Add a touch of elegance with a bow tie in a subtle pattern or color.\n\n**Semi-Formal Parties:**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A navy or gray blazer can add a touch of sophistication to a dress shirt and trousers.\n2. **Dress Pants**: Dark-washed dress pants in wool or cotton are versatile and stylish.\n3. **Polo Shirts**: A high-quality polo shirt in a bold color or pattern can add a pop of personality.\n4. **Loafers**: Slip-on loafers or dress shoes can complete a semi-formal look.\n\n**Casual Parties:**\n\n1. **Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans are a staple for casual parties.\n2. **Graphic T-Shirts**: A fun, graphic tee can add a playful touch to a casual outfit.\n3. **Hoodies**: A lightweight hoodie can be a great layering piece for a casual party.\n4. **Sneakers**: Comfortable sneakers in bold colors or patterns can add a stylish touch.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Watches**: A leather-strapped watch can add a touch of sophistication to a party outfit.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Simple cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to a dress shirt.\n3. **Pocket Squares**: A pocket square in a bold color or pattern can add a pop of personality.\n4. **Belts**: A high-quality leather belt can complete a party outfit.\n\n**Trends:**\n\n1. **Slim-Fit**: Slim-fit suits, trousers, and shirts are popular for their streamlined look.\n2. **Bold Colors**: Bold, bright colors are trending in party wear, from suits to accessories.\n3. **Patterns**: Subtle patterns like stripes, checks, and polka dots can add visual interest to a party outfit.\n4. **Mix-and-Match**: Mixing and matching different patterns, textures, and colors can create a unique and stylish party look.\n\nRemember, the key to pulling off a great party look is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Experiment with different styles and find what works best for you!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-01-03 12:40:00', '2026-01-03 12:40:12', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-01-03 12:40:12', '2026-01-03 12:40:12'),
(512, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a pointed or spread collar, which is designed to accommodate a tie.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs, which are also known as double cuffs. These cuffs are designed to be fastened with cufflinks.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality cotton or cotton-blend fabrics, such as Oxford cloth or pinpoint cotton.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely, with a slim fit through the body and sleeves.\n5. **Button-front**: Formal shirts usually have a button-front closure, with buttons made from mother-of-pearl or other high-quality materials.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a pointed collar and French cuffs.\n2. **Business shirt**: A slightly more relaxed version of the dress shirt, with a spread collar and button cuffs.\n3. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt designed to be worn with a tuxedo, typically with a wingtip collar and French cuffs.\n4. **Dress shirt with contrast cuffs**: A formal shirt with contrast-colored cuffs and collar, adding a touch of elegance to the overall design.\n\n**Colors and Patterns:**\n\n1. **White**: A classic choice for formal shirts, white is a timeless and versatile option.\n2. **Light blue**: A popular alternative to white, light blue formal shirts are perfect for business and formal events.\n3. **Pastel colors**: Soft pastel colors, such as pale pink or baby blue, can add a touch of elegance to a formal shirt.\n4. **Stripes and checks**: Subtle stripes and checks can add visual interest to a formal shirt, while still maintaining a professional look.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: A luxury brand known for its high-quality formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand that offers exquisite formal shirts with a focus on craftsmanship and attention to detail.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: An American brand that offers classic formal shirts with a preppy twist.\n4. **Ted Baker**: A British brand that offers stylish and affordable formal shirts with a focus on fashion and quality.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Choose a shirt that fits well**: A well-fitting formal shirt is essential for making a good impression.\n2. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a formal shirt that is suitable for the occasion, whether it\'s a business meeting or a formal event.\n3. **Pay attention to details**: Make sure the shirt is well-made, with attention to details such as stitching and button quality.\n4. **Accessories**: Don\'t forget to add a tie, cufflinks, and other accessories to complete the formal look.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-01-03 12:56:00', '2026-01-03 12:56:12', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-01-03 12:56:12', '2026-01-03 12:56:12'),
