(565, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:05', 'A bicycle, also known as a bike, is a human-powered or motor-powered, pedal-driven, single-track vehicle, having two wheels attached to a frame, one behind the other. Bicycles are a popular mode of transportation, recreation, and sport.\n\nHere are some interesting facts about bicycles:\n\n1. **Invention**: The first bicycle was invented in 1817 by German Baron Karl von Drais. It had no pedals and was powered by the rider\'s feet pushing against the ground.\n2. **Evolution**: Over the years, bicycles have evolved to include various designs, materials, and technologies, such as gears, brakes, and suspension systems.\n3. **Types**: There are many types of bicycles, including road bikes, mountain bikes, hybrid bikes, commuting bikes, and racing bikes, each designed for specific purposes and terrain.\n4. **Health benefits**: Cycling is a great way to improve cardiovascular health, build muscle, and increase flexibility. It\'s also a low-impact exercise that can be easy on the joints.\n5. **Environmental benefits**: Bicycles are an eco-friendly mode of transportation, producing no emissions or pollution, and reducing the need for fossil fuels.\n6. **Recreation**: Cycling is a popular recreational activity, with many people enjoying bike rides for leisure, fitness, and socializing.\n7. **Competition**: Cycling is also a competitive sport, with professional bike racing events, such as the Tour de France, and Olympic competitions.\n\nSome common bicycle components include:\n\n* Frame: The main structure of the bicycle\n* Wheels: The round, rotating parts that make contact with the ground\n* Pedals: The platforms that the rider pushes to propel the bicycle\n* Gears: The systems that allow the rider to change the difficulty of pedaling\n* Brakes: The mechanisms that slow or stop the bicycle\n* Seat: The cushioned area where the rider sits\n* Handlebars: The bars that the rider holds onto for steering and control\n\nOverall, bicycles are an efficient, fun, and environmentally friendly way to get around, and they offer many benefits for recreation, transportation, and overall well-being.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-01-06 12:05:00', '2026-01-06 12:05:11', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/girl_walking_with_a_transparent_umbrella_in_light_rain%2C_neon_reflections_on_wet_street%2C_aesthetic_photography%2C_soft_bokeh_lights%2C_fashionable_outfit%2C_cinematic_mood%2C_high-detail%2C_girl_walking_with_a_transparent_umbrella_in_light_rain%2C_neon_reflections_on_wet_street%2C_aesthetic_photography%2C_soft_bokeh_lights%2C_fashionable_outfit%2C_cinematic_mood%2C_high-detail%2C?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 18, '2026-01-06 12:05:11', '2026-01-06 12:05:11'),
