(897, 'pablo escobar', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely considered one of the most infamous and successful criminals in history. Here\'s a brief overview of his life and reign:\r\n\r\n**Early Life**\r\n\r\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned them. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working as a car thief and smuggler.\r\n\r\n**Rise to Power**\r\n\r\nIn the 1970s, Escobar started working for the Medellín cartel, a major cocaine trafficking organization. He quickly rose through the ranks, becoming a key figure in the cartel\'s operations. In 1976, he was arrested for cocaine possession, but he bribed his way out of prison.\r\n\r\n**Medellín Cartel**\r\n\r\nIn the 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the Medellín cartel, which controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade. He expanded the cartel\'s operations, establishing a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutal tactics, including murder, intimidation, and bribery.\r\n\r\n**Wealth and Extravagance**\r\n\r\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world. He lived a life of luxury, owning numerous properties, including a sprawling estate called Hacienda Napoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars.\r\n\r\n**Violence and Notoriety**\r\n\r\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by violence and bloodshed. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including rival cartel members, police officers, and innocent civilians. He also ordered the assassination of Colombian politicians, judges, and journalists who opposed him.\r\n\r\n**Manhunt and Death**\r\n\r\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility, which he designed himself. However, he escaped in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt ensued, with Colombian and American authorities working together to capture him.\r\n\r\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\r\n\r\n**Legacy**\r\n\r\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a folk hero by some, who view him as a champion of the poor and a symbol of resistance against government corruption and oppression.\r\n\r\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, serving as a reminder of the destructive power of crime and corruption.', '[\"Facebook\"]', 'draft', 1, 'pablo escobar', NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pablo escobar', 'https://res.cloudinary.com/diapmjeoc/image/upload/v1773033157/user_2_test21/fqm3v01hhqvjh6tq4scq.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, '2026-03-09 10:42:38', '2026-03-09 10:42:38'),
(898, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug cartels in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. His father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. Escobar grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in crime at a young age. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working as a car thief and a smuggler.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to build his cocaine empire, smuggling the drug from Colombia to the United States and other countries. He quickly rose to prominence in the Medellín cartel, becoming one of its top leaders. Escobar\'s success was due in part to his cunning, ruthlessness, and ability to bribe and intimidate government officials and law enforcement.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world. The cartel\'s operations were highly organized, with a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. Escobar\'s organization was responsible for smuggling hundreds of tons of cocaine into the United States, earning him an estimated $30 billion in revenue.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his brutal tactics, including murder, kidnapping, and intimidation. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, and journalists. Escobar\'s organization also carried out bombings and other terrorist attacks against government targets.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped from prison in 1992. A year later, on December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen by some as a folk hero, who used his wealth and power to benefit his community and provide for his family. Escobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world at the time.\n* He owned a private zoo, which included exotic animals such as lions, tigers, and elephants.\n* Escobar was a skilled soccer player and even sponsored a local soccer team.\n* He was known for his love of luxury cars and owned a collection of high-end vehicles, including a Mercedes-Benz 600 and a Porsche 911.\n* Escobar\'s grave in Medellín has become a tourist attraction, with many visitors leaving flowers and paying their respects to the notorious drug lord.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-09 10:45:00', '2026-03-09 10:45:06', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-09 10:45:06', '2026-03-09 10:45:06'),
(899, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and one of the most notorious criminals of the 20th century. He was the leader of the Medellín cartel, a powerful and ruthless organization that dominated the global cocaine trade in the 1980s.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was exposed to crime from a young age. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working as a car thief and a smuggler.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia. He started as a small-time smuggler, but his charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness quickly propelled him to the top of the Medellín cartel. By the early 1980s, Escobar had become one of the most powerful men in Colombia, with a vast network of loyal associates and a stranglehold on the cocaine trade.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, led by Escobar, was a highly organized and efficient operation that controlled every aspect of the cocaine trade, from production to distribution. The cartel\'s profits were staggering, with estimates suggesting that Escobar earned over $20 billion per year. The cartel\'s influence extended beyond Colombia, with tentacles reaching into the United States, Europe, and other parts of South America.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by brutal violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and journalists. His organization used bombings, assassinations, and kidnappings to intimidate and eliminate opponents. Escobar\'s most notorious tactic was the use of \"plata o plomo\" (silver or lead), which meant that those who cooperated with him would be rewarded, while those who opposed him would be killed.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped in 1992. A massive manhunt ensued, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he was also a charismatic figure who was admired by some for his generosity and his ability to provide for his community. Today, Escobar\'s story has been immortalized in numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a mansion with a private airport.\n* He was a skilled soccer player and even sponsored a local soccer team in Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for the deaths of over 4,000 people, including 500 police officers.\n* He was named one of the \"10 Most Wanted\" fugitives by the FBI in 1991.\n* Escobar\'s brother, Roberto, was also involved in the cartel and was arrested in 1990.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-09 10:50:00', '2026-03-09 10:50:05', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-09 10:50:05', '2026-03-09 10:50:05'),
(900, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals in history.\n\nEarly Life:\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was exposed to crime from a young age.\n\nRise to Power:\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder and others. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him become the leader of the cartel, and he expanded its operations to become one of the largest and most powerful drug trafficking organizations in the world.\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world. He was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a massive hacienda.\n\nViolence and Terror:\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and rival gang members. He also ordered the bombing of a commercial airliner, Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people.\n\nEscobar\'s most notorious act of violence was the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989. Galán was a strong opponent of Escobar and had vowed to extradite him to the United States if elected.\n\nManhunt and Death:\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a special facility, known as the \"Catedral,\" which he had built himself. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\nA massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down by Colombian police and U.S. DEA agents. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed in a rooftop shootout in Medellín, Colombia. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\nLegacy:\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the United States, which many Colombians felt was interfering in their country\'s affairs.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, and his impact on Colombian history and culture is still felt today.\n\nSome interesting facts about Pablo Escobar:\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of soccer and even built a soccer field in his prison, the \"Catedral.\"\n* He was a fan of the Colombian soccer team, Atlético Nacional, and even sponsored the team.\n* Escobar\'s favorite car was the Mercedes-Benz 600, which he had customized with bulletproof glass and armor plating.\n* He was known for his generosity to the poor and often donated money and goods to those in need.\n* Escobar\'s death was celebrated by many Colombians, who saw him as a symbol of violence and terror. However, others mourned his passing, seeing him as a folk hero and a symbol of resistance against the government.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-09 10:53:00', '2026-03-09 10:53:06', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-09 10:53:06', '2026-03-09 10:53:06'),
(901, 'H2O', 'Here\'s a detailed description of the commercial product advertisement image:\r\n\r\nThe image features a premium matte black 1-liter water bottle placed in the center of the frame, with a sleek and modern cylindrical design that exudes durability and style. The bottle\'s smooth matte black finish is complemented by a metallic silver screw cap lid, adding a touch of sophistication to the overall design.\r\n\r\nRealistic water droplets and condensation on the bottle\'s surface give it a fresh and chilled look, as if it was just taken out of a refrigerator. The dramatic studio lighting creates soft reflections and subtle highlights on the matte surface, making the bottle look luxurious and eye-catching.\r\n\r\nThe background is a cinematic blend of multiple lifestyle environments, slightly blurred with depth of field. On one side, a modern gym environment with dumbbells and workout equipment is visible, while another side shows a clean office desk with a laptop and notebook. A nature outdoor setting with mountains and greenery is also visible, adding a sense of adventure and freedom to the image.\r\n\r\nThe bottle is placed on a dark reflective surface, with splashes of water and ice cubes around it, giving a refreshing hydration theme. Dynamic water splash effects around the bottle create motion and energy, as if water has just been poured.\r\n\r\nAt the top of the image, the headline \"STAY HYDRATED IN STYLE\" is prominently displayed in a bold, modern font. Below the bottle, the product title \"Premium Black Water Bottle\" is written in a clean and elegant font.\r\n\r\nOn the side of the image, feature bullet points highlight the bottle\'s key features:\r\n\r\n* 1 Liter Capacity\r\n* Sleek Matte Finish\r\n* Durable and Lightweight\r\n* Perfect for Gym, Office & Travel\r\n\r\nA bright promotional price tag badge in red is placed on the bottom left corner of the image, with bold text reading \"ONLY ₹499\". A small promotional line at the bottom of the image reads \"Limited Stock – Order Now!\", creating a sense of urgency and encouraging viewers to make a purchase.\r\n\r\nThe image is rendered in ultra-realistic 8K resolution, with cinematic lighting, sharp focus, and professional product photography style. The aspect ratio is 1:1, making it perfect for social media advertisement. The overall design is modern, elegant, and vibrant, with a focus on showcasing the premium product in a lifestyle setting.\r\n\r\nStyle references include product photography, commercial advertisement, cinematic lighting, hyper-realistic rendering, modern marketing poster design, ultra HD quality, studio photography, realistic reflections, and professional brand ad style. The image is designed to grab the viewer\'s attention, convey the product\'s features and benefits, and ultimately drive sales.', '[\"Facebook\"]', 'scheduled', 1, 'Create a high-quality commercial product advertisement image of a premium matte black 1-liter water bottle placed in the center of the frame. The bottle should have a sleek, modern cylindrical design with a smooth matte black finish and a metallic silver screw cap lid. The bottle must look premium, durable, and stylish, suitable for everyday use like gym workouts, office desks, travel, hiking, and outdoor activities.\r\n\r\nThe bottle surface should have realistic water droplets and condensation, giving a fresh and chilled look as if the bottle was taken out of a refrigerator. The lighting should be dramatic studio lighting, with soft reflections and subtle highlights on the matte surface, making the bottle look luxurious and eye-catching.\r\n\r\nThe background should be a cinematic blend of multiple lifestyle environments, slightly blurred with depth of field:\r\n\r\none side showing a modern gym environment with dumbbells and workout equipment\r\n\r\nanother side showing a clean office desk with a laptop and notebook\r\n\r\nanother part showing a nature outdoor setting with mountains or greenery\r\n\r\nThe bottle should be placed on a dark reflective surface with splashes of water and ice cubes around it, giving a refreshing hydration theme.\r\n\r\nAdd dynamic water splash effects around the bottle to create motion and energy, as if water has just been poured.\r\n\r\nInclude professional advertisement typography in the design:\r\n\r\nTop headline:\r\n“STAY HYDRATED IN STYLE”\r\n\r\nProduct title:\r\n“Premium Black Water Bottle”\r\n\r\nFeature bullet points on the side:\r\n\r\n1 Liter Capacity\r\n\r\nSleek Matte Finish\r\n\r\nDurable and Lightweight\r\n\r\nPerfect for Gym, Office & Travel\r\n\r\nAdd a bright promotional price tag badge in red or yellow with bold text:\r\n\r\n“ONLY ₹499”\r\n\r\nAdd a small promotional line at the bottom:\r\n“Limited Stock – Order Now!”\r\n\r\nThe image should be ultra realistic, highly detailed, cinematic lighting, sharp focus, professional product photography style, 8K resolution, advertisement design, modern e-commerce marketing style, dramatic shadows, high contrast, realistic textures, commercial branding layout, vibrant but elegant color grading, photorealistic rendering, depth of field, premium product showcase.\r\n\r\nAspect ratio: 1:1 or 4:5 for social media advertisement.\r\n\r\nStyle references:\r\nproduct photography, commercial advertisement, cinematic lighting, hyper realistic rendering, modern marketing poster design, ultra HD quality, studio photography, realistic reflections, professional brand ad style.', '2026-03-09 11:10:00', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Create a high-quality commercial product advertisement image of a premium matte black 1-liter water bottle placed in the center of the frame. The bottle should have a sleek, modern cylindrical design with a smooth matte black finish and a metallic silver screw cap lid. The bottle must look premium, durable, and stylish, suitable for everyday use like gym workouts, office desks, travel, hiking, and outdoor activities.\r\n\r\nThe bottle surface should have realist