(912, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and narco-terrorist who was the founder and leader of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda Gaviria, after his father abandoned them. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working as a small-time smuggler, selling contraband cigarettes and whiskey.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder and other Colombian traffickers. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him build a vast network of loyal associates and expand the cartel\'s operations.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, with estimated annual revenues of $20 billion to $30 billion. Escobar\'s organization was responsible for smuggling massive quantities of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other countries.\n\nThe Medellín Cartel was known for its brutality and violence. Escobar and his associates used intimidation, murder, and terrorism to maintain control and eliminate rivals. The cartel was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, politicians, and civilians.\n\n**Personal Life and Luxuries**\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar was known for his charismatic personality and lavish lifestyle. He lived in a sprawling mansion, Hacienda Napoles, which was equipped with a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars. Escobar was also a fan of soccer and owned a soccer team, Atlético Nacional.\n\nEscobar was married to María Victoria Henao, and they had two children, Juan Pablo and Manuela. He was known for his devotion to his family and was often seen in public with his wife and children.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The Medellín Cartel was weakened by internal conflicts and the loss of key associates, including Escobar\'s partner, Gustavo Gaviria.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of the Medellín Cartel\'s reign of terror, but it did not eradicate the cocaine trade or the violence associated with it.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and destruction to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the failures of the war on drugs and the corrupting influence of power and wealth.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, serving as a reminder of the dangers of the drug trade and the importance of addressing the root causes of crime and violence.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-10 10:45:00', '2026-03-10 10:45:05', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-10 10:45:05', '2026-03-10 10:45:05'),
(913, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious organized crime groups in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned the family. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he quickly turned to crime to support himself and his family.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working for the Medellín cartel, which was led by Carlos Lehder and other prominent Colombian traffickers. He quickly rose through the ranks, becoming a key player in the cartel\'s cocaine smuggling operations. In 1979, Escobar and his partners assassinated Lehder, taking control of the cartel and establishing Escobar as the new leader.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel and Cocaine Empire**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and profitable organized crime groups in the world. The cartel\'s primary business was cocaine smuggling, and Escobar\'s organization dominated the global market. At the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be earning over $420 million per week, making him one of the richest men in the world.\n\nThe Medellín cartel\'s operations were characterized by extreme violence, intimidation, and corruption. Escobar and his associates used murder, torture, and bribery to maintain control over the cartel\'s territories and eliminate rivals. The cartel\'s influence extended to the highest levels of Colombian politics and law enforcement, with many officials and politicians on the cartel\'s payroll.\n\n**The War on Drugs and the Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the 1980s, the United States government launched a series of initiatives aimed at disrupting the Medellín cartel\'s operations and bringing Escobar to justice. The U.S. government worked closely with Colombian authorities to dismantle the cartel\'s infrastructure and capture or kill its leaders.\n\nThe hunt for Escobar became a major priority for the U.S. and Colombian governments. In 1991, the U.S. government offered a $10 million reward for information leading to Escobar\'s capture. The Colombian government, meanwhile, launched a series of military operations aimed at capturing or killing Escobar and his associates.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Colombian police finally tracked down Escobar to a rooftop in Medellín, where he was hiding with his bodyguard. After a brief shootout, Escobar was killed, reportedly by a single bullet wound to the head.\n\nEscobar\'s death marked the end of an era for the Medellín cartel, and his legacy continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a complex and multifaceted figure, with many Colombians viewing him as a folk hero or a symbol of resistance against the government. However, his legacy is also marked by the countless lives lost and destroyed by his organization\'s violence and addiction.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate in Medellín.\n* He was a skilled soccer player and even sponsored a local team, the Atlético Nacional.\n* Escobar was a devout Catholic and often sought to justify his actions as a way of providing for his family and community.\n* He was responsible for the deaths of an estimated 4,000 people, including politicians, police officers, and rival gang members.\n* Escobar\'s brother, Roberto, was also involved in the cartel and was arrested in 1990. He later cooperated with authorities and provided valuable information about the cartel\'s operations.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-10 10:50:00', '2026-03-10 10:50:06', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-10 10:50:06', '2026-03-10 10:50:06'),
(914, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and powerful criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Dari Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and motivate his pursuit of wealth and power.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a teenager, selling stolen cars and participating in other small-time scams. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him quickly rise through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder.\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the Medellín cartel, and his organization soon dominated the global cocaine trade. He was known for his innovative and brutal tactics, including the use of violence, intimidation, and bribery to eliminate competitors and maintain control.\n\n**Empire and Extravagance**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar\'s empire was estimated to be worth over $30 billion. He lived a life of extravagance, owning numerous properties, including his famous Hacienda Napoles estate, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic animals.\n\nEscobar was also known for his generosity and philanthropy, particularly in his hometown of Medellín. He built roads, schools, and hospitals, and provided financial support to local communities. This earned him a degree of popularity and loyalty among some Colombians, who saw him as a folk hero.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nHowever, Escobar\'s reign was also marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the murders of thousands of people, including politicians, judges, police officers, and rival gang members. His organization was notorious for its use of car bombs, assassinations, and other forms of terrorism.\n\nIn 1989, Escobar\'s men bombed an Avianca airliner, killing 110 people, in an attempt to intimidate the Colombian government. He also ordered the assassination of presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán, who was a vocal opponent of the cartel.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar\'s organization was weakened by internal power struggles and external pressure, and he was eventually forced to go into hiding.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the global cocaine trade, and his legacy continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His life and death have become a cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime and the corrupting influence of power.\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a complex and fascinating figure, symbolizing both the dark underbelly of the cocaine trade and the tragic consequences of poverty, violence, and social inequality in Colombia.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-10 10:53:00', '2026-03-10 10:53:07', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-10 10:53:07', '2026-03-10 10:53:07'),
(915, 'pop', 'It seems like you\'re referring to the concept of \"pop\" in a general sense, but without more context, it\'s difficult to provide a specific answer. However, I can give you an overview of what \"pop\" might refer to in different contexts:\r\n\r\n1. **Music**: Pop music, short for popular music, is a genre of music that is widely popular and appeals to a large audience. It often includes elements from other styles like rock, R&B, hip-hop, and electronic music.\r\n\r\n2. **Culture**: Pop culture, or popular culture, refers to the cultural elements that are prevalent in a society at a given time. This can include music, movies, television shows, memes, and trends.\r\n\r\n3. **Physics/Chemistry**: In a scientific context, \"pop\" might refer to the sudden release of pressure or energy, such as when a balloon pops or when a chemical reaction causes a container to burst.\r\n\r\n4. **Food/Drink**: Pop can also refer to a type of carbonated beverage, often called soda pop.\r\n\r\n5. **Art**: Pop art is a style of art that emerged in the 1950s and 60s, characterized by its use of popular culture imagery and mass-produced materials.\r\n\r\nIf you could provide more details or specify which context you\'re interested in, I\'d be happy to give a more focused response.', '[\"Facebook\"]', 'published', 1, 'body', NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'body', 'https://pollinations.ai/p/body', NULL, 'approved', NULL, '2026-03-10 10:59:34', '2026-03-10 10:59:34'),
(916, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a possible Facebook post for a soccer sports business/creator:\n\n**Get Ready for the Beautiful Game!**\n\nHere are a few things to keep in mind as we head into the new season:\n* The pitch is where heroes are made\n* Every goal is a dream come true\n* Teamwork makes the dream work\n* The beautiful game is a way of life\n* Soccer is not just a sport, it\'s a passion\n\nJoin us as we celebrate the love of soccer! #SoccerLove #FootballFever #SportsNews #TrendingNow #NewSeasonAlert #SoccerFansUnite #BeautifulGame #FootballIsLife #SportsEnthusiast #SoccerLife', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-10 11:18:00', '2026-03-10 11:18:07', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Ultra_realistic_portrait_of_a_young_man%2C_soft_natural_lighting%2C_DSLR_photography_style%2C_shallow_depth_of_field%2C_85mm_lens%2C_highly_detailed_skin_texture?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-03-10 11:18:07', '2026-03-10 11:18:07'),
(917, 'mercedes benz', 'Mercedes-Benz is a renowned German multinational automotive corporation that has been a leading manufacturer of luxury vehicles, buses, coaches, and trucks since 1926. The company was founded by Karl Benz and Gottlieb Daimler, who are credited with inventing the first gasoline-powered automobile.\r\n\r\nHere are some key facts about Mercedes-Benz:\r\n\r\n**History:**\r\n- Founded in 1926 by the merger of Karl Benz\'s company, Benz & Cie., and Gottlieb Daimler\'s company, Daimler-Motoren-Gesellschaft (DMG)\r\n- Introduced the first gasoline-powered automobile, the Benz Patent-Motorwagen, in 1886\r\n- Produced the first modern car, the Mercedes 35 hp, in 1901\r\n\r\n**Models:**\r\n- Mercedes-Benz offers a wide range of vehicles, including:\r\n  - Sedans: C-Class, E-Class, S-Class\r\n  - SUVs: GLA, GLC, GLE, GLS\r\n  - Coupes: C-Class Coupe, E-Class Coupe, S-Class Coupe\r\n  - Roadsters: SLC, AMG GT\r\n  - Electric and Hybrid Vehicles: EQC, EQA, EQB\r\n\r\n**Innovations:**\r\n- Introduced the first anti-lock braking system (ABS) in 1978\r\n- Developed the first airbag system in 1980\r\n- Introduced the first electronic stability program (ESP) in 1995\r\n- Launched the first hybrid vehicle, the Mercedes-Benz S400 Hybrid, in 2009\r\n\r\n**Motorsports:**\r\n- Mercedes-Benz has a long history of participating in motorsports, including:\r\n  - Formula 1: Mercedes-AMG Petronas Motorsport\r\n  - DTM (Deutsche Tourenwagen Masters)\r\n  - GT Racing: Mercedes-AMG GT3\r\n\r\n**Awards and Recognition:**\r\n- Mercedes-Benz has received numerous awards and recognition for its vehicles, including:\r\n  - \"Best Car\" awards from various publications\r\n  - \"World Car of the Year\" awards\r\n  - \"European Car of the Year\" awards\r\n\r\n**Sustainability:**\r\n- Mercedes-Benz is committed to reducing its environmental impact and has set goals to:\r\n  - Reduce CO2 emissions from its vehicles and production processes\r\n  - Increase the use of renewable energy sources\r\n  - Develop more efficient and sustainable vehicles, including electric and hybrid models\r\n\r\nOverall, Mercedes-Benz is a legendary brand that has been at the forefront of innovation, design, and performance in the automotive industry for over a century.', '[\"Facebook\"]', 'published', 1, 'mercedes benz', NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'mercedes benz', 'https://res.cloudinary.com/diapmjeoc/image/upload/v1773121891/user_2_test21/tsjk2melnoedx52iabda.jpg', NULL, 'approved', NULL, '2026-03-10 11:21:31', '2026-03-10 11:21:31'),
(918, 'mercedes-benz amg', 'Mercedes-Benz AMG, also known as AMG, is a high-performance division of the German automobile manufacturer Mercedes-Benz. AMG was founded in 1967 by Hans Werner Aufrecht and Erhard Melcher, and the company\'s name is derived from the initials of the founders\' surnames and the town of Großaspach, where the company was founded.\r\n\r\nHere are some key details about Mercedes-Benz AMG:\r\n\r\n**History**: AMG was founded as a racing engine manufacturer, and its first product was a racing engine for the Mercedes-Benz 300SEL. In the 1970s and 1980s, AMG began to develop and produce high-performance versions of Mercedes-Benz production cars. In 1999, Mercedes-Benz acquired a majority stake in AMG, and in 2005, AMG became a wholly owned subsidiary of Mercedes-Benz.\r\n\r\n**Models**: Mercedes-Benz AMG offers a range of high-performance models, including:\r\n\r\n* AMG GT: a sports car with a V8 engine\r\n* C63 AMG: a high-performance version of the Mercedes-Benz C-Class\r\n* E63 AMG: a high-performance version of the Mercedes-Benz E-Class\r\n* S63 AMG: a high-performance version of the Mercedes-Benz S-Class\r\n* GLC63 AMG: a high-performance version of the Mercedes-Benz GLC\r\n* G63 AMG: a high-performance version of the Mercedes-Benz G-Class\r\n\r\n**Technology**: Mercedes-Benz AMG is known for its advanced technology, including:\r\n\r\n* V8 engines: AMG is famous for its V8 engines, which are used in many of its models\r\n* 4MATIC all-wheel drive: AMG\'s 4MATIC system provides improved traction and stability\r\n* AMG SPEEDSHIFT transmission: a high-performance transmission that provides quick and smooth shifting\r\n* AMG RIDE CONTROL suspension: a suspension system that provides improved handling and stability\r\n\r\n**Motorsports**: Mercedes-Benz AMG has a long history of involvement in motorsports, including:\r\n\r\n* Formula 1: AMG has been involved in Formula 1 as an engine supplier since 2010\r\n* DTM: AMG has been competing in the Deutsche Tourenwagen Masters (DTM) series since 1988\r\n* GT racing: AMG has been competing in GT racing series, including the FIA GT World Cup and the 24 Hours of Spa\r\n\r\n**Design**: Mercedes-Benz AMG is known for its distinctive design language, which includes:\r\n\r\n* AMG-specific exterior styling: AMG models have unique exterior styling, including distinctive bumpers, side skirts, and wheels\r\n* AMG-specific interior styling: AMG models have unique interior styling, including sport seats, a flat-bottomed steering wheel, and AMG-specific trim elements\r\n* AMG badges: AMG models feature distinctive AMG badges, which are used to identify the vehicle as an AMG model.\r\n\r\nOverall, Mercedes-Benz AMG is a renowned high-performance division that offers a range of exciting models with advanced technology, distinctive design, and a rich history of involvement in motorsports.', '[\"Facebook\"]', 'scheduled', 1, 'mercedes-benz amg', '2026-03-10 11:42:00', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'mercedes-benz amg', 'https://res.cloudinary.com/diapmjeoc/image/upload/v1773122974/user_2_test21/tlsmuaq8mdambglze73y.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, '2026-03-10 11:39:35', '2026-03-10 11:39:35'),
(919, 'human', 'The human species, also known as Homo sapiens, is a complex and dynamic entity. Here\'s an overview of what it means to be human:\r\n\r\n**Physical Characteristics:**\r\n\r\n* Humans are bipedal, meaning they walk on two legs\r\n* They have a upright posture, with a torso, arms, and legs\r\n* Their brain is large and developed, with a cerebral cortex that enables advanced thought and problem-solving\r\n* They have a wide range of physical characteristics, including skin color, hair texture, and body shape\r\n\r\n**Emotional and Social Aspects:**\r\n\r\n* Humans are social creatures, with a strong desire for connection and community\r\n* They experience a wide range of emotions, including joy, sadness, anger, and love\r\n* They have a capacity for empathy, compassion, and cooperation\r\n* They form complex relationships with others, including family, friends, and romantic partners\r\n\r\n**Cognitive Abilities:**\r\n\r\n* Humans have advanced cognitive abilities, including language, problem-solving, and abstract thinking\r\n* They have a capacity for learning, memory, and innovation\r\n* They use tools, technology, and other resources to adapt to their environment and achieve their goals\r\n* They have a sense of self-awareness, with the ability to reflect on their own thoughts, feelings, and experiences\r\n\r\n**Culture and Society:**\r\n\r\n* Humans live in complex societies, with social norms, customs, and institutions\r\n* They have a rich cultural heritage, with art, music, literature, and other forms of creative expression\r\n* They have a capacity for cooperation, collaboration, and mutual support\r\n* They have a desire for meaning, purpose, and fulfillment, which they often seek through work, relationships, and personal pursuits\r\n\r\n**Challenges and Vulnerabilities:**\r\n\r\n* Humans are vulnerable to physical and emotional harm, including injury, illness, and trauma\r\n* They are susceptible to cognitive biases, errors, and limitations, which can impact their decision-making and behavior\r\n* They face numerous challenges, including poverty, inequality, and environmental degradation\r\n* They have a finite lifespan, with the inevitability of death and the unknown beyond\r\n\r\nOverall, being human is a complex, multifaceted experience that encompasses physical, emotional, cognitive, and social aspects. It is marked by both incredible achievements and profound challenges, and is shaped by a wide range of factors, including culture, environment, and individual experience.', '[\"Facebook\"]', 'published', 1, 'human', NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'human', 'https://pollinations.ai/p/human', NULL, 'approved', NULL, '2026-03-10 12:25:45', '2026-03-10 12:25:45'),
(920, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Party wear for men can vary depending on the occasion, location, and personal style. Here are some popular options:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. Suits: A classic two-piece or three-piece suit in black, navy, or gray is always a safe choice.\n2. Tuxedos: A black tie event calls for a tuxedo, complete with a bow tie and cummerbund.\n3. Dress Shirts: A crisp, white dress shirt with a wing-tip collar is a must-have for formal events.\n4. Dress Pants: Formal trousers in matching color with the suit or tuxedo.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. Blazer and Jeans: A navy or gray blazer paired with dark wash jeans and a dress shirt is a stylish option.\n2. Dress Shirts with Chinos: A dress shirt with chinos or khaki pants is a versatile and comfortable choice.\n3. Polo Shirts: A polo shirt in a bold color or pattern can add a touch of personality to a semi-formal outfit.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. Graphic T-Shirts: A fun, graphic tee paired with jeans or shorts is perfect for a casual party.\n2. Henley Shirts: A Henley shirt in a bold color or pattern can add a laid-back touch to a casual outfit.\n3. Chinos or Jeans: Dark wash chinos or jeans are a staple for casual parties.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. Watches: A leather strap or metal watch can add a touch of sophistication to any outfit.\n2. Cufflinks: Cufflinks can add a personal touch to a dress shirt.\n3. Shoes: Dress shoes, such as oxfords or loafers, can complete a formal or semi-formal outfit.\n4. Belts: A leather belt can add a finishing touch to a pair of pants or chinos.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. Consider the dress code: Make sure to check the dress code for the party to ensure you\'re dressed accordingly.\n2. Dress for the occasion: Choose an outfit that fits the theme and style of the party.\n3. Accessorize wisely: Too many accessories can be overwhelming, so choose a few statement pieces to complete your outfit.\n4. Be confident: Own your outfit and have fun!\n\nSome popular party wear styles for men include:\n\n1. Minimalist Chic: A simple, monochromatic outfit with clean lines and minimal accessories.\n2. Dapper Gentleman: A classic, sophisticated look with a suit, tie, and pocket watch.\n3. Street Style: A casual, edgy look with bold graphics, sneakers, and a backpack.\n4. Vintage Inspired: A retro-inspired look with suspenders, a bow tie, and a fedora.\n\nRemember, the key to pulling off a great party outfit is to be confident, comfortable, and true to your personal style.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-10 12:40:00', '2026-03-10 12:40:59', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/Party_Wear_for_Mens', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-03-10 12:40:59', '2026-03-10 12:40:59'),
(921, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is designed to be worn for formal occasions, such as business meetings, weddings, and other special events. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Types of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress Shirt:** A classic style of formal shirt, characterized by a pointed collar, French cuffs, and a fitted silhouette.\n2. **Button-Down Shirt:** A type of formal shirt with a button-down collar, which is less formal than a dress shirt but still suitable for business casual events.\n3. **Wingtip Shirt:** A formal shirt with a wingtip collar, which is similar to a dress shirt but with a more relaxed fit.\n\n**Features of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Collar Style:** Formal shirts often have a pointed collar, which is considered more formal than a spread collar.\n2. **Cuff Style:** French cuffs are a common feature of formal shirts, as they add a touch of elegance to the overall design.\n3. **Fabric:** Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit:** Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim silhouette and a fitted waist.\n5. **Buttoning:** Formal shirts often have a button-front closure, with a single button or a double button at the top.\n\n**Styles of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Classic White:** A timeless choice, classic white formal shirts are versatile and can be paired with a variety of suits and ties.\n2. **Light Blue:** A light blue formal shirt is a popular alternative to white, and can add a touch of personality to a outfit.\n3. **Pastel Colors:** Soft pastel colors such as pink, yellow, and lavender can add a touch of elegance to a formal outfit.\n4. **Striped and Checked:** Formal shirts with subtle stripes or checks can add visual interest to a outfit.\n\n**Brands and Prices:**\n\n1. **Luxury Brands:** High-end brands such as Tom Ford, Burberry, and Ermenegildo Zegna offer formal shirts with a price range of $200-$500.\n2. **Mid-Range Brands:** Brands such as Brooks Brothers, Ralph Lauren, and Calvin Klein offer formal shirts with a price range of $50-$200.\n3. **Affordable Brands:** Affordable brands such as H&M, Uniqlo, and Gap offer formal shirts with a price range of $10-$50.\n\n**Tips for Wearing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Pair with a Suit:** A formal shirt is best paired with a suit and tie for a complete formal outfit.\n2. **Choose the Right Color:** Choose a formal shirt that complements the color of your suit and tie.\n3. **Pay Attention to Fit:** Make sure the formal shirt fits well, with a slim silhouette and a fitted waist.\n4. **Accessories:** Add a touch of elegance to your outfit with a simple watch, a quality belt, and a pair of dress shoes.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-10 12:56:00', '2026-03-10 12:56:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/Formal_shirt_for_mens', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-03-10 12:56:16', '2026-03-10 12:56:16'),
