(1001, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a potential Facebook post for a dragon-themed business/creator:\n\n\"As we soar into the new week, let\'s take a moment to reflect on what drives us. Here are a few things that inspire me as a dragon:\n\n* Embracing my unique strengths and abilities\n* Continuously learning and growing to stay ahead of the curve\n* Surrounding myself with a supportive community that encourages me to spread my wings\n* Taking calculated risks to achieve my goals and pursue my passions\n* Staying true to myself and my values, even in the face of adversity\n\nI hope these points resonate with you, and that you\'re having a fantastic week so far! #DragonInspiration #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #BusinessTips #PersonalGrowth #ProfessionalDevelopment #DragonSquad #FacebookBusiness #EntrepreneurLife\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, as well as some specific to the dragon theme and business/creator niche. The tone is professional and relatable, with a touch of personality and inspiration.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 10:35:00', '2026-03-12 10:35:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-03-12 10:35:14', '2026-03-12 10:35:14'),
(1002, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely considered one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and crime, and he was involved in various illicit activities from a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working for various crime bosses in Medellín, including Carlos Lehder, who would later become a key partner in the Medellín Cartel. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness quickly earned him a reputation as a rising star in the Colombian underworld.\n\nIn 1976, Escobar and his partners founded the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world. The cartel\'s primary business was smuggling cocaine into the United States, and Escobar\'s organization quickly dominated the market.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel expanded its operations to include extortion, kidnapping, and murder. The cartel\'s influence extended to the highest levels of Colombian politics and law enforcement, and Escobar became a wealthy and feared figure in Colombian society.\n\nThe Medellín Cartel\'s success was due in part to Escobar\'s innovative tactics, including the use of small planes to transport cocaine and the creation of a network of hidden landing strips and laboratories. The cartel\'s profits were enormous, and Escobar became one of the richest men in Colombia.\n\n**Violence and Notoriety**\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was marked by violence and bloodshed. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, and rival cartel members. The Medellín Cartel\'s tactics included bombings, assassinations, and massacres, and Escobar became known as \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) or \"El Diablo\" (The Devil).\n\nIn 1989, Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people. The bombing was intended to kill a Colombian presidential candidate, but it missed its target.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a luxurious private prison, which he had built himself. However, he escaped in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\nThe Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a massive manhunt for Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and cunning crime boss who was responsible for thousands of deaths and untold suffering. However, he was also a charismatic figure who was admired by many in Colombia for his generosity and his willingness to challenge the establishment.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite his notoriety, Escobar remains a fascinating and complex figure, and his story continues to captivate audiences around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 10:45:00', '2026-03-12 10:45:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-12 10:45:16', '2026-03-12 10:45:16'),
(1003, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. He began his career in crime at a young age, selling stolen cars and cigarettes on the black market. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was then a relatively new and lucrative market.\n\nEscobar quickly rose to prominence in the Medellín cartel, which he helped to found and lead. He became known for his cunning, ruthlessness, and business acumen, which allowed him to outmaneuver his competitors and establish the Medellín cartel as the dominant force in the Colombian cocaine trade.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and wealthy organized crime syndicates in the world. The cartel\'s operations were characterized by violence, intimidation, and corruption, and it was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, and rival gang members.\n\nEscobar\'s success was fueled by his ability to bribe and coerce officials, as well as his use of violence and intimidation to maintain control over his empire. He was known to be ruthless in his dealings, and his reputation for brutality was legendary.\n\n**The \"King of Cocaine\"**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world. He was known as the \"King of Cocaine\" and was revered by many in Colombia as a folk hero, who had risen from poverty to become one of the most powerful men in the country.\n\nHowever, Escobar\'s success was short-lived. In the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the support of the United States, launched a series of crackdowns on the Medellín cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and his empire began to crumble.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\nEscobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was a brutal and ruthless crime lord, he was also a charismatic figure who was able to inspire loyalty and devotion in many of his followers. His rise to power and his subsequent fall are a testament to the enduring power of the cocaine trade and the corrupting influence of wealth and power.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which tells the story of his rise and fall.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate in Medellín.\n* He was a prolific philanthropist, who donated millions of dollars to charitable causes and built schools, hospitals, and other infrastructure projects in Colombia.\n* Escobar was a skilled politician, who was able to manipulate public opinion and build a cult of personality around himself.\n* He was known for his intelligence and strategic thinking, which allowed him to outmaneuver his competitors and stay one step ahead of the law.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar was a complex and fascinating figure, who left an indelible mark on the world of organized crime and the history of Colombia.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 10:50:00', '2026-03-12 10:50:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-12 10:50:21', '2026-03-12 10:50:21'),
(1004, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. His father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. Escobar grew up in a troubled neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and violence at a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began his career in organized crime, working as a car thief and a smuggler. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, which was led by Carlos Lehder. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness earned him the respect and loyalty of his associates.\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the Medellín Cartel, which dominated the global cocaine trade. He expanded the cartel\'s operations, establishing a vast network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. Escobar\'s organization was responsible for smuggling an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine into the United States.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his brutal tactics, using violence and intimidation to maintain control over his organization and eliminate his rivals. He was responsible for the murders of hundreds of people, including police officers, judges, and politicians. Escobar\'s henchmen, known as \"sicarios,\" carried out many of these killings.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The Colombian police and military, led by Colonel Hugo Martínez, conducted a massive manhunt, known as \"Operation Search Block,\" to track down Escobar.\n\n**Death**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police on the rooftop of a safe house in Medellín. The police had tracked Escobar to the location using a combination of intelligence and technology. Escobar died from a single bullet wound to the head, fired by a police officer.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and violent individual who was responsible for the deaths of many innocent people. However, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and lucrative empire.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and career have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" These portrayals have helped to cement Escobar\'s status as a larger-than-life figure, both fascinating and terrifying.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate, known as Hacienda Napoles.\n* He was estimated to have earned over $30 billion during his lifetime, making him one of the richest people in the world.\n* Escobar was a skilled politician and was elected to the Colombian Congress in 1982.\n* He was known for his Robin Hood-like persona, using his wealth and influence to build roads, schools, and hospitals in poor neighborhoods.\n* Escobar\'s death was met with widespread celebration in Colombia, but his legacy continues to be felt in the country, with many regarding him as a symbol of the country\'s troubled past.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 10:53:00', '2026-03-12 10:53:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-12 10:53:15', '2026-03-12 10:53:15'),
(1005, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a possible Facebook post for a dragon business/creator:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of connecting with my audience. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Be fierce, but also kind - it\'s possible to be both powerful and compassionate at the same time.\n* Don\'t be afraid to show your true colors - authenticity is key to building trust with your audience.\n* Hoard your treasure, but also share it with others - generosity and kindness can go a long way in building a loyal following.\n* Take time to breathe fire and relax - self-care is essential for maintaining a healthy and happy lifestyle.\n\n#DragonLife #FireBreathingTips #ScaleUpYourBusiness #TrendingNow #DragonSquad #MythicalCreatures #FantasyFiction #BusinessTips #MotivationMonday #FacebookFamous #DragonFire\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of trending and niche-specific hashtags to reach a wider audience. The brand voice is professional, yet relatable and engaging.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 11:18:00', '2026-03-12 11:18:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-03-12 11:18:14', '2026-03-12 11:18:14'),
(1006, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. Suits: A well-tailored suit in black, navy, or gray is a classic choice for formal parties.\n2. Tuxedos: A tuxedo is a must-have for black-tie events, paired with a bow tie and cummerbund.\n3. Dress Shirts: A crisp, white dress shirt with a wingtip collar is a staple for formal parties.\n4. Dress Pants: Formal dress pants in black, navy, or gray can be paired with a dress shirt and blazer.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. Blazer and Jeans: A navy or gray blazer paired with dark wash jeans and a dress shirt is a stylish option.\n2. Dress Shoes: Loafers, brogues, or dress boots can add a touch of sophistication to a semi-formal outfit.\n3. Patterned Shirts: A patterned dress shirt in a subtle design can add visual interest to a semi-formal outfit.\n4. Chinos: Light or dark chinos can be paired with a dress shirt and blazer for a semi-formal look.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. Graphic T-Shirts: A graphic t-shirt in a bold design can be paired with jeans or casual pants.\n2. Polos: A polo shirt in a bright color can add a pop of color to a casual outfit.\n3. Jeans: Dark wash jeans are a versatile choice for casual parties.\n4. Sneakers: Sneakers in bold colors or unique designs can add a fun touch to a casual outfit.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. Watches: A leather strap watch or a metallic watch can add a touch of sophistication to a party outfit.\n2. Cufflinks: Cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to a formal or semi-formal outfit.\n3. Pocket Squares: A pocket square in a bold color or pattern can add a pop of color to a suit or blazer.\n4. Hats: A fedora or a Panama hat can add a stylish touch to a party outfit.\n\n**Grooming Tips:**\n\n1. Hair: Style your hair with a pomade or a styling cream to add a sleek touch.\n2. Beard: Trim your beard to maintain a neat and tidy look.\n3. Fragrance: Wear a subtle fragrance that complements your outfit.\n4. Nails: Make sure your nails are clean and trimmed to complete your party look.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to be confident and have fun with your outfit!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 12:40:00', '2026-03-12 12:41:07', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/Party_Wear_for_Mens', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-03-12 12:41:07', '2026-03-12 12:41:07'),
(1007, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of dress shirt designed to be worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key features and styles to consider:\n\n**Types of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress Shirt:** A classic, collared shirt with a button-front closure, typically made from cotton, linen, or a blend of fabrics.\n2. **Dress Shirt with French Cuffs:** A dress shirt with cuffs that are folded back and fastened with cufflinks.\n3. **Wingtip Collar Shirt:** A dress shirt with a wing-shaped collar, often worn with a bow tie.\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar Style:** Pointed, spread, or wingtip collars are common styles.\n2. **Cuff Style:** Barrel cuffs, French cuffs, or button cuffs are available.\n3. **Placket Style:** A plain or pleated placket (the front panel of the shirt) can add texture and visual interest.\n4. **Button Type:** Mother-of-pearl, plastic, or metal buttons are commonly used.\n5. **Fabric:** Cotton, linen, or blends are popular choices for formal shirts.\n\n**Popular Fabrics:**\n\n1. **Cotton:** A classic choice, cotton is breathable, durable, and easy to care for.\n2. **Linen:** A natural, textured fabric that\'s perfect for warm weather and formal events.\n3. **Oxford Cloth:** A type of cotton fabric with a subtle texture and a soft, smooth finish.\n\n**Colors and Patterns:**\n\n1. **White:** A classic choice, white formal shirts are versatile and timeless.\n2. **Light Blue:** A popular alternative to white, light blue shirts are perfect for business and formal events.\n3. **Stripes:** Subtle stripes can add visual interest to a formal shirt.\n4. **Checks:** Small, subtle checks can add texture and depth to a formal shirt.\n\n**Tips for Choosing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the occasion:** Choose a shirt that\'s suitable for the event or occasion.\n2. **Think about your skin tone:** Cool skin tones look best with blue-based colors, while warm skin tones look best with yellow-based colors.\n3. **Pay attention to fit:** A well-fitted shirt is essential for a polished, put-together look.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink:** Known for their high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet:** A French brand offering luxurious, bespoke formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers:** An American brand offering classic, stylish formal shirts.\n\nRemember, a formal shirt is a versatile and essential item in a man\'s wardrobe. With so many styles, fabrics, and colors to choose from, you\'re sure to find the perfect shirt to suit your needs and preferences.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 12:56:00', '2026-03-12 12:57:07', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/Formal_shirt_for_mens', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-03-12 12:57:07', '2026-03-12 12:57:07'),
(1008, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', 'Here\'s a possible Facebook post for a dragon-themed business/creator:\n\n**Embracing Your Inner Fire**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned that success and growth come from within. Here are a few key takeaways to help you unleash your inner strength:\n\n* Believe in yourself and your abilities\n* Set ambitious goals and work towards achieving them\n* Surround yourself with positive influences and supportive people\n* Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things\n* Keep learning and adapting to stay ahead of the curve\n\nBy following these principles, you can tap into your inner fire and achieve greatness. Remember to stay focused, motivated, and true to yourself.\n\n#DragonInspiration #MotivationMonday #InnerStrength #PersonalGrowth #SuccessTips #TrendingNow #BusinessMotivation #InspirationalQuotes #FacebookBusiness #DragonPower\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, including #MotivationMonday, #TrendingNow, and #BusinessMotivation, to help increase the post\'s visibility and reach a wider audience.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-12 13:03:00', '2026-03-12 13:04:03', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/Women_Sandel', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-03-12 13:04:03', '2026-03-12 13:04:03'),
