(1118, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a relatable caption for a dragon-themed business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing our true nature and unleashing our inner fire. Here are a few things I\'ve learned on my journey:\n\n* Believe in yourself and your abilities, even when others doubt you\n* Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things - it\'s often the best way to learn and grow\n* Surround yourself with people who support and encourage you\n* Remember that it\'s okay to make mistakes - they\'re an opportunity to learn and become stronger\n\n#DragonSquad #FireBreathingMotivation #BelieveInYourself #TakeRisks #SupportSystem #LearnFromMistakes #InnerStrength #TrendingNow #DragonPower #MotivationMonday #Inspiration\"\n\nThis caption is professional, relatable, and includes a mix of trending and niche-specific hashtags to reach a wider audience on Facebook.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-16 10:35:00', '2026-03-16 10:35:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-03-16 10:35:15', '2026-03-16 10:35:15'),
(1119, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. His father was a farmer, and his mother was a teacher. Escobar grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in petty crime and street violence at a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working for various Colombian crime lords, including Carlos Lehder, who would later become a key associate. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthless tactics quickly earned him a reputation as a rising star in the Colombian underworld.\n\nIn 1976, Escobar co-founded the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world. The cartel\'s primary business was smuggling cocaine into the United States, where it was distributed by a network of dealers and distributors.\n\n**Empire and Extravagance**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar\'s empire was estimated to be worth over $30 billion. He owned numerous properties, including a luxurious mansion in Medellín, known as Hacienda Napoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic animals.\n\nEscobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a fleet of cars, planes, and yachts. He also invested in various legitimate businesses, such as real estate, construction, and agriculture.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nHowever, Escobar\'s success was built on violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including rival gang members, police officers, judges, and politicians. His cartel was also responsible for numerous bombings, kidnappings, and assassinations.\n\nIn 1989, Escobar\'s cartel was involved in the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán, who had vowed to crack down on the cartel\'s activities.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, he continued to run his empire from behind bars and eventually escaped in 1992.\n\nA massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down by Colombian police and U.S. DEA agents on December 1, 1993. He was shot and killed in a rooftop shootout in Medellín, just one day after his 44th birthday.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was a ruthless and brutal criminal, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast empire and evade capture for many years.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story has captivated audiences around the world, and he remains one of the most infamous and fascinating figures in modern history.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his generosity and philanthropy in his hometown of Medellín, where he built roads, schools, and hospitals.\n* He was a fan of soccer and owned a team, Atlético Nacional, which won several championships during his ownership.\n* Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for the production of over 80% of the world\'s cocaine in the 1980s.\n* He was known for his love of animals and had a private zoo at his Hacienda Napoles estate, which featured exotic animals such as lions, tigers, and elephants.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-16 10:45:00', '2026-03-16 10:45:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-16 10:45:16', '2026-03-16 10:45:16'),
(1120, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug cartels in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. His father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. Escobar grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and violence at a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power began in the 1970s, when he started working as a smuggler and a trafficker of contraband goods, including cigarettes and electronics. He quickly became involved in the cocaine trade, which was becoming increasingly lucrative in Colombia at the time. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him to build a network of loyal associates and to establish himself as a major player in the cocaine trade.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar co-founded the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world. The cartel\'s success was based on its ability to produce and distribute large quantities of high-quality cocaine, which was in high demand in the United States and other countries. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and violence, and it was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, and rival gang members.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Galán, who was a leading candidate in the Colombian presidential election. The killing was carried out by Escobar\'s associates, who used a remote-controlled bomb to blow up Galán\'s car.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s associates planted a bomb on an Avianca airliner, which exploded in mid-air, killing 110 people. The bombing was intended to kill a Colombian presidential candidate who was on board, but he was not on the flight.\n3. **The murder of Colombian police officers**: Escobar\'s organization was responsible for the deaths of hundreds of Colombian police officers, who were targeted and killed in revenge for their efforts to crack down on the cartel.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major effort to capture or kill Escobar. The pursuit of Escobar was led by a special task force, known as the Search Bloc, which was composed of Colombian police officers and soldiers.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death. Escobar\'s death marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror, and it paved the way for the rise of other drug cartels in Colombia.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. At the same time, he is also remembered as a charismatic and intelligent leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which tells the story of his rise and fall. Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a fascinating and intriguing figure, and his legacy continues to captivate people around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-16 10:50:00', '2026-03-16 10:50:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-16 10:50:14', '2026-03-16 10:50:14'),
(1121, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began his life of crime at a young age, initially as a car thief and smuggler. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was then a relatively new and lucrative business.\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was rapid, and by the early 1980s, he had become one of the leading figures in the Medellín Cartel, a powerful and ruthless organization that dominated the global cocaine trade. He was known for his cunning, intelligence, and brutality, as well as his ability to build a vast network of loyal associates and corrupt officials.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel and the Cocaine Trade**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became a multibillion-dollar empire, with operations in Colombia, the United States, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was based on its ability to produce and distribute high-quality cocaine, as well as its ruthless tactics, including murder, intimidation, and bribery.\n\nEscobar was known for his innovative marketing strategies, which included branding his cocaine with a distinctive logo and packaging it in small, easily concealable packets. He also invested heavily in infrastructure, including roads, bridges, and airports, to facilitate the transportation of his product.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and intimidation. He was responsible for numerous murders, including those of police officers, judges, politicians, and journalists. He also ordered the bombings of buildings, cars, and other targets, including a commercial airliner that was blown up in mid-air, killing all 107 people on board.\n\nEscobar\'s most notorious tactic was the use of \"plata o plomo\" (silver or lead), which meant that his enemies were given a choice between paying a bribe (plata) or facing death (plomo). This tactic was used to intimidate and corrupt officials, as well as to eliminate rivals and competitors.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major effort to capture or kill Escobar. The hunt was led by a special task force, known as the Search Bloc, which was trained and equipped by the United States.\n\nThe search for Escobar was intense and dramatic, with numerous shootouts, raids, and betrayals. Escobar was finally killed on December 1, 1993, in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy and Impact**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. On the one hand, he was a ruthless and brutal crime lord who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering. On the other hand, he was a charismatic and cunning leader who built a vast and lucrative empire, and who became a folk hero to many in Colombia and beyond.\n\nEscobar\'s impact on Colombia and the world has been profound. He helped to fuel a global cocaine epidemic, which has had devastating consequences for public health, crime, and social order. He also contributed to the destabilization of Colombia, which has struggled with violence, corruption, and poverty for decades.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a fascinating and enigmatic figure, who continues to captivate and intrigue people around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-16 10:53:00', '2026-03-16 10:53:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-16 10:53:17', '2026-03-16 10:53:17'),
(1122, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a symbol of power and strength, we dragons are often misunderstood. Here are a few things you might not know about us:\n\n* We\'re not just fire-breathers, we\'re also guardians of treasure and knowledge\n* We\'re fiercely loyal to our hoards and will stop at nothing to protect them\n* Despite our tough exterior, we have a soft spot for adventure and exploration\n* We\'re not just solitary creatures, we thrive in communities and value our dragon friendships\n\n#DragonsOfFacebook #DragonSquad #FireBreathersUnite #TreasureHunters #LoyalCompanions #AdventureSeekers #TrendingNow #DragonNation #MythicalCreatures #FantasyBeasts\"\n\nThis caption aims to showcase the professional brand voice while being relatable and engaging. The use of trending hashtags can help increase the post\'s visibility on Facebook.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-16 11:18:00', '2026-03-16 11:18:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-03-16 11:18:15', '2026-03-16 11:18:15'),
(1123, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Suits**: A classic choice for formal parties, suits come in a variety of colors and styles, including black tie, navy, and charcoal.\n2. **Tuxedos**: Perfect for black-tie events, tuxedos are a timeless and elegant choice.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A crisp, white dress shirt is a must-have for formal parties.\n4. **Bow Ties**: Add a touch of sophistication with a bow tie, available in various colors and patterns.\n5. **Cufflinks**: Complete your formal look with stylish cufflinks.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A blazer can add a touch of elegance to a dress shirt and trousers.\n2. **Dress Pants**: Dark-washed dress pants are a versatile choice for semi-formal parties.\n3. **Button-Down Shirts**: A button-down shirt in a bold color or pattern can add a pop of personality to your outfit.\n4. **Loafers**: Slip-on loafers or dress shoes can complete your semi-formal look.\n5. **Pocket Squares**: Add a splash of color with a pocket square.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans are a staple for casual parties.\n2. **T-Shirts**: A plain or graphic T-shirt can be dressed up or down.\n3. **Hoodies**: A hoodie can add a casual touch to your outfit.\n4. **Sneakers**: Sneakers are a comfortable and stylish choice for casual parties.\n5. **Trucker Hats**: Add a laid-back vibe with a trucker hat.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Watches**: A stylish watch can add a touch of sophistication to your outfit.\n2. **Belts**: A leather belt can complete your look and add a touch of elegance.\n3. **Sunglasses**: Sunglasses can add a cool, casual vibe to your outfit.\n4. **Jewelry**: A simple necklace or earrings can add a touch of personality to your outfit.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Dress according to the theme**: Make sure to dress according to the party theme, whether it\'s formal, semi-formal, or casual.\n2. **Pay attention to fit**: Ensure your clothes fit well and are comfortable to wear.\n3. **Accessories matter**: Add a touch of personality to your outfit with accessories like watches, belts, and jewelry.\n4. **Grooming is key**: Make sure to groom yourself well, including your hair, beard, and nails.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-16 12:40:00', '2026-03-16 12:41:09', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/Party_Wear_for_Mens', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-03-16 12:41:09', '2026-03-16 12:41:09');
