(1252, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a possible Facebook post for the Dragon business/creator:\n\n\"As a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about being fierce and successful. Here are some relatable points to keep in mind:\n\n* Believe in yourself and your abilities, just like I believe in my fire-breathing skills\n* Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things - it\'s how I discovered my love for hoarding treasure\n* Surround yourself with people who support and encourage you, just like my loyal dragon friends\n* Keep learning and growing, whether it\'s through reading books or attending dragon conferences\n* And most importantly, never give up on your dreams - even if they seem as impossible as flying to the moon\n\n#DragonMotivation #BusinessTips #SuccessMindset #FireBreathingInspiration #TrendingNow #DragonSquad #ProfessionalDevelopment #FacebookForBusiness\"\n\nThis post uses a professional tone while still being relatable and engaging, and includes a mix of trending and niche-specific hashtags to reach a wider audience.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 10:35:00', '2026-03-20 10:35:13', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-03-20 10:35:13', '2026-03-20 10:35:13'),
(1253, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely considered one of the most infamous and ruthless figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949, to a middle-class family. He grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and eventually turned to cocaine trafficking. Escobar\'s rise to power began in the 1970s, when he started working for a local cocaine trafficker. He quickly built a reputation as a ruthless and cunning operator, and by the early 1980s, he had established himself as one of the leading figures in the Colombian cocaine trade.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared organized crime groups in the world. The cartel\'s main business was cocaine trafficking, and it quickly expanded its operations to include other crimes, such as extortion, kidnapping, and murder. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and violence, and he was feared by his enemies and rivals.\n\n**Wealth and Excess**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was one of the richest men in the world, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion. He lived a life of extravagance and excess, with a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a vast estate in Medellín known as Hacienda Napoles. He also invested in real estate, buying properties in Colombia and abroad, and donated to charitable causes, earning him a degree of popularity among some Colombians.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nHowever, Escobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including rival gang members, police officers, judges, and politicians. He was also behind a series of bombings and assassinations, including the killing of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989. Escobar\'s organization was known for its use of terror tactics, including the killing of innocent civilians and the bombing of public places.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar\'s organization was weakened by internal conflicts and the loss of key associates, and he was eventually forced to go into hiding. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the Colombian cocaine trade, and the Medellín cartel was eventually dismantled.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord, responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. However, he is also seen by some as a folk hero, who brought wealth and jobs to Medellín and surrounding areas. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV series, including the Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which chronicles his rise and fall. Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a fascinating and intriguing figure, and his story continues to captivate audiences around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 10:45:00', '2026-03-20 10:45:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-20 10:45:18', '2026-03-20 10:45:18'),
(1254, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world during the 1980s and early 1990s. Here are some key facts about his life and career:\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda Gaviria, after his father abandoned the family. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working on the streets, selling stolen cars and other items.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in the drug trade began in the early 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, becoming a key player in the organization. In 1976, he was arrested for smuggling cocaine, but he was released from prison after bribing the judge.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the late 1970s and early 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the Medellín cartel, which dominated the global cocaine trade. The cartel\'s success was due in part to Escobar\'s innovative marketing and distribution strategies, which included using small planes to transport cocaine from Colombia to the United States.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his ruthless tactics, which included murder, intimidation, and bribery. He ordered the killings of hundreds of people, including police officers, judges, and politicians, who stood in his way. He also used violence to maintain control over his organization and to eliminate rivals.\n\n**Wealth and Luxury**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was one of the richest men in the world, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion. He lived a life of luxury, with a large estate in Medellín, known as Hacienda Napoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to the Colombian authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped from prison in 1992. The Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a massive manhunt for Escobar, who was eventually killed in a shootout with Colombian police on December 1, 1993, in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and the world. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a massive and powerful organization. His life and career have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of soccer and even built a soccer field at his estate, Hacienda Napoles.\n* He was a fan of the Colombian soccer team, Atlético Nacional, and even sponsored the team.\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world at the time.\n* He was known for his extravagant spending, including buying a private island and a collection of exotic cars.\n* Escobar\'s death was a major blow to the Medellín cartel, which eventually collapsed without his leadership.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 10:50:00', '2026-03-20 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-20 10:50:18', '2026-03-20 10:50:18'),
(1255, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious cartels in the history of organized crime. He is often considered one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and dropped out of school in the seventh grade. Escobar began his career in crime as a car thief and a smuggler, but he eventually turned to cocaine trafficking in the 1970s.\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar co-founded the Medellín cartel with his cousin, Gustavo Gaviria, and other associates. The cartel quickly gained control of the cocaine trade in Colombia and expanded its operations to other countries, including the United States, Mexico, and Europe.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world. The cartel\'s success was due in part to Escobar\'s innovative tactics, including the use of small planes and boats to transport cocaine, and the creation of a network of hidden laboratories and warehouses.\n\nThe cartel\'s profits were enormous, and Escobar became one of the richest men in the world, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion. He used his wealth to build a lavish lifestyle, including a private zoo, a collection of exotic cars, and a sprawling estate called Hacienda Napoles.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nHowever, Escobar\'s success was also marked by violence and terror. The Medellín cartel was responsible for countless murders, kidnappings, and bombings, including the assassination of politicians, judges, and police officers who dared to oppose them.\n\nIn 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán, who was a strong opponent of the cartel. The killing sparked a wave of violence and retaliation, and Escobar\'s popularity began to decline.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn 1991, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a massive manhunt for Escobar. The search was led by the Colombian police and the U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA).\n\nEscobar went into hiding, and a series of intense battles between the cartel and the authorities ensued. In 1992, Escobar escaped from prison, where he had been serving a sentence for murder, and went into hiding again.\n\n**Death**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a shootout in Medellín. The police had tracked him down to a rooftop in the city, where he was hiding with his bodyguard.\n\nEscobar\'s death marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror, and it paved the way for the rise of other cartels and organized crime groups in Colombia.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and clever entrepreneur who built a massive business empire and became one of the richest men in the world.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which tells the story of his rise and fall.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s story is a fascinating and cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime and the corrupting influence of power and wealth.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 10:53:00', '2026-03-20 10:53:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-20 10:53:18', '2026-03-20 10:53:18'),
(1256, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a relatable caption for a dragon-themed business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of breathing fire into our passions and pursuits. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Set goals that make your heart roar\n* Don\'t be afraid to take risks and fly into the unknown\n* Surround yourself with people who fuel your fire\n* Remember to take breaks and rest in your cave - self-care is essential\n\nLet\'s spread our wings and soar to new heights together! #DragonsDen #BusinessTips #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #FireUpYourPassion #EntrepreneurLife #DragonSlaying #SuccessMindset\"\n\nThis caption uses a professional tone while still being relatable and engaging. The use of hashtags like #TrendingNow and #MotivationMonday can help increase the post\'s visibility and reach a wider audience.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 11:18:00', '2026-03-20 11:18:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-03-20 11:18:15', '2026-03-20 11:18:15'),
(1257, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:39', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing your inner fire. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Believe in yourself and your abilities - you are capable of achieving great things!\n* Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things - it\'s often the best way to learn and grow\n* Surround yourself with people who support and uplift you - a strong community can make all the difference\n* Take care of your physical and mental health - a happy and healthy dragon is a powerful one!\n\n#DragonSquad #FireBreathingMotivation #InnerStrength #MentalHealthMatters #SelfCare #PositiveVibesOnly #TrendingNow #DragonInspiration #MythicalCreatures #FantasyLovers #BusinessMotivation\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, as well as some niche-specific ones to reach a wider audience. The brand voice is professional and relatable, making it suitable for a business page on Facebook.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 11:39:00', '2026-03-20 11:39:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 35, '2026-03-20 11:39:15', '2026-03-20 11:39:15'),
(1258, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'When it comes to party wear for men, there are numerous options to choose from, depending on the occasion, theme, and personal style. Here are some popular and stylish party wear ideas for men:\n\n**Formal Parties:**\n\n1. **Suits**: A classic choice, suits are perfect for formal parties like weddings, galas, and black-tie events. Choose from a range of colors, fabrics, and styles, such as navy, black, gray, or patterned.\n2. **Dress Shirts**: Pair a dress shirt with a suit or a blazer for a stylish and elegant look. Opt for a crisp, white, or light-colored shirt with a slim collar.\n3. **Tuxedos**: For a more luxurious and sophisticated look, consider a tuxedo. Perfect for black-tie events, tuxedos are available in various styles, including single-breasted, double-breasted, and peak lapel.\n\n**Semi-Formal Parties:**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A blazer can add a touch of sophistication to a casual outfit. Pair it with a dress shirt, dark jeans, and dress shoes for a stylish look.\n2. **Dress Pants**: Dress pants in dark colors like navy, gray, or black are versatile and can be paired with a variety of tops, including dress shirts, sweaters, or polo shirts.\n3. **Polo Shirts**: Polo shirts are a great option for semi-formal parties. Look for ones with a slim collar and a fitted silhouette.\n\n**Casual Parties:**\n\n1. **Graphic T-Shirts**: Graphic t-shirts are perfect for casual parties like birthday bashes or game nights. Pair them with jeans or shorts for a relaxed look.\n2. **Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans are a staple for casual parties. Pair them with a graphic t-shirt, a sweater, or a leather jacket for a stylish look.\n3. **Hoodies**: Hoodies are great for casual parties, especially during the winter months. Look for ones with a fitted silhouette and a bold design.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Watches**: A watch can add a touch of sophistication to any outfit. Choose from a range of styles, including leather-strapped, metal, or smartwatches.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to a dress shirt. Opt for ones that match your shirt or suit.\n3. **Shoes**: Dress shoes, loafers, or boots can complete a party outfit. Choose from a range of styles, including oxfords, brogues, or Chelsea boots.\n\n**Grooming:**\n\n1. **Hairstyle**: Style your hair with a comb, pomade, or hair wax for a sleek and polished look.\n2. **Beard**: Trim or shape your beard to complement your outfit.\n3. **Fragrance**: Apply a fragrance that suits your personality and style.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Experiment with different styles, and don\'t be afraid to add your own personal touch to your outfit!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 12:40:00', '2026-03-20 12:41:06', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/Party_Wear_for_Mens', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-03-20 12:41:06', '2026-03-20 12:41:06');
