(1282, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business/creator on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing my true self and living life to the fullest. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Be fearless and take risks - it\'s the only way to truly grow and learn\n* Never be afraid to show your true colors - authenticity is key to building strong relationships\n* Protect and care for those around you - being a good friend and ally is just as important as being a powerful dragon\n* Don\'t be afraid to take a step back and breathe - self-care is essential for maintaining your physical and mental health\n* Always keep learning and growing - there\'s always more to discover and explore in this world\n\n#DragonSquad #FireBreathingMotivation #ScaleNewHeights #TrendingNow #DragonLife #MythicalCreatures #FantasyInspiration #BusinessOfBeingABoss #EntrepreneurLife #MotivationMonday #TuesdayTips #WednesdayWisdom #ThursdayThoughts #FridayFeeling\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending hashtags, as well as some niche-specific hashtags to attract the target audience. The brand voice is professional and inspiring, with a touch of personality and humor.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-21 10:35:00', '2026-03-21 10:35:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-03-21 10:35:15', '2026-03-21 10:35:15'),
(1283, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working in the streets, selling fruit and cigarettes.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in crime began in the 1970s, when he worked as a car thief and a smuggler. He eventually turned to cocaine trafficking, which became his main source of income. In the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín cartel, which quickly became one of the largest and most powerful cartels in the world.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel was a highly organized and efficient operation that controlled the production, transportation, and distribution of cocaine. Escobar was the leader of the cartel, and he used his charm, intelligence, and ruthlessness to build a vast network of loyal associates and operatives. The cartel\'s operations spanned the globe, with connections in Colombia, Panama, the United States, and other countries.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar was known for his brutal tactics and his willingness to use violence to achieve his goals. He ordered the assassination of politicians, judges, and police officers who opposed him, as well as the murder of rival cartel members and anyone else who got in his way. The Medellín cartel was responsible for thousands of deaths, including the killing of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The Colombian police and military engaged in a fierce battle with the Medellín cartel, and Escobar was eventually forced to go into hiding.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal crime lord who was responsible for thousands of deaths and untold suffering. However, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful empire. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a vast estate in Medellín.\n* He was a skilled businessman and was able to amass a vast fortune, estimated to be around $30 billion at the time of his death.\n* Escobar was a fan of soccer and owned a team in Colombia, the Atlético Nacional.\n* He was a devout Catholic and built a church in Medellín, which still stands today.\n* Escobar\'s grave in Medellín has become a tourist attraction, with many visitors paying their respects to the notorious crime lord.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-21 10:45:00', '2026-03-21 10:45:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-21 10:45:20', '2026-03-21 10:45:20'),
(1284, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and feared organized crime groups in history. Here\'s a brief overview of his life and rise to infamy:\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. He was a bright and charismatic student, but he dropped out of school in the seventh grade to pursue a life of crime.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his criminal career in the 1970s, smuggling cigarettes and other goods. He quickly moved on to more lucrative ventures, including cocaine trafficking. In the early 1980s, he partnered with other Colombian traffickers to form the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, smuggling tons of the drug into the United States, Europe, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s cunning, ruthlessness, and strategic thinking. He was known for his ability to bribe and intimidate officials, as well as his willingness to use violence to eliminate rivals and enemies.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by brutal violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, judges, police officers, and innocent civilians. He was also known for his use of car bombs, assassinations, and other forms of terrorism. In 1989, he ordered the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán, who was a strong opponent of the cartel.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar went into hiding, but he was eventually tracked down by Colombian police and U.S. DEA agents. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed in a rooftop shootout in Medellín, Colombia. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal criminal who was responsible for immense suffering and violence. However, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of luxury and extravagance. He owned a private zoo, a collection of rare cars, and a sprawling estate in Medellín.\n* He was a skilled manipulator and was able to bribe and intimidate many Colombian officials, including politicians, judges, and police officers.\n* Escobar was a prolific philanthropist and was known for his charitable donations to poor communities in Colombia. However, his philanthropy was often seen as a way to buy loyalty and support for his cartel.\n* He was a devoted family man and was married to María Victoria Henao, with whom he had two children.\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power, making him one of the richest people in the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-21 10:50:00', '2026-03-21 10:50:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-21 10:50:17', '2026-03-21 10:50:17');
