(1389, 'Auto Post for facebook at 14:00', 'Here\'s a possible Facebook post for a business/creator with the description of a dragon:\n\n**Post:**\n\"Embracing our inner fire \nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned to harness my passion and energy to achieve my goals. Here are some key takeaways:\n* Believe in yourself and your abilities\n* Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things\n* Surround yourself with people who support and encourage you\n* Keep learning and growing, both personally and professionally\n* Stay true to your values and vision\n\nBy following these principles, you can unlock your full potential and achieve greatness. Remember to stay focused, stay driven, and always keep your inner fire burning!\n\n#MotivationMonday #DragonEnergy #InnerFire #BelieveInYourself #TrendingNow #BusinessTips #PersonalGrowth #ProfessionalDevelopment #FacebookBusiness\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, including #MotivationMonday, #TrendingNow, and #BusinessTips, to increase the post\'s visibility and reach. The tone of the post is professional and relatable, with a touch of personality and flair.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-24 14:00:00', '2026-03-24 14:00:27', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds', NULL, 'pending', 51, '2026-03-24 14:00:27', '2026-03-24 14:00:27'),
(1390, 'Auto Post for facebook at 14:36', 'Wood collection can refer to the process of gathering and storing wood for various purposes, such as:\n\n1. **Firewood collection**: Gathering wood for use as fuel for heating, cooking, or other purposes.\n2. **Timber collection**: Harvesting trees for lumber, pulp, or other wood products.\n3. **Driftwood collection**: Gathering wood that has washed up on beaches or rivers, often used for decorative or craft purposes.\n4. **Woodcraft collection**: Collecting wood for use in woodworking, woodcarving, or other craft projects.\n\nSome tips for wood collection:\n\n1. **Sustainability**: Ensure that wood collection is done in a sustainable manner, without harming the environment or depleting natural resources.\n2. **Safety**: Wear protective gear, such as gloves and safety glasses, when handling wood.\n3. **Quality**: Choose wood that is dry, straight, and free of defects.\n4. **Storage**: Store wood in a dry, well-ventilated area to prevent rot and insect damage.\n\nTypes of wood that are commonly collected:\n\n1. **Hardwoods**: Oak, maple, cherry, and walnut are popular for their strength and beauty.\n2. **Softwoods**: Pine, spruce, and fir are often used for construction and fuel.\n3. **Exotic woods**: Woods like mahogany, teak, and ebony are prized for their unique grain patterns and durability.\n\nWood collection can be a fun and rewarding hobby, but it\'s essential to follow local regulations and guidelines to ensure responsible and sustainable practices.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-24 14:36:00', '2026-03-24 14:36:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://pollinations.ai/p/table', NULL, 'pending', 11, '2026-03-24 14:36:17', '2026-03-24 14:36:17'),
