(1597, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor household with his mother, Hermilda, and his father, Abel. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and inform his actions.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime at a young age, selling stolen cars and contraband. He eventually turned to cocaine smuggling, which would become the foundation of his empire. In the 1970s, Escobar partnered with Carlos Lehder, a Colombian-American cocaine trafficker, to establish a cocaine smuggling operation. The partnership proved lucrative, and Escobar\'s wealth and influence grew rapidly.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world. The cartel\'s success was built on a combination of factors, including:\n\n1. **Cocaine production**: Escobar controlled a significant portion of Colombia\'s coca leaf production, which he used to manufacture high-quality cocaine.\n2. **Smuggling networks**: The cartel established an extensive network of smugglers, who transported cocaine from Colombia to the United States and other countries.\n3. **Intimidation and violence**: Escobar and his associates used violence and intimidation to maintain control over their territory and eliminate rivals.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The murder of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: Escobar ordered the assassination of Galán, who had vowed to crack down on the Medellín Cartel.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: Escobar\'s associates planted a bomb on the flight, which exploded mid-air, killing 110 people.\n3. **The murder of Colombian police officers**: Escobar ordered the killing of numerous police officers who had been tasked with capturing him.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the assistance of the United States, launched a series of operations aimed at capturing or killing Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was responsible for countless deaths and suffering, he also:\n\n1. **Created jobs and economic opportunities**: The Medellín Cartel provided employment and income for thousands of people in Colombia.\n2. **Invested in infrastructure and social programs**: Escobar invested in roads, schools, and healthcare facilities in Medellín, which improved the quality of life for many residents.\n3. ** Became a cultural icon**: Escobar\'s larger-than-life personality and exploits have inspired numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy serve as a cautionary tale about the dangers of unchecked power, corruption, and the destructive nature of the drug trade.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-31 10:50:00', '2026-03-31 10:50:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-31 10:50:19', '2026-03-31 10:50:19'),
(1598, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he dropped out of school in the seventh grade.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was then a relatively small and disorganized industry. He quickly rose to prominence due to his cunning, ruthlessness, and business acumen. Escobar\'s organization, the Medellín cartel, dominated the cocaine trade in the 1980s, and he became one of the wealthiest men in the world.\n\n**Criminal Empire**\n\nEscobar\'s organization was responsible for smuggling massive amounts of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other countries. He used a variety of methods to transport the drugs, including planes, ships, and even submarines. The Medellín cartel also used violence and intimidation to maintain control over the trade and eliminate competitors.\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar\'s organization was estimated to be earning over $20 billion per year, making him one of the richest men in the world. He invested his wealth in real estate, businesses, and other ventures, and he became a prominent figure in Colombian society.\n\n**Violence and Notoriety**\n\nEscobar\'s organization was responsible for numerous violent acts, including murders, kidnappings, and bombings. He was known for his ruthless tactics, and his organization was feared by law enforcement and rival gangs.\n\nIn 1989, Escobar\'s organization was responsible for the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people. He was also suspected of ordering the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, he escaped from the prison in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\nA massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down by Colombian police and American DEA agents. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed in a rooftop shootout in Medellín, Colombia. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering. However, he is also seen as a symbol of Colombian culture and a reminder of the country\'s tumultuous past.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, and his name has become synonymous with the cocaine trade and organized crime.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate in Medellín.\n* He was a skilled politician and was elected to the Colombian Congress in 1982.\n* Escobar was a devout Catholic and was known to have made large donations to the Catholic Church.\n* He was a fan of soccer and was the owner of a Colombian soccer team, Atlético Nacional.\n* Escobar\'s death was celebrated by many Colombians, who saw him as a symbol of the country\'s corruption and violence.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-31 10:53:00', '2026-03-31 10:53:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-03-31 10:53:17', '2026-03-31 10:53:17'),
(1599, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Empowering Your Business: Key Takeaways**\n\nAs a dragon in the business world, I\'ve learned a thing or two about what it takes to succeed. Here are some key points to keep in mind:\n\n* **Set clear goals**: Define your objectives and prioritize your tasks to achieve them.\n* **Be adaptable**: Stay flexible and adjust to changing circumstances to stay ahead of the competition.\n* **Foster a positive work environment**: Encourage collaboration, creativity, and open communication among your team members.\n* **Invest in yourself**: Continuously learn and develop new skills to stay relevant in your industry.\n* **Stay organized**: Manage your time and resources effectively to maximize productivity.\n\n#BusinessTips #ProductivityHacks #LeadershipGoals #Entrepreneurship #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #BusinessSuccess #DragonApproved #FacebookForBusiness', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-31 11:18:00', '2026-03-31 11:18:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-03-31 11:18:14', '2026-03-31 11:18:14'),
(1600, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:57', 'A pen is a writing instrument used to apply ink to a surface, typically paper, to create written characters, symbols, and drawings. It consists of a nib or tip that dispenses ink onto the paper as the user moves it.\n\nThere are several types of pens, including:\n\n1. **Ballpoint pens**: These use a small metal ball to dispense ink onto the paper.\n2. **Rollerball pens**: These use a small metal ball to dispense liquid ink onto the paper.\n3. **Fountain pens**: These use a nib to dispense ink from an ink reservoir, often refillable.\n4. **Gel pens**: These use a water-based ink that is suspended in a gel-like substance.\n5. **Fineliners**: These are fine-tip pens often used for detailed work, such as drawing and illustration.\n\nPens have been an essential tool for writing and communication throughout history, with early forms of pens made from reeds, quills, and other materials. Today, pens are an everyday item used by people all over the world for a variety of purposes, from writing and drawing to signing documents and creating art.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-31 11:57:00', '2026-03-31 11:58:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen?model=flux&width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 16, '2026-03-31 11:58:23', '2026-03-31 11:58:23'),
(1601, 'Auto Post for instagram at 11:59', 'A pen packet is a small, usually sealed, package that contains one or more pens, often along with an ink refill or other accessories. These packets are commonly used for promotional purposes, such as:\n\n1. **Free samples**: Companies may distribute pen packets as free samples to promote their brand, product, or service.\n2. **Marketing campaigns**: Pen packets can be used as a marketing tool to reach a large audience, with the pen serving as a reminder of the company\'s message or logo.\n3. **Conventions and events**: Pen packets are often distributed at conferences, trade shows, and other events to provide attendees with a useful item while promoting the company\'s brand.\n\nA typical pen packet may contain:\n\n* A pen (or multiple pens)\n* An ink refill\n* A business card or brochure\n* A promotional insert or flyer\n* A sticker or other small accessory\n\nPen packets can be customized with a company\'s logo, branding, and messaging, making them a effective way to promote a business or product.', '[\"instagram\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-03-31 11:59:00', '2026-03-31 12:00:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen_Packet?model=flux&width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 17, '2026-03-31 12:00:24', '2026-03-31 12:00:24'),
