(1633, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'As a dragon, I\'d like to share with you what makes my day-to-day life exciting and relatable. Here are a few points:\n\n* Waking up early to take in the breathtaking views from my mountain lair\n* Managing my treasure hoard and making sure it\'s always up-to-date\n* Taking breaks to fly around and enjoy the thrill of soaring through the skies\n* Meeting with my fellow dragon friends to discuss the latest dragon trends and news\n* Continuously learning and improving my fire-breathing skills to stay ahead of the game\n\n#DragonLife #Relatable #FireBreathing #TreasureHoard #MountainLair #FlyingHigh #DragonSquad #TrendingNow #DragonTales #MythicalCreatures #FantasyLife #LegendaryBeast', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-01 10:35:00', '2026-04-01 10:35:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-01 10:35:14', '2026-04-01 10:35:14'),
(1634, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and limited opportunities, which led him to turn to crime at a young age. He began his career as a car thief and a smuggler, but soon became involved in the cocaine trade.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar partnered with other Colombian traffickers to form the Medellín cartel, which quickly became one of the dominant players in the global cocaine market. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him to rise to the top of the organization, and he eventually became the leader of the cartel.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel expanded its operations and became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and its profits were estimated to be in the billions of dollars.\n\nEscobar\'s success was due in part to his ability to corrupt and intimidate government officials, police, and other rival traffickers. He was known for his brutal tactics, including murder, kidnapping, and torture, which he used to eliminate his enemies and maintain control over his empire.\n\n**The War on Drugs and the Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the 1980s, the United States and Colombian governments launched a joint effort to take down the Medellín cartel and bring Escobar to justice. The war on drugs, as it came to be known, was marked by intense violence and bloodshed, as Escobar and his associates fought to maintain their power and control.\n\nThe hunt for Escobar became a major international effort, with the US and Colombian governments offering large rewards for his capture. Escobar went into hiding, using his network of loyal associates and corrupt officials to evade capture.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\nEscobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and brutal criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful empire through his intelligence and strategic thinking.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, and his impact on the global drug trade and the war on drugs remains a topic of debate and discussion.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate in Medellín.\n* He was a skilled politician and was able to build relationships with high-ranking government officials and business leaders.\n* Escobar was a prolific philanthropist, and he used his wealth to build roads, schools, and hospitals in poor communities.\n* He was a devout Catholic and was known to have a strong sense of loyalty and family values.\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power, making him one of the richest people in the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-01 10:45:00', '2026-04-01 10:45:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-01 10:45:15', '2026-04-01 10:45:15'),
(1635, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug cartels in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor household and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, and his father, Abel. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was exposed to the world of crime at a young age.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began his career in crime by smuggling contraband and stealing cars. He eventually turned to cocaine trafficking, which became the foundation of his empire. Escobar\'s rise to power was rapid, and by the mid-1980s, he had become one of the wealthiest and most influential men in Colombia.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, led by Escobar, was a massive and complex organization that dominated the global cocaine trade. The cartel\'s operations were highly organized, with a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and ruthlessness, and he was feared by his enemies and respected by his allies.\n\nAt the height of its power, the Medellín cartel was responsible for smuggling an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine into the United States. Escobar\'s empire was worth an estimated $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and journalists. Escobar\'s organization was known for its use of bombings, assassinations, and kidnappings to intimidate and eliminate its enemies.\n\nOne of the most notable examples of Escobar\'s violence was the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989. Galán was a leading candidate in the presidential election and had vowed to crack down on the Medellín cartel. Escobar\'s organization was also responsible for the bombing of Avianca Flight 203 in 1989, which killed 110 people.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar\'s organization was weakened by internal power struggles and the loss of key allies.\n\nOn June 19, 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility, known as the \"Cathedral.\" However, Escobar continued to run his empire from prison, and in July 1992, he escaped and went into hiding.\n\nA massive manhunt was launched, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. His death marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror and paved the way for the rise of other cartels in Colombia.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and calculating leader who was able to build a vast and powerful empire.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His life and death have also had a lasting impact on Colombian politics and society, and his legacy continues to be felt today.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s legacy has been the subject of controversy, with some arguing that he was a folk hero who was unfairly targeted by the Colombian government and the United States. Others argue that he was a brutal and ruthless criminal who deserves no sympathy or admiration.\n\nRegardless of how one views Escobar\'s legacy, it is clear that he was a significant figure in the history of organized crime and that his impact on Colombian society and politics will be felt for generations to come.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-01 10:50:00', '2026-04-01 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-01 10:50:18', '2026-04-01 10:50:18'),
(1636, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and powerful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life:**\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He grew up in a humble household with his parents and siblings. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty, and he was forced to drop out of school to work and support his family.\n\n**Rise to Power:**\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began his career in crime, initially as a small-time smuggler and thief. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by his cousin, Gustavo Gaviria. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness earned him the respect and loyalty of his peers, and he soon became a key player in the organization.\n\n**Medellín Cartel:**\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared crime syndicates in the world. The cartel\'s main business was cocaine trafficking, and Escobar\'s network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers helped to flood the global market with the drug. At the height of his power, Escobar\'s organization was estimated to be worth over $30 billion.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation:**\nEscobar was known for his brutal tactics and his willingness to use violence to maintain control and eliminate his enemies. He was responsible for the murders of hundreds of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and rival gang members. His organization also carried out bombings, kidnappings, and other terrorist attacks.\n\n**Manhunt and Death:**\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially designed facility, known as the \"Cathedral,\" which he had built for himself. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt ensued, involving Colombian and American law enforcement agencies. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy:**\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to many people, but he was also a charismatic and calculating leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts:**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a vast estate, known as Hacienda Napoles.\n* He was a skilled politician and was able to build alliances with other crime lords and politicians.\n* Escobar was a major contributor to the Colombian economy, and his organization was estimated to have employed thousands of people.\n* He was a devout Catholic and was known to have made large donations to the Catholic Church.\n* Escobar\'s death was seen as a major victory for law enforcement, but it also led to a power vacuum in the Medellín cartel, which was eventually filled by other crime lords.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-01 10:53:00', '2026-04-01 10:53:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-01 10:53:16', '2026-04-01 10:53:16'),
(1637, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'As a dragon in the business world, I understand the importance of being relatable and authentic. Here\'s a relatable caption in points, along with some trending hashtags for Facebook:\n\n**Embracing My True Self**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned to love and accept myself for who I am. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Being different is what makes me unique and special\n* I don\'t have to hide my true nature to fit in\n* My fiery personality is an asset, not a liability\n* I\'m capable of achieving great things, even if I don\'t always follow the traditional path\n\n#DragonsInBusiness #EmbracingMyTrueSelf #SelfAcceptance #DiversityAndInclusion #TrendingNow #MotivationMonday #Inspiration #DragonPower #FireBreathingEntrepreneur #ScaleNewHeights #RoarWithConfidence\n\nBy sharing my story and using relevant hashtags, I hope to inspire and motivate others to be their authentic selves, both in business and in life. Remember, being different is what makes you special, and embracing your true self is the key to success.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-01 11:18:00', '2026-04-01 11:18:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-01 11:18:14', '2026-04-01 11:18:14'),
