(1692, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a symbol of strength, courage, and resilience, dragons have long fascinated humans. Here are some key takeaways from the dragon\'s world that can be applied to our own lives:\n\n* **Believe in yourself**: Just like a dragon\'s roar can be heard for miles, our confidence and self-assurance can make a lasting impact on those around us.\n* **Protect your passions**: Dragons are known for guarding their treasure, and we should do the same with our goals and aspirations.\n* **Embrace change**: A dragon\'s ability to adapt to new environments and situations is a valuable lesson in being flexible and open to new experiences.\n* **Lead with wisdom**: As a mythical creature, dragons are often seen as wise and just leaders, reminding us of the importance of making informed decisions and guiding others with kindness and compassion.\n\n#DragonEnergy #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #Inspiration #PersonalGrowth #LeadershipLessons #ConfidenceIsKey #ResilienceMatters #BelieveInYourself', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 10:35:00', '2026-04-03 10:35:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-03 10:35:14', '2026-04-03 10:35:14'),
(1693, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, often referred to as the \"King of Cocaine.\" He was the founder and leader of the Medellín cartel, which became one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world during the 1980s.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he became involved in crime at a young age. He started by selling stolen cars and eventually moved on to more serious crimes, such as robbery and smuggling.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia. He began by working for other smugglers, but soon established his own operation. Escobar\'s success in the cocaine trade was due in part to his ruthless tactics and his ability to bribe and intimidate law enforcement officials.\n\nBy the early 1980s, Escobar had become one of the most powerful men in Colombia, with a vast network of cocaine producers, smugglers, and distributors. He was known for his charisma and his ability to inspire loyalty in his followers, who were often drawn to his wealth and power.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, which Escobar founded and led, was responsible for smuggling vast quantities of cocaine into the United States and other countries. The cartel\'s operations were highly organized and sophisticated, with a complex network of producers, smugglers, and distributors.\n\nEscobar\'s organization was also known for its brutality and violence. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including rival gang members, law enforcement officials, and innocent civilians. Escobar\'s tactics included bombings, assassinations, and kidnappings, which terrorized the people of Colombia and earned him the nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss).\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of crackdowns on the Medellín cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, but he continued to orchestrate his operations from secret locations.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death. The circumstances surrounding his death are still disputed, with some claiming that he was betrayed by one of his own associates.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. However, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His life and death have also been the subject of much debate and controversy, with some viewing him as a folk hero and others as a monstrous villain.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of luxury and extravagance. He owned a private zoo, a collection of exotic cars, and a vast array of expensive jewelry and artwork.\n* Escobar was a skilled politician and was able to build alliances with other powerful figures in Colombia, including politicians and military leaders.\n* Escobar\'s organization was responsible for the production of an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine during the 1980s.\n* Escobar\'s death was a major blow to the Medellín cartel, which eventually collapsed in the years following his death.\n* Escobar\'s legacy continues to be felt in Colombia, where he is still remembered as a powerful and feared figure.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 10:45:00', '2026-04-03 10:45:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-03 10:45:16', '2026-04-03 10:45:16'),
(1694, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord and founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and feared criminal organizations in the world. He is often referred to as the \"King of Cocaine\" due to his dominance of the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Dari Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a poor household with several siblings and was raised in a traditional Colombian family. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his involvement in organized crime.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, which was founded by his cousin, Gustavo Gaviria. In the early 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the cartel, and his organization began to dominate the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Cocaine Empire**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel expanded its operations to include cocaine production, transportation, and distribution. The cartel used sophisticated methods to smuggle cocaine into the United States, including the use of submarines, planes, and hidden compartments in cars and trucks. Escobar\'s organization also used violence and intimidation to maintain control over the cocaine trade, including assassinations, bombings, and kidnappings.\n\n**Personal Life**\n\nEscobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a mansion in Medellín. He was also known for his charitable works, including building homes and roads for poor communities in Colombia. However, his personal life was also marked by violence and controversy, including his involvement in the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a campaign to capture or kill Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped from prison in 1992. A massive manhunt was launched, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning leader who built a vast cocaine empire, but also as a charismatic figure who was able to inspire loyalty and devotion in his followers. His life and death have been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" However, his legacy is also marked by the devastating impact of his organization\'s violence and corruption on Colombian society.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power.\n* He was known for his love of soccer and even built a soccer stadium in Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s organization was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, and politicians.\n* He was a skilled politician and was able to manipulate the Colombian government and media to his advantage.\n* Escobar\'s death was a major blow to the Medellín Cartel, and the organization began to fragment and decline after his death.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 10:50:00', '2026-04-03 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-03 10:50:18', '2026-04-03 10:50:18'),
(1695, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, narco-terrorist, and one of the most notorious criminals of the 20th century. He is widely regarded as one of the most successful and ruthless drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and inform his actions.\n\nEscobar began his career in crime at a young age, selling stolen cars and cigarettes. He eventually turned to smuggling, first with whiskey and later with cocaine. In the early 1970s, Escobar partnered with other smugglers to form the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel and Escobar\'s Empire**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel expanded rapidly, and he became one of the wealthiest and most powerful men in Colombia. At the height of his empire, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world.\n\nEscobar\'s operation was notorious for its brutality and efficiency. He used violence, intimidation, and bribery to maintain control over his empire, which included a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. He also invested heavily in real estate, construction, and other legitimate businesses to launder his profits and expand his influence.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Violence**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous heinous crimes, including:\n\n1. **The Palace of Justice siege**: In 1985, Escobar\'s henchmen stormed the Palace of Justice in Bogotá, taking hundreds of hostages and killing over 100 people, including several Supreme Court justices.\n2. **The assassination of Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Galán, a presidential candidate who had vowed to crack down on the Medellín Cartel.\n3. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s operatives planted a bomb on an Avianca flight, killing 110 people.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility, known as the \"Cathedral,\" which he had designed himself. However, he escaped in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\nA massive manhunt ensued, with the Colombian military and police, assisted by the US DEA and CIA, searching for Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed in a rooftop shootout with Colombian police in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy and Cultural Impact**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the US, which many Colombians perceived as corrupt and oppressive.\n\nEscobar\'s life and exploits have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which chronicles his rise and fall. His story has also inspired countless articles, documentaries, and podcasts, cementing his place in popular culture as one of the most infamous figures of the 20th century.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 10:53:00', '2026-04-03 10:53:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-03 10:53:18', '2026-04-03 10:53:18'),
(1696, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a powerful and mythical creature, I\'ve learned a thing or two about resilience, adaptability, and passion. Here are some key takeaways from my journey:\n\n* **Embracing change**: Just like the cycles of fire and ice, life is full of ups and downs. Learn to adapt and thrive in any environment.\n* **Protecting your treasure**: Whether it\'s your family, your business, or your personal goals, be fierce in defending what matters most to you.\n* **Soaring to new heights**: Don\'t be afraid to take risks and push beyond your comfort zone. The view from the top is always worth it.\n* **Breathing fire**: Pursue your passions with unrelenting energy and enthusiasm. When you\'re doing what you love, the fire within you will burn bright.\n\n#DragonsDen #BusinessLessons #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #FireWithin #ProfessionalGrowth #FacebookBusiness #MythicalMentor #LessonsFromADragon #Inspiration #MondayMotivation', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 11:18:00', '2026-04-03 11:18:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-03 11:18:14', '2026-04-03 11:18:14'),
(1697, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:39', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Den**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about perseverance, adaptability, and passion. Here are some key takeaways that can help you ignite your own inner fire:\n\n* **Set clear goals**: Just like a dragon protects its treasure, define what\'s precious to you and focus on achieving it.\n* **Be resilient**: Life can be unpredictable, but with a strong will and determination, you can overcome any obstacle.\n* **Stay curious**: Continuously learn and explore new ideas, just like a dragon discovers new lands and hoards knowledge.\n* **Build a supportive community**: Surround yourself with people who believe in you and your vision, just like a dragon\'s loyal followers.\n* **Take calculated risks**: Don\'t be afraid to take bold steps, just like a dragon soaring through the skies.\n\nBy embracing these principles, you\'ll be well on your way to unleashing your full potential and achieving greatness.\n\n#DragonInspiration #MotivationMonday #FireWithin #GoalSetting #Resilience #Curiosity #CommunityFirst #RiskAndReward #TrendingNow #FacebookInspiration #ProfessionalGrowth #PersonalDevelopment #BusinessTips #SuccessStories', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 11:39:00', '2026-04-03 11:39:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 35, '2026-04-03 11:39:15', '2026-04-03 11:39:15'),
(1698, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', '**Party Wear for Men:**\n\nWhen it comes to dressing up for a party, men have a wide range of options to choose from. Here are some popular party wear ideas for men:\n\n1. **Suits:** A well-tailored suit is a classic choice for any party. You can opt for a black, navy, or gray suit, and pair it with a crisp white shirt and a tie.\n2. **Blazers:** A blazer can add a touch of sophistication to any outfit. You can wear it with a dress shirt, trousers, and dress shoes for a stylish look.\n3. **Dress Shirts:** A dress shirt is a must-have for any party. You can choose from a variety of colors and patterns, and pair it with trousers or jeans.\n4. **Trousers:** Trousers are a versatile option for party wear. You can wear them with a dress shirt, blazer, or a casual shirt.\n5. **Jeans:** Dark-washed jeans are a great option for a more casual party. You can pair them with a dress shirt, blazer, or a casual shirt.\n6. **Shoes:** Dress shoes, such as oxfords or loafers, are a must-have for any party. You can also opt for boots or sneakers for a more casual look.\n7. **Accessories:** Add a touch of personality to your outfit with accessories like a watch, cufflinks, or a pocket square.\n\n**Party Wear Ideas for Men:**\n\n1. **Formal Party:** Wear a suit, tie, and dress shoes for a formal party.\n2. **Semi-Formal Party:** Wear a blazer, dress shirt, and trousers for a semi-formal party.\n3. **Casual Party:** Wear jeans, a casual shirt, and sneakers for a casual party.\n4. **Theme Party:** Dress according to the theme of the party, such as a suit for a James Bond theme or a Hawaiian shirt for a luau theme.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Dress according to the occasion:** Make sure to dress according to the type of party you\'re attending.\n2. **Be confident:** Own your outfit and be confident in what you\'re wearing.\n3. **Pay attention to details:** Make sure your outfit is well-coordinated and pay attention to details like socks, belt, and accessories.\n4. **Groom yourself:** Make sure you\'re well-groomed, with a clean shave, trimmed hair, and fresh breath.\n\n**Popular Party Wear Brands for Men:**\n\n1. **Armani:** Known for their stylish and sophisticated suits.\n2. **Hugo Boss:** Offers a wide range of party wear options, from suits to casual shirts.\n3. **Calvin Klein:** Popular for their stylish and comfortable jeans and casual shirts.\n4. **Tommy Hilfiger:** Offers a wide range of party wear options, from suits to casual shirts.\n5. **Ralph Lauren:** Known for their classic and sophisticated party wear options.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 12:40:00', '2026-04-03 12:40:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-04-03 12:40:15', '2026-04-03 12:40:15'),
(1699, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of dress shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key features and considerations for formal shirts for men:\n\n**Types of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress Shirt:** A classic, collared shirt with a button-front closure and a fitted silhouette.\n2. **Dress Shirt with French Cuffs:** A dress shirt with cuffs that are folded back and fastened with cufflinks.\n3. **Wingtip Collar Shirt:** A dress shirt with a wing-shaped collar that is often worn with a bow tie.\n\n**Features of a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Collar Style:** Pointed, spread, or wingtip collars are common for formal shirts.\n2. **Cuff Style:** Barrel cuffs, French cuffs, or button cuffs are available.\n3. **Fabric:** High-quality cotton, linen, or silk fabrics are often used for formal shirts.\n4. **Fit:** Slim fit, regular fit, or tailored fit options are available to suit different body types.\n5. **Button Front:** A button-front closure is typical for formal shirts.\n6. **Pockets:** Some formal shirts may have a breast pocket or no pockets at all.\n\n**Popular Brands for Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink:** Known for their high-quality, stylish dress shirts.\n2. **Charvet:** A French luxury brand offering exquisite, bespoke dress shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers:** An American brand famous for their classic, preppy dress shirts.\n4. **Armani:** An Italian fashion brand offering elegant, sophisticated dress shirts.\n5. **Hugo Boss:** A German luxury brand providing high-quality, stylish dress shirts.\n\n**Tips for Choosing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the occasion:** Choose a shirt that matches the formality of the event.\n2. **Think about your body type:** Select a fit that flatters your physique.\n3. **Pay attention to fabric:** Choose a breathable, high-quality fabric that feels comfortable.\n4. **Accessories matter:** Pair your shirt with a suitable tie, cufflinks, and shoes.\n5. **Get it tailored:** If possible, have your shirt tailored to ensure a perfect fit.\n\n**Prices:**\n\nFormal shirts for men can range from affordable to very expensive, depending on the brand, quality, and features. Here are some approximate price ranges:\n\n1. **Budget-friendly:** $20-$50 (e.g., H&M, Uniqlo)\n2. **Mid-range:** $50-$100 (e.g., Gap, Banana Republic)\n3. **Luxury:** $100-$300 (e.g., Thomas Pink, Charvet)\n4. **High-end:** $300-$500 (e.g., Armani, Hugo Boss)\n5. **Bespoke:** $500-$1,000+ (e.g., custom-made shirts from high-end tailors)', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-03 12:56:00', '2026-04-03 12:56:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-04-03 12:56:17', '2026-04-03 12:56:17'),
