(1722, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Empowering Your Business with a Roar: Key Takeaways**\n\nAs a dragon in the business world, I\'ve learned a thing or two about what it takes to succeed. Here are some key points to consider:\n\n* **Set clear goals**: Define your vision and mission to stay focused on what matters most\n* **Build a strong team**: Surround yourself with talented and dedicated individuals who share your passion\n* **Innovate and adapt**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new technologies and trends\n* **Foster a positive company culture**: Encourage collaboration, creativity, and open communication\n* **Continuously learn and improve**: Stay up-to-date with industry developments and best practices\n\nBy following these principles, you\'ll be well on your way to achieving success and making a lasting impact in your field. #BusinessSuccess #Entrepreneurship #Innovation #Teamwork #Leadership #Trending #BusinessTips #Motivation #Inspiration #DragonApproved #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalDevelopment', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-04 10:35:00', '2026-04-04 10:35:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-04 10:35:14', '2026-04-04 10:35:14'),
(1723, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious organized crime groups in history. He is often considered one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He grew up in a violent and impoverished environment, which would later shape his worldview and inform his actions. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began his life of crime, starting with small-time thievery and smuggling.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was a rapidly growing and lucrative industry at the time. He quickly rose through the ranks, becoming a key player in the Medellín cartel, which was founded by his mentor, Carlos Lehder. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him build a vast network of associates and establish himself as a major player in the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organized crime groups in the world. The cartel\'s operations spanned the globe, with tentacles in Colombia, the United States, Europe, and Asia. Escobar\'s organization was responsible for smuggling massive quantities of cocaine into the United States, earning him an estimated $30 billion in profits.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his brutal tactics, using violence and intimidation to maintain control and eliminate rivals. He was responsible for numerous assassinations, bombings, and massacres, including the killing of Colombian politicians, judges, and police officers. Escobar\'s organization also targeted civilians, including journalists, activists, and ordinary citizens who dared to oppose him.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially designed facility, known as La Catedral, which he had built himself. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt ensued, with Colombian and American authorities working together to track him down.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. At the same time, he is also seen as a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the United States, which many Colombians viewed as corrupt and oppressive.\n\nEscobar\'s life and death have been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which chronicles his rise and fall. His story continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, serving as a cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime and the corrupting influence of power.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate, known as Hacienda Nápoles.\n* He was a prolific philanthropist, building schools, hospitals, and roads in his hometown of Medellín, which earned him a degree of popularity among locals.\n* Escobar\'s organization was responsible for the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n* He was known for his clever use of tunnels and hidden passages to evade authorities, earning him the nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss).\n* Escobar\'s death was met with widespread celebration in Colombia, with many people viewing it as a major victory in the war against organized crime.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-04 10:45:00', '2026-04-04 10:45:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-04 10:45:17', '2026-04-04 10:45:17'),
(1724, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely considered one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would shape his future actions. He began his criminal career as a teenager, smuggling goods and stealing cars.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was then a relatively new and lucrative business. He quickly rose through the ranks, becoming a key player in the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness made him a natural leader, and he eventually took control of the cartel.\n\n**Medellín Cartel and Cocaine Empire**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. Escobar\'s empire was built on the back of cocaine, which he smuggled into the United States, Europe, and other countries. He used a network of distributors, money launderers, and assassins to maintain control and eliminate rivals.\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world. He lived a lavish lifestyle, with a collection of luxury cars, houses, and artwork. Escobar also invested in legitimate businesses, such as real estate and agriculture, to launder his money and provide a cover for his illicit activities.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and rival gang members. Escobar\'s favorite method of dealing with enemies was to have them killed, often in brutal and public ways.\n\nOne of the most infamous examples of Escobar\'s violence was the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989. Escobar had Galán killed because he was seen as a threat to the cartel\'s interests. The murder sparked a wave of violence and intimidation, which Escobar used to maintain control and silence his opponents.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar\'s empire began to crumble, and he was forced to go into hiding.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was tracked down by Colombian police and killed in a shootout in Medellín. The circumstances of his death are still disputed, with some claiming that he was killed by police and others believing that he took his own life.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who built a vast empire through violence and intimidation. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the dark side of globalization and the failures of the war on drugs.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been immortalized in books, films, and TV series, including the popular Netflix show \"Narcos.\" His life and death have also sparked debates about the ethics of drug prohibition and the impact of the war on drugs on communities and individuals.\n\nIn Colombia, Escobar\'s legacy is still felt, with many people viewing him as a folk hero or a symbol of resistance against the government. However, others see him as a monster who brought terror and destruction to their country.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and death serve as a reminder of the dangers of unchecked power and the devastating consequences of the drug trade.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-04 10:50:00', '2026-04-04 10:50:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-04 10:50:15', '2026-04-04 10:50:15'),
(1725, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely considered one of the most notorious and powerful crime lords in history.\n\n**Early Life:**\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he quickly became involved in street crime and gang activity.\n\n**Rise to Power:**\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working for a local cocaine smuggler, and soon became involved in the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him rise through the ranks of the cartel, and he eventually became the leader of the organization.\n\n**Medellín Cartel:**\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and profitable crime organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and Escobar\'s wealth and influence grew exponentially. At the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion.\n\n**Violence and Terror:**\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, politicians, and innocent civilians. He also ordered the assassination of several high-profile targets, including Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán.\n\n**Manhunt and Death:**\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a luxurious prison he had built for himself. However, he escaped in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down and killed in a shootout with Colombian police on December 1, 1993, in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy:**\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the country\'s struggles with poverty, inequality, and corruption. Escobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts:**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate called Hacienda Napoles.\n* He was a skilled politician and was elected to the Colombian Congress in 1982.\n* Escobar was responsible for the construction of many soccer fields, schools, and hospitals in Medellín, which helped to gain him popularity and support among the local population.\n* He was a prolific user of violence and intimidation, and was known for his use of \"sicarios\" (hitmen) to carry out his orders.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy are a complex and fascinating topic, and his impact on Colombia and the world is still felt today.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-04 10:53:00', '2026-04-04 10:53:12', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-04 10:53:12', '2026-04-04 10:53:12'),
(1726, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Facebook Post:**\n\nAs a dragon, I understand the importance of setting goals and achieving them. Here are some relatable points to consider:\n\n* Setting realistic goals is crucial to success\n* Breaking down large tasks into smaller, manageable chunks can help reduce stress\n* Creating a schedule and sticking to it can increase productivity\n* Taking breaks and practicing self-care is essential for maintaining motivation\n* Surrounding yourself with supportive people can make a big difference in achieving your goals\n\nLet\'s work together to achieve our goals and make our dreams a reality. #Trending #GoalSetting #ProductivityHacks #MotivationMonday #SuccessTips #DragonInspiration #BusinessGoals #EntrepreneurMindset #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalDevelopment', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-04 11:18:00', '2026-04-04 11:18:13', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-04 11:18:13', '2026-04-04 11:18:13'),
(1727, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'When it comes to party wear for men, there are several styles and options to choose from, depending on the occasion, theme, and personal taste. Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-tailored suit is a classic choice for formal parties. You can opt for a black, navy, or gray suit, and pair it with a crisp white shirt and a tie.\n2. **Blazers**: A blazer can add a touch of sophistication to a party outfit. You can wear a blazer over a dress shirt and trousers, or with a T-shirt and jeans for a more casual look.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A dress shirt is a versatile option that can be dressed up or down. You can wear a plain white shirt or opt for a patterned or colored shirt to add some personality to your outfit.\n4. **Tuxedos**: A tuxedo is a great option for formal parties, such as black-tie events or weddings. Make sure to pair it with a bow tie and a cummerbund.\n5. **Jeans and a Nice Top**: For a more casual party, you can wear a pair of dark wash jeans with a nice top, such as a button-down shirt or a sweater.\n6. **Leather Jackets**: A leather jacket can add an edgy touch to a party outfit. You can wear it over a T-shirt and jeans, or with a dress shirt and trousers.\n7. **Accessories**: Don\'t forget to add some accessories to your outfit, such as a watch, a wallet, and a pair of cufflinks.\n\n**Party Themes**:\n\n1. **Formal**: For a formal party, opt for a suit, tie, and dress shoes.\n2. **Semi-Formal**: For a semi-formal party, wear a blazer, dress shirt, and dress shoes.\n3. **Casual**: For a casual party, wear a T-shirt, jeans, and sneakers.\n4. **Theme Party**: If the party has a specific theme, such as a Halloween party, dress accordingly.\n\n**Tips**:\n\n1. **Dress according to the occasion**: Make sure to dress according to the party\'s theme and formality level.\n2. **Pay attention to fit**: Ensure that your clothes fit well and are not too tight or too loose.\n3. **Groom yourself**: Make sure to groom yourself properly, including trimming your nails, shaving, and styling your hair.\n4. **Be confident**: Own your outfit and have fun at the party!\n\nSome popular party wear brands for men include:\n\n1. **Armani**\n2. **Gucci**\n3. **Tom Ford**\n4. **Ralph Lauren**\n5. **Hugo Boss**\n\nRemember, the key to pulling off a great party outfit is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-04 12:40:00', '2026-04-04 12:40:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-04-04 12:40:17', '2026-04-04 12:40:17');
