(1743, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Embracing the Fire Within: 5 Key Takeaways for Ambitious Entrepreneurs**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned to harness my inner fire to drive success. Here are some relatable points to consider:\n\n* **Set bold goals**: Just like a dragon sets its sights on a treasure hoard, you should aim high and be fearless in pursuit of your objectives.\n* **Develop a strong sense of self**: Understand your strengths, weaknesses, and passions to stay focused and motivated.\n* **Cultivate a supportive community**: Surround yourself with people who believe in you and your vision, just like a dragon\'s loyal hoard.\n* **Stay adaptable and resilient**: Be prepared to navigate challenges and setbacks, and remember that every failure is an opportunity to learn and grow.\n* **Keep learning and innovating**: Continuously update your skills and knowledge to stay ahead of the curve and stay relevant in your industry.\n\n#DragonEnergy #EntrepreneurMindset #BusinessSuccess #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #FacebookForBusiness #ProfessionalDevelopment #GoalSetting #CommunityFirst #ResilienceMatters #InnovationNation', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 10:35:00', '2026-04-05 10:35:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-05 10:35:17', '2026-04-05 10:35:17'),
(1744, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely considered one of the most notorious and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Career:**\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a peasant family. He grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in petty crime and eventually worked his way up to become a major player in the city\'s underworld. In the 1970s, Escobar began smuggling cocaine into the United States, and his operation quickly expanded to become one of the largest and most profitable in the world.\n\n**Rise to Power:**\nEscobar\'s success in the cocaine trade was largely due to his innovative and ruthless business practices. He invested heavily in infrastructure, including roads, bridges, and warehouses, to facilitate the production and transportation of cocaine. He also formed alliances with other crime groups and bribed or intimidated government officials to ensure his operation ran smoothly.\n\n**Medellín Cartel:**\nThe Medellín Cartel, which Escobar founded and led, became one of the most powerful and feared crime organizations in the world. At its peak, the cartel was responsible for producing and distributing an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutal tactics, including murder, kidnapping, and extortion.\n\n**Personal Life:**\nEscobar was known for his flamboyant and extravagant lifestyle. He owned numerous properties, including a luxury mansion in Medellín, and was known for his love of expensive cars, jewelry, and women. He was also a devoted family man and was particularly close to his mother, Hermilda.\n\n**Pursuit and Death:**\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, Escobar\'s empire began to crumble under the pressure of law enforcement efforts. The Colombian government, with the support of the United States, launched a series of operations aimed at capturing or killing Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy:**\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and calculating businessman who was able to build a vast and lucrative empire through his innovative and ruthless tactics. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts:**\n\n* Escobar was known for his nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) and was feared and respected by his associates and enemies alike.\n* He was estimated to have amassed a fortune of over $30 billion at the height of his power.\n* Escobar was a skilled politician and was able to manipulate the Colombian government and media to further his interests.\n* He was known for his generosity and philanthropy, particularly in his hometown of Medellín, where he built roads, schools, and other infrastructure.\n* Escobar\'s death was seen as a major victory for law enforcement and marked the beginning of the end of the Medellín Cartel\'s dominance in the cocaine trade.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 10:45:00', '2026-04-05 10:45:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-05 10:45:15', '2026-04-05 10:45:15'),
(1745, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. He grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in crime at a young age, selling stolen cars and smuggling cigarettes.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to build his empire by smuggling cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Colombian underworld, becoming a key player in the Medellín Cartel. His success was fueled by his cunning, ruthlessness, and strategic thinking.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel\'s main business was smuggling cocaine into the United States, where it was sold to distributors and eventually to consumers.\n\nEscobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and violence. He and his associates used intimidation, murder, and bribery to maintain control over the cartel\'s operations and eliminate any potential threats. Escobar was also known for his lavish spending and philanthropy, which earned him a degree of popularity among some Colombians.\n\n**The War on Drugs and the Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the 1980s, the United States and Colombian governments launched a joint effort to dismantle the Medellín Cartel and bring Escobar to justice. The war on drugs was marked by intense violence and bloodshed, with both sides committing atrocities.\n\nThe Colombian government, with the help of the US DEA, launched a series of raids and operations against the cartel, killing many of Escobar\'s top associates and destroying much of the organization\'s infrastructure. Escobar himself became a fugitive, using his vast network of loyal associates and corrupt officials to evade capture.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era for the Medellín Cartel, and the organization\'s power and influence began to wane.\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including innocent civilians, police officers, and rival gang members. However, he is also seen by some as a folk hero and a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the US-backed war on drugs.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, serving as a reminder of the dangers and consequences of the drug trade and the enduring power of organized crime.\n\n**Key Facts and Figures**\n\n* Estimated net worth: $30 billion\n* Estimated number of deaths attributed to the Medellín Cartel: 4,000-6,000\n* Number of years on the run: 16\n* Number of homes and properties owned: over 400\n* Number of cars owned: over 100\n* Favorite car: Mercedes-Benz 600 Pullman\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was a fan of soccer and owned a soccer team, Atlético Nacional.\n* He was known for his love of luxury and extravagance, and owned a private zoo and a collection of rare animals.\n* Escobar was a devout Catholic and often sought to justify his actions as a form of revenge against the Colombian government and the US.\n* He was a skilled politician and strategist, and was able to manipulate public opinion and gain support from some sectors of Colombian society.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 10:50:00', '2026-04-05 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-05 10:50:18', '2026-04-05 10:50:18'),
(1746, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely considered one of the most notorious and successful criminals of all time.\n\n**Early Life:**\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned them. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and behavior.\n\n**Rise to Power:**\nEscobar began his career in crime as a car thief and smuggler. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was then a relatively new and lucrative business. He quickly rose to prominence as a key player in the Medellín cartel, a powerful and ruthless organization that dominated the global cocaine market.\n\n**Medellín Cartel:**\nThe Medellín cartel, led by Escobar, was responsible for smuggling massive amounts of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was built on a combination of factors, including:\n\n1. **Violence and intimidation**: Escobar and his associates used brutal violence to eliminate competitors, law enforcement, and anyone who stood in their way.\n2. **Corruption**: The cartel bribed and corrupted government officials, police officers, and other influential individuals to ensure their operations were protected.\n3. **Sophisticated smuggling networks**: The cartel developed complex networks of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers to move cocaine and profits around the world.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Feats:**\n\n1. **Assassination of politicians and law enforcement**: Escobar ordered the murder of several prominent politicians, judges, and police officers who threatened his operations.\n2. **Bombings and terrorist attacks**: The Medellín cartel carried out numerous bombings and terrorist attacks, including the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people.\n3. **Luxurious lifestyle**: Escobar\'s wealth and influence allowed him to live a life of luxury, with extravagant homes, cars, and parties.\n\n**Downfall and Death:**\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy:**\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was a brutal and ruthless criminal, he was also a charismatic and calculating leader who built a vast and powerful empire. His story has captivated the public imagination, inspiring numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts:**\n\n1. **Wealth**: At the height of his power, Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion.\n2. **Hacienda Napoles**: Escobar\'s luxurious estate, Hacienda Napoles, featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic animals.\n3. **Philanthropy**: Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar was known to have donated to charitable causes and built infrastructure projects in his hometown of Medellín.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy serve as a cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime, corruption, and the destructive power of greed and ambition.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 10:53:00', '2026-04-05 10:53:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-05 10:53:14', '2026-04-05 10:53:14'),
(1747, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a symbol of power, strength, and resilience, dragons have long fascinated human imagination. Here are a few key takeaways from the dragon\'s world that can inspire and motivate you:\n\n* **Courage in the face of adversity**: Dragons are known for their fearlessness, reminding us to stand up to challenges and overcome obstacles with confidence.\n* **Protecting what matters**: Just like a dragon guards its treasure, we should prioritize and safeguard our values, relationships, and passions.\n* **Continuous growth and evolution**: Dragons are often depicted as ever-changing, adapting to their environments and growing stronger with time. We can learn from this by embracing lifelong learning and self-improvement.\n* **Community and connection**: Despite their fearsome reputation, dragons are sometimes shown to have a strong sense of community and loyalty. This highlights the importance of building and nurturing our relationships with others.\n\n#DragonInspiration #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #PersonalGrowth #Resilience #Courage #CommunityFirst #LifelongLearning #InspirationFromMythology #FacebookMotivation #ProfessionalDevelopment #GrowthMindset #PositiveVibesOnly', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 11:18:00', '2026-04-05 11:18:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-05 11:18:16', '2026-04-05 11:18:16'),
(1748, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'When it comes to party wear for men, there are many options to choose from, depending on the type of party, the dress code, and personal style. Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-tailored suit is always a great option for a party. You can choose from a variety of colors, patterns, and fabrics, such as navy, black, gray, or beige.\n2. **Dress Shirts**: A dress shirt with a pair of dress pants or a suit is a classic party wear option. You can choose from a range of colors, patterns, and fabrics, such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n3. **Blazers**: A blazer is a versatile and stylish option for a party. You can pair it with a dress shirt, dress pants, or even a pair of dark jeans.\n4. **Tuxedos**: If you\'re attending a formal party, a tuxedo is a great option. You can choose from a range of styles, including peak lapel, shawl collar, or notch lapel.\n5. **Cocktail Attire**: Cocktail attire is a great option for a more casual party. You can pair a dress shirt with a pair of dark jeans or dress pants and add a blazer or a leather jacket.\n6. **Party Wear Bottoms**: Party wear bottoms, such as dress pants, trousers, or chinos, are a great option to pair with a dress shirt or a t-shirt.\n7. **Leather Jackets**: A leather jacket can add a cool and edgy touch to your party wear outfit. You can pair it with a dress shirt, t-shirt, or a sweater.\n8. **Accessories**: Don\'t forget to add some accessories to your party wear outfit, such as a watch, cufflinks, or a pocket square.\n\n**Trendy Party Wear Options for Men:**\n\n1. **Slim-Fit Suits**: Slim-fit suits are a popular trend in party wear for men. They are tailored to fit closely to the body, creating a sleek and stylish look.\n2. **Patterned Shirts**: Patterned shirts, such as stripes or checks, are a great option for a party. You can pair them with a pair of dark jeans or dress pants.\n3. **Bold Colors**: Bold colors, such as red, blue, or purple, are a great way to add some personality to your party wear outfit.\n4. **Statement Pieces**: Statement pieces, such as a bold watch or a patterned pocket square, can add a touch of personality to your party wear outfit.\n\n**Tips for Choosing the Right Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Consider the Dress Code**: Make sure to consider the dress code for the party before choosing your outfit.\n2. **Know Your Body Type**: Choose an outfit that flatters your body type. For example, if you\'re tall and lean, a slim-fit suit is a great option.\n3. **Be Comfortable**: Choose an outfit that you feel comfortable in. You\'ll be more confident and have more fun if you\'re wearing something that feels good.\n4. **Add Some Personality**: Add some personality to your outfit with accessories, such as a watch, cufflinks, or a pocket square.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 12:40:00', '2026-04-05 12:40:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-04-05 12:40:14', '2026-04-05 12:40:14'),
(1749, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a point collar, spread collar, or wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or cufflinks.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the chest and shoulders.\n5. **Button-front**: Formal shirts usually have a button-front closure.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a point collar and French cuffs.\n2. **Wingtip shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and cufflinks.\n3. **Spread collar shirt**: A formal shirt with a spread collar and a more relaxed fit.\n4. **Slim fit shirt**: A formal shirt with a slim fit through the chest and shoulders.\n5. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt specifically designed to be worn with a tuxedo, typically with a wingtip collar and French cuffs.\n\n**Colors and Patterns:**\n\n1. **White**: A classic color for formal shirts, suitable for business and formal events.\n2. **Light blue**: A popular color for formal shirts, suitable for business and casual events.\n3. **Pastel colors**: Soft pastel colors such as pink, lavender, and peach are suitable for formal events and special occasions.\n4. **Stripes**: Thin stripes are a classic pattern for formal shirts, suitable for business and formal events.\n5. **Checks**: Small checks are a subtle pattern for formal shirts, suitable for business and casual events.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: A luxury brand known for high-quality formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand known for exquisite formal shirts with intricate details.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: A classic American brand known for traditional formal shirts.\n4. **Armani**: A luxury brand known for stylish and modern formal shirts.\n5. **Hugo Boss**: A German brand known for high-quality formal shirts with a focus on style and comfort.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Choose a shirt that fits well**: A well-fitting shirt is essential for a formal look.\n2. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a shirt that is suitable for the occasion, such as a white shirt for a business meeting or a black shirt for a formal event.\n3. **Pay attention to details**: Look for shirts with high-quality details such as cufflinks, buttons, and stitching.\n4. **Iron your shirt**: A well-ironed shirt is essential for a formal look.\n5. **Accessories**: Add a tie, pocket square, and cufflinks to complete your formal look.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 12:56:00', '2026-04-05 12:56:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-04-05 12:56:14', '2026-04-05 12:56:14'),
(1750, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', '**Unlock the Power of Dragon\'s Den: Top 5 Business Lessons**\n\nAs a renowned dragon in the business world, I\'m excited to share with you the most valuable lessons I\'ve learned throughout my journey. Here are the top 5 takeaways:\n\n* **Innovation is key**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new ideas and technologies.\n* **Risk management is crucial**: Weigh your options carefully and make informed decisions to minimize risks.\n* **Networking is essential**: Build strong relationships with fellow entrepreneurs and industry leaders.\n* **Adaptability is vital**: Be prepared to pivot when necessary and stay flexible in an ever-changing market.\n* **Resilience is paramount**: Learn from your failures and use them as opportunities for growth.\n\nJoin the conversation and share your own business lessons learned. #DragonApproved #BusinessLessons #Entrepreneurship #InnovationNation #RiskManagement #NetworkingTips #AdaptOrDie #ResilienceMatters #TrendingNow #FacebookBusiness #DragonDen', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-05 13:03:00', '2026-04-05 13:03:13', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Women_Sandel?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-04-05 13:03:13', '2026-04-05 13:03:13'),
