(1805, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'As a dragon in the business world, I\'d like to share some relatable points with you. Here\'s a post for Facebook:\n\n\"Being a dragon in the corporate world can be challenging, but someone\'s gotta do it. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Breathing fire isn\'t always the answer, but it can be a great way to get a point across\n* Scales are not just for show, they\'re also great for protecting your assets\n* Hoarding treasure is not just about accumulating wealth, it\'s about investing in your future\n* Flying high can be exhilarating, but it\'s also important to stay grounded and focused on your goals\n* Sometimes, you just need to take a step back, relax, and enjoy the view from the top of the mountain\n\n#DragonLife #BusinessTips #Relatable #CorporateWorld #FireBreathing #ScaleUp #TreasureHunter #FlyingHigh #GoalOriented #TrendingNow #DragonSquad #ProfessionalLife\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending hashtags on Facebook, including #TrendingNow, which is a great way to increase visibility and reach a wider audience.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-07 10:35:00', '2026-04-07 10:35:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-07 10:35:16', '2026-04-07 10:35:16'),
(1806, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, criminal, and one of the most infamous figures in the history of organized crime. He was the founder and leader of the Medellín cartel, which became one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was exposed to crime from a young age. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working in the streets, selling fruit and other goods.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started working for a local cocaine smuggler. He quickly rose through the ranks and became a key player in the Colombian cocaine trade. In the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, with an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine supply passing through its hands. The cartel\'s operations were highly organized and sophisticated, with a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers.\n\nEscobar\'s success was due in part to his ruthless tactics, which included murder, intimidation, and bribery. He was known for his ability to corrupt and manipulate government officials, judges, and law enforcement agents, which allowed him to operate with relative impunity.\n\n**The \"King of Cocaine\"**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was known as the \"King of Cocaine.\" He was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the wealthiest men in the world. He lived a lavish lifestyle, with a private zoo, a collection of exotic cars, and a mansion in Medellín.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nHowever, Escobar\'s reign of terror eventually came to an end. In 1991, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and a massive manhunt was launched to capture him.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the world of organized crime, and it had a significant impact on the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also remembered as a folk hero by some, who see him as a symbol of resistance against the government and the establishment.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story continues to fascinate and captivate audiences around the world, and his impact on the world of organized crime remains significant to this day.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his generosity and philanthropy, and he built roads, schools, and hospitals in his hometown of Medellín.\n* He was a fan of soccer and owned a team, the Atlético Nacional, which won several championships during his ownership.\n* Escobar\'s private zoo, Hacienda Nápoles, was home to exotic animals such as hippos, giraffes, and elephants.\n* He was known for his love of luxury cars and had a collection of over 100 vehicles, including a Mercedes-Benz 600 Pullman and a Porsche 911.\n* Escobar\'s grave in Medellín has become a tourist attraction, with many visitors paying their respects to the infamous drug lord.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-07 10:45:00', '2026-04-07 10:45:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-07 10:45:16', '2026-04-07 10:45:16'),
(1807, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. He was a bright and ambitious student, but he dropped out of school in his teenage years to pursue a life of crime.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime by selling stolen cars and motorcycles, and later became involved in the cocaine trade. In the 1970s, he started working for the Medellín Cartel, a powerful drug trafficking organization led by Carlos Lehder. Escobar quickly rose through the ranks and became a key figure in the cartel, earning the nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss).\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and Escobar\'s wealth and influence grew exponentially. He was known for his ruthless tactics, including murder, intimidation, and bribery, which he used to eliminate his enemies and maintain control over the cartel.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The Assassination of Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán, who had vowed to crack down on the Medellín Cartel.\n2. **The Bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people. The bombing was intended to kill a Colombian politician who was on the flight, but he was not on board.\n3. **The Murder of Police Officers**: Escobar was responsible for the murder of hundreds of police officers and government officials who were trying to bring him to justice.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a luxurious private prison, which he had built himself. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was finally tracked down by Colombian police on December 1, 1993. He was shot and killed in a shootout with police in Medellín, Colombia.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal crime lord who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. However, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful empire. His life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n1. **Wealth**: At the height of his power, Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world.\n2. **Hacienda Napoles**: Escobar built a vast and luxurious estate called Hacienda Napoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars.\n3. **Philanthropy**: Despite his notorious crimes, Escobar was known to be a generous philanthropist, and he built roads, schools, and hospitals in poor neighborhoods in Medellín.\n4. **Family**: Escobar was married to María Victoria Henao, and they had two children together. His son, Juan Pablo Escobar, has spoken publicly about his father\'s legacy and has written a book about his experiences growing up as the son of a notorious crime lord.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-07 10:50:00', '2026-04-07 10:50:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-07 10:50:15', '2026-04-07 10:50:15'),
(1808, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. His family was of modest means, and his father was a farmer. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and a lack of education. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working on the streets, selling cigarettes and other small items.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s entry into the world of organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into Colombia. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder and other Colombian traffickers. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him become a key player in the cartel, and he eventually took over as its leader.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and Escobar\'s network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers stretched from Colombia to the United States, Europe, and beyond.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He ordered the killings of thousands of people, including rival gang members, police officers, judges, and politicians. He also orchestrated bombings, kidnappings, and other acts of terrorism. Escobar\'s most notorious crime was the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n\n**Wealth and Excess**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world. He lived a life of excess, with a vast collection of luxury cars, mansions, and other possessions. His Hacienda Nápoles estate, which included a private zoo and a collection of exotic animals, was a symbol of his wealth and power.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and his organization began to crumble. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the country\'s struggles with poverty, inequality, and corruption. Escobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his charisma and ability to connect with ordinary people. He was often referred to as \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) or \"El Señor\" (The Lord).\n* He was a skilled manipulator and used his wealth and influence to bribe and intimidate politicians, police, and other officials.\n* Escobar\'s organization was responsible for the deaths of an estimated 4,000 people, including many innocent civilians.\n* He was a fan of soccer and owned a team called the Atlético Nacional.\n* Escobar\'s Hacienda Nápoles estate has been converted into a theme park and a museum, which attracts thousands of visitors each year.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-07 10:53:00', '2026-04-07 10:53:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-07 10:53:18', '2026-04-07 10:53:18'),
(1809, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Journey**\n\nAs a symbol of power, strength, and resilience, dragons have long fascinated human imagination. Here are a few key takeaways from the dragon\'s perspective:\n\n* **Courage in the face of adversity**: Dragons are known for their fearlessness, a trait that allows them to soar to great heights and overcome even the most daunting challenges.\n* **Adaptability and resilience**: With their ability to thrive in diverse environments, dragons remind us of the importance of being flexible and able to adapt to changing circumstances.\n* **Loyalty and protection**: Dragons are often depicted as fiercely protective of their territories and those they care about, highlighting the value of loyalty and dedication.\n* **Growth and transformation**: As dragons shed their skin and emerge anew, they embody the potential for personal growth and transformation that lies within each of us.\n\n#Trending #DragonEnergy #MotivationMonday #PersonalGrowth #Resilience #Courage #Loyalty #Transformation #Inspiration #FacebookMotivation #BusinessLessons #DragonInspiration #ProfessionalGrowth #SuccessTips', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-07 11:18:00', '2026-04-07 11:18:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-07 11:18:15', '2026-04-07 11:18:15'),
(1810, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:57', 'A pen is a writing instrument used to apply ink to a surface, typically paper, to create written characters, symbols, and designs. It is one of the most common and widely used writing tools in the world.\n\nThere are several types of pens, including:\n\n1. **Ballpoint pen**: This is the most common type of pen, which uses a small metal ball to dispense ink onto the paper.\n2. **Rollerball pen**: This type of pen uses a small metal ball to dispense liquid ink onto the paper, creating a smooth and fluid writing experience.\n3. **Fountain pen**: This type of pen uses a nib to deliver ink onto the paper, and is often considered a more traditional and elegant writing instrument.\n4. **Gel pen**: This type of pen uses a water-based ink that is suspended in a gel-like substance, creating a vibrant and colorful writing experience.\n5. **Fineliner pen**: This type of pen uses a fine tip to create precise lines and details, often used for drawing and illustration.\n\nPens are used for a variety of purposes, including:\n\n1. **Writing**: Pens are used to write letters, notes, and documents.\n2. **Drawing**: Pens are used to create artwork, illustrations, and designs.\n3. **Signing**: Pens are used to sign documents, contracts, and artwork.\n4. **Journaling**: Pens are used to write in journals, diaries, and notebooks.\n\nOverall, pens are an essential tool for communication, creativity, and self-expression.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-07 11:57:00', '2026-04-07 11:57:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 16, '2026-04-07 11:57:18', '2026-04-07 11:57:18'),
(1811, 'Auto Post for instagram at 11:59', 'A pen packet is a small, usually paper or plastic, packet that contains a single pen or a set of pens, often with a clip or a string to attach it to a keychain, lanyard, or other object. \n\nPen packets can be found in various settings, including:\n\n1. **Hotel rooms**: Many hotels provide a pen packet with their logo or branding as a complimentary item for guests.\n2. **Conferences and events**: Pen packets are often given away as promotional items or swag at conferences, trade shows, and other events.\n3. **Office supplies**: Some office supply companies offer pen packets as a convenient way to store and carry pens.\n4. **Travel kits**: Pen packets can be included in travel kits or pouches as a useful item for travelers.\n\nThe contents of a pen packet can vary, but it typically includes:\n\n* A pen or pens (ballpoint, rollerball, or gel)\n* A clip or attachment to secure the pen to a keychain or lanyard\n* Sometimes, additional items like a pencil, highlighter, or notepad\n\nOverall, pen packets are a practical and convenient way to carry a writing instrument, and they can also serve as a promotional item or a small gift.', '[\"instagram\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-07 11:59:00', '2026-04-07 11:59:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen_Packet?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 17, '2026-04-07 11:59:15', '2026-04-07 11:59:15'),
