(1843, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Embracing Your Inner Strength: Lessons from a Dragon**\n\nAs a symbol of power and resilience, dragons remind us of the importance of perseverance and determination. Here are a few key takeaways from these mythical creatures:\n\n* **Courage in the face of adversity**: Dragons are known for their fearlessness, teaching us to stand up for ourselves and face challenges head-on.\n* **Protection and loyalty**: Dragons are often depicted as guardians, highlighting the value of loyalty and dedication to those we care about.\n* **Growth and transformation**: From eggs to fire-breathing adults, dragons undergo significant transformations, reminding us that growth and change are essential parts of life.\n\nLet\'s draw inspiration from these legendary creatures and strive to embody their strengths. Share with us in the comments: what qualities do you admire most about dragons?\n\n#DragonInspiration #InnerStrength #Resilience #Courage #Loyalty #GrowthMindset #TrendingNow #MotivationMonday #FacebookCommunity #ProfessionalDevelopment #PersonalGrowth', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 10:35:00', '2026-04-08 10:35:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-08 10:35:14', '2026-04-08 10:35:14'),
(1844, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely considered one of the most notorious and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. He grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and smuggling at a young age. In the 1970s, Escobar began to build his empire by smuggling cocaine into the United States, using his charisma and business skills to establish himself as a major player in the Colombian cocaine trade.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar co-founded the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and violent drug cartels in the world. The cartel\'s success was based on Escobar\'s ability to produce and distribute large quantities of high-quality cocaine, as well as his ruthless tactics in eliminating competitors and maintaining control over the trade.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his brutal tactics, including murder, intimidation, and bribery. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, and rival gang members. His cartel was also involved in bombings, kidnappings, and other violent acts.\n\n**Wealth and Extravagance**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was one of the richest men in the world, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion. He lived a life of luxury, owning multiple mansions, cars, and planes, and was known for his extravagant spending and love of luxury goods.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, began to crack down on the Medellín Cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and his empire began to crumble. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín, Colombia. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he is widely regarded as a ruthless and violent criminal, he is also remembered as a charismatic and cunning figure who was able to build a vast and powerful empire. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known as \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) or \"Don Pablo\" by his associates and admirers.\n* He was a major sponsor of Colombian football and owned a team called Atlético Nacional.\n* Escobar\'s Hacienda Napoles, a sprawling estate in Puerto Triunfo, Colombia, was a favorite hideout and featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars.\n* Escobar\'s death was seen as a major victory for the Colombian government and the international community, but it also marked the beginning of a period of increased violence and instability in Colombia.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 10:45:00', '2026-04-08 10:45:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-08 10:45:22', '2026-04-08 10:45:22'),
(1845, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, with his family struggling to make ends meet. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working on the streets, selling fruit and cigarettes to support his family.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in the drug trade began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, becoming a key player in the organization. In 1979, Escobar was arrested for cocaine trafficking, but he was released from prison after bribing the judge.\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the Medellín cartel, which was responsible for smuggling an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine into the United States. He built a vast network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers, and his empire grew rapidly. Escobar\'s success was fueled by his ruthless tactics, including murder, intimidation, and bribery.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n2. The bombing of Avianca Flight 203 in 1989, which killed 110 people.\n3. The murder of hundreds of police officers, judges, and politicians who opposed him.\n4. The kidnapping and murder of numerous civilians, including businessmen, politicians, and journalists.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down by Colombian police and US DEA agents.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal leader who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering. However, he was also a charismatic figure who was admired by many in Colombia for his generosity and philanthropy. Escobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar\'s impact on Colombian society and politics cannot be overstated. His reign of terror and violence contributed to a decade of instability and bloodshed in Colombia, and his legacy continues to shape the country\'s politics and economy to this day.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 10:50:00', '2026-04-08 10:50:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-08 10:50:17', '2026-04-08 10:50:17'),
(1846, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious crime organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned them. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began his life of crime, starting with small-time scams and thefts.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was gaining popularity in Colombia. He quickly rose through the ranks, becoming a key figure in the Medellín cartel, led by Carlos Lehder. After Lehder\'s arrest in 1981, Escobar took control of the cartel and expanded its operations, establishing a vast network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers.\n\n**Medellín Cartel and Cocaine Empire**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. He and his associates smuggled massive amounts of cocaine into the United States, using a variety of methods, including planes, boats, and hidden compartments in cars and trucks.\n\nEscobar\'s empire was built on violence, intimidation, and corruption. He bribed or killed anyone who stood in his way, including law enforcement officials, judges, and politicians. His organization was responsible for the deaths of hundreds of people, including rival gang members, police officers, and innocent civilians.\n\n**The \"King of Cocaine\"**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was known as the \"King of Cocaine.\" He was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world. He lived a lavish lifestyle, with a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate, Hacienda Napoles.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, began to crack down on Escobar\'s operation. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped from prison in 1992.\n\nA massive manhunt ensued, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was tracked down and killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy and Impact**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the country\'s struggle against poverty and inequality, and his rise to power is often attributed to the failure of the Colombian government to address these issues.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which dramatizes his life and death. His legacy continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world, serving as a reminder of the dangers of organized crime and the importance of addressing the root causes of poverty and inequality.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 10:53:00', '2026-04-08 10:53:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-08 10:53:17', '2026-04-08 10:53:17'),
(1847, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a possible Facebook post:\n\n\"As a business owner and creator, I\'ve learned a thing or two about what it takes to succeed. Here are some key takeaways:\n\n* **Stay focused**: Keep your eyes on the prize and don\'t get distracted by non-essential tasks.\n* **Be adaptable**: Be willing to pivot when circumstances change or new opportunities arise.\n* **Keep learning**: Continuously update your skills and knowledge to stay ahead of the curve.\n* **Build a strong team**: Surround yourself with talented and dedicated individuals who share your vision.\n* **Take calculated risks**: Don\'t be afraid to take bold action when the potential reward is worth it.\n\nBy following these principles, you can set yourself up for success and achieve your goals. Remember to stay driven, stay motivated, and always keep pushing forward! #Entrepreneurship #BusinessTips #SuccessMindset #ProductivityHacks #LeadershipLessons #TrendingNow #BusinessGrowth #Innovation #MotivationMonday\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, including #TrendingNow to reach a wider audience. The tone is professional and the language is concise and easy to understand.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 11:18:00', '2026-04-08 11:18:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-08 11:18:17', '2026-04-08 11:18:17'),
(1848, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:00', 'Happy Birthday Komal. May your day be filled with love, laughter, and all your favorite things. Wishing you a wonderful year ahead.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 12:00:00', '2026-04-08 12:00:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Happy_Birthday_Komal?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 29, '2026-04-08 12:00:15', '2026-04-08 12:00:15'),
(1849, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Suits**: A classic choice for formal parties, suits can be worn in a variety of colors and patterns, including black, navy, gray, and pinstripe.\n2. **Tuxedos**: Perfect for black-tie events, tuxedos are a stylish and sophisticated option.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A crisp, white dress shirt is a timeless choice for formal parties.\n4. **Dress Pants**: Formal dress pants, such as those made from wool or cotton, can be paired with a dress shirt and blazer for a stylish look.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A blazer can add a touch of sophistication to a dress shirt and jeans or dress pants.\n2. **Dress Shoes**: Dress shoes, such as oxfords or loafers, can elevate a semi-formal outfit.\n3. **Jeans**: Dark wash jeans can be dressed up with a dress shirt and blazer for a semi-formal look.\n4. **Polo Shirts**: A polo shirt can be a stylish and comfortable option for a semi-formal party.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Graphic T-Shirts**: A fun and casual option, graphic t-shirts can be paired with jeans or shorts.\n2. **Hoodies**: A hoodie can be a great option for a casual party, especially in colder weather.\n3. **Sneakers**: Sneakers, such as Converse or Vans, can add a casual touch to an outfit.\n4. **Chinos**: Chinos can be a stylish and comfortable option for a casual party.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Watches**: A watch can add a touch of sophistication to an outfit.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to a dress shirt.\n3. **Pocket Squares**: A pocket square can add a pop of color and texture to an outfit.\n4. **Belt**: A belt can help to define the waist and add a touch of style to an outfit.\n\n**Grooming:**\n\n1. **Hair**: Make sure your hair is well-groomed and styled for the party.\n2. **Beard**: If you have a beard, make sure it is well-groomed and trimmed.\n3. **Nails**: Make sure your nails are clean and well-groomed.\n4. **Fragrance**: Wear a fragrance that is suitable for the party and your personal style.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to be confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Choose an outfit that reflects your personal style and the theme of the party.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 12:40:00', '2026-04-08 12:40:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-04-08 12:40:16', '2026-04-08 12:40:16'),
(1850, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key characteristics and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Characteristics:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a point collar, spread collar, or a wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have cuffs that are buttoned or linked.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the torso and sleeves.\n5. **Button-front**: Formal shirts usually have a button-front closure.\n\n**Common Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a point collar and button cuffs.\n2. **Business shirt**: A formal shirt with a spread collar and button cuffs, often worn for business meetings and presentations.\n3. **Evening shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and cufflinks, often worn for formal events such as black-tie weddings and galas.\n4. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and studs, designed to be worn with a tuxedo.\n\n**Popular Fabrics:**\n\n1. **Cotton**: A popular choice for formal shirts, cotton is breathable, durable, and easy to care for.\n2. **Linen**: A natural fiber that is lightweight, breathable, and perfect for warm weather.\n3. **Silk**: A luxurious fabric that is smooth, lustrous, and ideal for special occasions.\n\n**Tips for Choosing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a shirt that is suitable for the occasion, such as a business meeting or a formal event.\n2. **Think about the color**: White, light blue, and pale pink are classic colors for formal shirts.\n3. **Pay attention to fit**: A well-fitting shirt is essential for a polished, professional look.\n4. **Accessories**: Consider the type of cufflinks, tie, and shoes that will complement your shirt.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: A luxury brand known for its high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand that offers exquisite, bespoke formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: A classic American brand that offers a range of formal shirts with a preppy twist.\n4. **Ted Baker**: A British brand that offers stylish, affordable formal shirts with a touch of personality.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 12:56:00', '2026-04-08 12:56:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-04-08 12:56:16', '2026-04-08 12:56:16'),
(1851, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', 'As a dragon, I understand the importance of staying connected with my community. Here\'s a relatable post for my Facebook audience:\n\n**Morning Motivation from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\n* Waking up in my cave, feeling refreshed and ready to take on the day\n* Breathing fire to get my blood pumping and energize my scales\n* Soaring through the skies, feeling the wind beneath my wings and taking in the breathtaking views\n* Connecting with my fellow dragons, sharing stories and experiences, and learning from one another\n* Embracing my unique abilities and using them to make a positive impact on the world\n\n#DragonsOfFacebook #MorningMotivation #FireBreathingTips #ScaleSquad #DragonSociety #TrendingNow #MotivationMonday #InspirationFromTheSkies #ProfessionalDragonsUnite #FacebookFamousDragons', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-08 13:03:00', '2026-04-08 13:03:12', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Women_Sandel?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-04-08 13:03:12', '2026-04-08 13:03:12'),
