(2001, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Unlocking the Power of Dragon\'s Business**\n\nAs a renowned business leader, I\'m excited to share with you the key aspects of our company\'s success. Here are the highlights:\n\n* **Innovative Solutions**: We provide cutting-edge products and services that cater to the evolving needs of our customers.\n* **Customer-Centric Approach**: Our team is dedicated to delivering exceptional customer experiences, ensuring satisfaction and loyalty.\n* **Strategic Partnerships**: We foster strong collaborations with industry experts to stay ahead of the curve and drive growth.\n* **Continuous Learning**: Our organization is committed to ongoing education and training, enabling us to adapt and innovate in a rapidly changing landscape.\n\nJoin us on this journey and discover how our expertise can help your business thrive. #DragonsBusiness #Innovation #CustomerFirst #PartnershipGoals #ContinuousLearning #BusinessSuccess #Entrepreneurship #Leadership #TrendingNow #FacebookBusiness #DragonLeader', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-13 10:35:00', '2026-04-13 10:35:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-13 10:35:16', '2026-04-13 10:35:16'),
(2002, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and powerful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and motivations.\n\nEscobar began his career in crime at a young age, selling stolen cars and cigarettes on the black market. He eventually turned to cocaine trafficking, which became his primary source of income. In the 1970s, Escobar partnered with other Colombian traffickers to form the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world.\n\n**Medellín Cartel and Cocaine Empire**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, smuggling tons of the drug into the United States, Europe, and other countries. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality, using violence and intimidation to maintain control and eliminate rivals.\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world. He lived a lavish lifestyle, owning luxury homes, cars, and airplanes, and was known for his extravagant spending habits.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and rival gang members. His organization was also linked to numerous bombings, kidnappings, and assassinations.\n\nOne of the most notorious incidents attributed to Escobar was the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people in 1989. Escobar was also suspected of ordering the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a crackdown on the Medellín Cartel. Escobar\'s organization was severely weakened, and many of his top lieutenants were killed or captured.\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to the Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially designed facility, known as the \"Cathedral,\" which he had helped design. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the global cocaine trade, and his legacy continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world.\n\n**Legacy and Cultural Impact**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s life and death have been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries. The Netflix series \"Narcos\" (2015-2017) is a fictionalized account of his life and the rise and fall of the Medellín Cartel.\n\nEscobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was a ruthless and violent criminal, he was also a charismatic leader who was able to build a massive empire and inspire loyalty in his followers. His story serves as a cautionary tale about the dangers of unchecked power and the devastating consequences of the drug trade.\n\nIn Colombia, Escobar\'s legacy is still felt today. Many people in Medellín and other cities continue to view him as a folk hero, despite his brutal methods and the harm he caused. However, others see him as a symbol of the country\'s dark past and a reminder of the need for continued efforts to combat organized crime and promote social justice.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-13 10:45:00', '2026-04-13 10:45:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-13 10:45:16', '2026-04-13 10:45:16'),
(2003, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a lower-middle-class family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned the family. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he quickly became involved in street crime and smuggling.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to build his cocaine empire, initially by smuggling small quantities of the drug into the United States. He quickly expanded his operations, forming alliances with other traffickers and establishing a network of labs, smugglers, and distributors.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nBy the early 1980s, Escobar had become one of the most powerful and feared men in Colombia. He had amassed a vast fortune, estimated to be over $30 billion, and had built a network of loyal associates and enforcers. The Medellín cartel, which Escobar led, dominated the global cocaine trade, controlling an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine market.\n\nEscobar\'s success was due in part to his cunning and ruthlessness. He was known for his willingness to use violence and intimidation to eliminate rivals and law enforcement officials who stood in his way. He also invested heavily in corrupting government officials and law enforcement, often bribing them to turn a blind eye to his activities.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the support of the United States, launched a series of operations aimed at capturing or killing Escobar. The hunt for Escobar became a global manhunt, with law enforcement agencies from around the world working together to track him down.\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, he continued to run his empire from behind bars, using his connections and wealth to maintain control.\n\n**The Final Confrontation**\n\nIn 1992, Escobar escaped from La Catedral, sparking a massive manhunt. The Colombian government, with the support of the United States, launched a series of operations aimed at capturing or killing Escobar.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. The circumstances of his death are still disputed, with some claiming that he was executed by the police, while others believe that he took his own life.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is widely regarded as one of the most successful and notorious criminals in history, and his name has become synonymous with the cocaine trade. However, his actions also had a devastating impact on Colombia and the world, contributing to the rise of violence, corruption, and addiction.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV series, including the hit Netflix show \"Narcos,\" which chronicled his rise and fall. Despite his notoriety, Escobar remains a fascinating and enigmatic figure, a symbol of the darker side of human nature and the corrupting influence of power and wealth.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-13 10:50:00', '2026-04-13 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-13 10:50:18', '2026-04-13 10:50:18'),
(2004, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is often referred to as the \"King of Cocaine\" due to his dominance of the global cocaine trade during the 1980s.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. He grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and violence from a young age. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty, violence, and a lack of opportunities, which would later shape his worldview and drive his ambition to become a wealthy and powerful figure.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to build his reputation as a smuggler and a dealer of contraband goods, including stolen cars and electronics. He quickly expanded his operations to include cocaine, which was becoming increasingly popular in the United States. Escobar\'s ability to deliver large quantities of high-quality cocaine to the US market, combined with his ruthless tactics and strategic alliances, allowed him to rapidly rise to the top of the Colombian cocaine trade.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world. The cartel\'s success was driven by Escobar\'s innovative approaches to production, transportation, and distribution, as well as his willingness to use violence and intimidation to eliminate competitors and maintain control.\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel expanded its operations to include a vast network of cocaine production facilities, laboratories, and distribution channels. The cartel\'s reach extended from Colombia to the United States, Mexico, and other countries in Central and South America, as well as to Europe and Asia.\n\n**Violence and Terrorism**\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was marked by violence and terrorism. He was responsible for numerous bombings, assassinations, and massacres, including the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people, and the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán.\n\nEscobar\'s tactics were designed to intimidate and terrorize his enemies, including rival cartels, government officials, and law enforcement agencies. He was known for his use of \"plata o plomo\" (silver or lead), a tactic in which he would offer his enemies a choice between accepting a bribe (plata) or facing death (plomo).\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, Escobar\'s empire began to crumble under the pressure of international law enforcement efforts and internal conflicts within the cartel. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned, but he continued to run his empire from behind bars.\n\nIn 1992, Escobar escaped from prison and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the history of organized crime and the beginning of a new era in the global war on drugs.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning businessman who was willing to do whatever it took to achieve his goals. At the same time, he is also remembered as a charismatic leader who was able to inspire loyalty and devotion in his followers.\n\nEscobar\'s impact on Colombian society and politics was profound. His rise to power was facilitated by corruption and weakness in the Colombian government, and his downfall was driven by international pressure and the efforts of brave Colombian law enforcement officials.\n\nToday, Escobar\'s legacy continues to fascinate and repel people around the world. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite the controversy surrounding his life and death, Escobar remains a figure of enduring fascination and a reminder of the dangers and complexities of the global war on drugs.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-13 10:53:00', '2026-04-13 10:53:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-13 10:53:16', '2026-04-13 10:53:16'),
(2005, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Key Takeaways for Ambitious Entrepreneurs**\n\nAs a dragon in the business world, I\'ve learned a thing or two about what it takes to succeed. Here are some relatable points to consider:\n\n* **Set clear goals**: Just like a dragon knows its treasure, you should know what you\'re working towards.\n* **Be adaptable**: Markets and trends can shift like the winds, so be prepared to adjust your strategy.\n* **Protect your assets**: Whether it\'s your brand, your team, or your intellectual property, safeguard what\'s yours.\n* **Innovate and evolve**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new technologies and ideas.\n* **Roar with confidence**: Believe in yourself and your vision, and don\'t be afraid to show it.\n\n#Entrepreneurship #BusinessTips #DragonMode #InnovationNation #TrendingNow #SuccessStory #GoalOriented #AdaptAndThrive #BrandProtection #ConfidenceIsKey #FacebookForBusiness', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-13 11:18:00', '2026-04-13 11:18:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-13 11:18:17', '2026-04-13 11:18:17'),
