(2318, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:49', 'Wooden crafts are a popular and creative way to work with wood, creating beautiful and functional items for the home, garden, or as gifts. Here are some types of wooden crafts:\n\n1. **Wood Carving**: Carving wooden figures, ornaments, or decorative items using hand tools or power tools.\n2. **Wood Turning**: Creating symmetrical objects like bowls, vases, or candlesticks using a lathe.\n3. **Wood Burning**: Using a pyrography pen to create designs, patterns, or images on wood.\n4. **Wood Inlay**: Creating intricate designs by inserting small pieces of wood into a larger wooden surface.\n5. **Wood Marquetry**: Creating images or patterns by arranging small pieces of wood into a larger design.\n6. **Woodworking**: Building furniture, cabinets, or other wooden items using various woodworking techniques.\n7. **Intarsia**: Creating detailed images or designs by combining small pieces of wood into a larger wooden surface.\n8. **Scroll Sawing**: Cutting intricate designs or patterns into wood using a scroll saw.\n9. **Pyrography**: Using a heated tool to burn designs or patterns into wood.\n10. **Wood Whittling**: Carving wooden figures or objects using a knife or other hand tool.\n\nSome popular wooden craft projects include:\n\n* Coasters\n* Picture frames\n* Jewelry boxes\n* Wooden signs\n* Candle holders\n* Birdhouses\n* Custom furniture\n* Wooden toys\n\nTo get started with wooden crafts, you\'ll need some basic tools and materials, such as:\n\n* Wood (various types and sizes)\n* Hand tools (e.g., chisels, gouges, mallet)\n* Power tools (e.g., drill press, sanders, lathe)\n* Safety equipment (e.g., gloves, safety glasses)\n* Adhesives and finishes (e.g., glue, varnish, stain)\n\nRemember to always follow safety guidelines and use proper techniques when working with wood and power tools.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-21 17:49:00', '2026-04-21 17:49:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/wood_spoon?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 10, '2026-04-21 17:49:16', '2026-04-21 17:49:16'),
(2319, 'Auto Post for facebook at 18:07', 'A flower pot is a container used to hold soil and plants, typically made of materials such as ceramic, clay, plastic, or wood. Flower pots come in a wide range of shapes, sizes, and designs, and can be used to add a decorative touch to indoor and outdoor spaces.\n\nSome common types of flower pots include:\n\n1. Terracotta pots: Made from natural clay, these pots are breathable and allow for good drainage.\n2. Ceramic pots: Often glazed and decorated, these pots can be more decorative than functional.\n3. Plastic pots: Lightweight and inexpensive, these pots are often used for mass-produced plants.\n4. Wooden pots: Made from natural wood, these pots can add a rustic touch to outdoor spaces.\n5. Self-watering pots: These pots have a built-in water reservoir that allows plants to draw water as needed.\n\nFlower pots can be used to plant a variety of flowers, herbs, and other plants, and can be placed on patios, decks, balconies, or indoors. They can also be used to create beautiful arrangements and displays, such as:\n\n* Hanging baskets\n* Window boxes\n* Planters\n* Topiaries\n\nOverall, flower pots are a great way to add some greenery to your space and can be a fun and creative way to express your personal style.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-21 18:07:00', '2026-04-21 18:07:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Flower_pot?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 33, '2026-04-21 18:07:19', '2026-04-21 18:07:19'),
(2320, 'Auto Post for facebook at 18:26', 'Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday are the weekdays. Saturday and Sunday are the weekend days. \n\nSo, the weekdays are: \n1. Monday\n2. Tuesday\n3. Wednesday\n4. Thursday\n5. Friday', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-21 18:26:00', '2026-04-21 18:26:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Week_days_post-Good_Morning_Like_(Monday%2CTuesday%2CWednesday%2CThursday%2CFriday%2CSaturday%2CSunday).?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 34, '2026-04-21 18:26:18', '2026-04-21 18:26:18'),
