(2323, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned to harness my inner strength and passion to achieve greatness. Here are a few key takeaways that can help you do the same:\n\n* **Set ambitious goals**: Don\'t be afraid to dream big and aim high. Whether it\'s conquering a new market or launching a innovative product, remember that the sky\'s the limit.\n* **Stay focused and determined**: Obstacles will arise, but it\'s how you respond that matters. Keep your eyes on the prize and push forward with unwavering dedication.\n* **Cultivate a strong sense of community**: Surround yourself with like-minded individuals who share your vision and values. Together, you can achieve far more than you could alone.\n* **Continuously learn and adapt**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new technologies, trends, and best practices. This will help you stay competitive and thrive in an ever-changing landscape.\n\n#DragonInspiration #BusinessLessons #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #SuccessTips #Entrepreneurship #Innovation #Leadership #CommunityFirst #LifelongLearning #ProfessionalGrowth #FacebookBusiness #BusinessTips #Inspiration', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 10:35:00', '2026-04-22 10:35:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-04-22 10:35:15', '2026-04-22 10:35:15'),
(2324, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a lower-middle-class family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned the family. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was exposed to the world of crime from a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a teenager, smuggling cigarettes and other contraband. He later became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia during the 1970s. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthless tactics helped him quickly rise through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, which he founded in the late 1970s.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine market, and Escobar\'s wealth and influence grew exponentially. He was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included luxury homes, private jets, and a collection of exotic animals.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by violence and terror. He ordered the murders of hundreds of people, including politicians, police officers, and rival gang members. He also orchestrated bombings and other attacks on civilians, including a 1989 bombing of an Avianca Airlines plane that killed 110 people.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. He was finally tracked down on December 1, 1993, in Medellín, Colombia, and was killed in a shootout with Colombian police.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who wreaked havoc on Colombia and the world. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the country\'s struggle with poverty, inequality, and corruption. His life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power.\n* He was known for his love of soccer and even built a soccer field in his prison cell while awaiting trial.\n* Escobar\'s Medellín Cartel was responsible for the deaths of an estimated 4,000 people.\n* He was a skilled politician and was elected to the Colombian Congress in 1982.\n* Escobar\'s death was celebrated by many Colombians, who saw him as a symbol of the country\'s problems with violence and corruption.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 10:45:00', '2026-04-22 10:45:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-22 10:45:20', '2026-04-22 10:45:20'),
(2325, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, narco-terrorist, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely considered one of the most infamous and successful cocaine traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor household and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would shape his future actions.\n\nEscobar began his criminal career in the 1970s, smuggling cigarettes and marijuana. He quickly rose to prominence in the Colombian underworld, earning the respect and fear of his peers. In the late 1970s, he co-founded the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, smuggling hundreds of tons of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was built on a combination of factors, including:\n\n1. **Violence and intimidation**: Escobar and his associates used brutal violence to maintain control and eliminate competitors.\n2. **Corruption**: The cartel bribed and corrupted government officials, police, and military personnel to turn a blind eye to their activities.\n3. **Innovative smuggling methods**: The cartel developed sophisticated smuggling techniques, including the use of submarines, airplanes, and hidden compartments in vehicles.\n\n**Personal Life and Excesses**\n\nEscobar\'s personal life was marked by excess and extravagance. He:\n\n1. **Built a lavish estate**: Escobar constructed a grand mansion, known as Hacienda Nápoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic animals.\n2. **Collected rare cars and planes**: He owned a fleet of luxury vehicles, including a Learjet and a collection of rare sports cars.\n3. **Invested in real estate**: Escobar purchased numerous properties, including apartments, houses, and commercial buildings, in Colombia and abroad.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The pressure on the cartel increased, and internal conflicts weakened the organization.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the global cocaine trade, and the Medellín cartel\'s power began to decline.\n\n**Legacy and Impact**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted:\n\n1. **Narco-terrorism**: Escobar\'s use of violence and intimidation tactics inspired a new generation of narco-terrorists.\n2. **Global cocaine trade**: The Medellín cartel\'s success helped establish the global cocaine trade, which continues to thrive today.\n3. **Colombian politics and economy**: Escobar\'s influence extended into Colombian politics and economy, with many politicians and business leaders accused of ties to the cartel.\n4. **Popular culture**: Escobar\'s life and legacy have been immortalized in numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s story is a cautionary tale about the dangers of unchecked power, corruption, and the devastating consequences of the global cocaine trade.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 10:50:00', '2026-04-22 10:50:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-22 10:50:17', '2026-04-22 10:50:17'),
(2326, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the leader of the Medellín cartel, a notorious crime organization that dominated the global cocaine trade in the 1980s. He is widely considered one of the most infamous and powerful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life and Career**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was drawn to crime at a young age. He began his career as a car thief and a smuggler, but soon turned to cocaine trafficking, which would become his main source of income.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar co-founded the Medellín cartel with his partners, including Carlos Lehder and Gustavo Gaviria. The cartel quickly gained control of the Colombian cocaine trade, and Escobar became its leader. He used his charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness to build a vast network of cocaine producers, smugglers, and distributors.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s success was fueled by his ability to bribe and intimidate government officials, law enforcement, and rival cartels. He also invested heavily in real estate, buying properties and businesses to launder his profits. By the mid-1980s, Escobar had become one of the richest men in Colombia, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He ordered the assassination of politicians, judges, and police officers who opposed him, as well as rival cartel members and innocent civilians. He was responsible for the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people, and the assassination of presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, which he had designed himself. However, he escaped in 1992 and went into hiding. The Colombian government, with the help of the US DEA, launched a massive manhunt for Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal leader who was responsible for thousands of deaths and the destruction of entire communities. However, he was also a charismatic and cunning entrepreneur who built a vast empire and became a folk hero to some in Colombia. His story has been immortalized in films, books, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a mansion with a private airport.\n* He was a prolific builder and invested in many infrastructure projects, including roads, bridges, and housing developments.\n* Escobar was a devout Catholic and built a church in his hometown of Rionegro.\n* He was a skilled politician and was elected to the Colombian Congress in 1982.\n* Escobar\'s death was celebrated by many in Colombia, but his legacy continues to be felt, with many still glorifying him as a hero and a symbol of resistance against the government.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 10:53:00', '2026-04-22 10:53:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-04-22 10:53:19', '2026-04-22 10:53:19'),
(2327, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Unlocking the Fire Within: 5 Key Takeaways for Entrepreneurs**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about passion, perseverance, and success. Here are some relatable points to consider:\n\n* **Set your goals ablaze**: Don\'t be afraid to dream big and aim high. Your goals should be ambitious and inspiring, just like a dragon\'s fiery breath.\n* **Hoarding knowledge is key**: Continuously learn and improve your skills to stay ahead of the competition. A dragon\'s treasure hoard is not just gold and jewels, but also knowledge and wisdom.\n* **Breathing fire into your passion**: Pursue your passions with relentless energy and enthusiasm. When you\'re doing something you love, it\'s like breathing fire - it comes naturally and ignites your inner spark.\n* **Scales of resilience**: Develop a thick skin and learn to bounce back from failures and setbacks. A dragon\'s scales protect it from harm, and you should cultivate a similar resilience to overcome obstacles.\n* **Soaring to new heights**: Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things. A dragon\'s wings take it to incredible heights, and you should strive to reach new heights in your personal and professional life.\n\n#DragonInspiration #EntrepreneurMindset #MotivationMonday #BusinessTips #SuccessStrategies #TrendingNow #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalDevelopment #GoalSetting #ResilienceMatters #PassionPursuit #KnowledgeIsPower #InnovationNation', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 11:18:00', '2026-04-22 11:18:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-04-22 11:18:18', '2026-04-22 11:18:18'),
(2328, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:00', 'Happy Birthday Komal. May this special day be filled with love, laughter, and all your favorite things. Wishing you a year ahead that\'s bright, beautiful, and beyond your wildest dreams.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 12:00:00', '2026-04-22 12:00:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Happy_Birthday_Komal?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 29, '2026-04-22 12:00:22', '2026-04-22 12:00:22'),
(2329, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'When it comes to party wear for men, there are various styles and options to choose from, depending on the occasion and personal taste. Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-fitted suit is a classic choice for formal parties. You can opt for a black, navy, or gray suit, paired with a crisp white shirt and a tie.\n2. **Blazers**: A blazer can add a touch of elegance to any outfit. You can wear it with a dress shirt, trousers, and dress shoes for a stylish look.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A dress shirt with a unique design or pattern can be a great party wear option. You can pair it with dark-washed jeans or trousers and dress shoes.\n4. **Tuxedos**: A tuxedo is a must-have for black-tie events. It\'s a classic and sophisticated choice that\'s sure to make you stand out.\n5. **Cocktail Attire**: For a more casual party, you can opt for a cocktail attire, which includes a dress shirt, dark-washed jeans, and dress shoes.\n6. **Leather Jackets**: A leather jacket can add an edgy touch to any outfit. You can wear it with a dress shirt, trousers, and boots for a stylish look.\n7. **Party Shirts**: Party shirts with unique designs or patterns can be a great way to add some personality to your outfit. You can pair them with dark-washed jeans or trousers and dress shoes.\n\n**Accessories**:\n\n1. **Ties**: A tie can add a touch of elegance to any outfit. You can opt for a classic tie or a bow tie, depending on the occasion.\n2. **Pocket Squares**: A pocket square can add a pop of color to your outfit. You can choose a plain or patterned pocket square, depending on your taste.\n3. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks can add a touch of sophistication to your outfit. You can opt for classic or novelty cufflinks, depending on the occasion.\n4. **Watches**: A watch can be a great accessory for any party wear outfit. You can opt for a classic leather strap or a metallic strap, depending on your taste.\n5. **Shoes**: Dress shoes, boots, or loafers can complete any party wear outfit. Make sure to choose shoes that are comfortable and stylish.\n\n**Tips**:\n\n1. **Dress according to the occasion**: Make sure to dress according to the occasion and the dress code specified.\n2. **Be confident**: Confidence is key to pulling off any outfit. Own your look and have fun.\n3. **Pay attention to fit**: Make sure your clothes fit well and are not too tight or too loose.\n4. **Add a personal touch**: Add a personal touch to your outfit with accessories or a unique piece of clothing.\n\nRemember, party wear for men is all about expressing your personal style and having fun. Experiment with different looks and find what works best for you.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 12:40:00', '2026-04-22 12:40:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-04-22 12:40:20', '2026-04-22 12:40:20'),
(2330, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, or special occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a point collar or a spread collar, which is a classic and timeless choice.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or barrel cuffs, which are more formal than button cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality cotton, linen, or silk fabrics.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit snugly, with a fitted silhouette and a slim collar.\n5. **Button-front**: Formal shirts usually have a button-front closure, with a placket (a strip of fabric that covers the buttons) or a fly-front (a hidden button closure).\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic dress shirt with a point collar and French cuffs, often worn with a suit and tie.\n2. **Business shirt**: A more relaxed version of the dress shirt, with a spread collar and barrel cuffs, suitable for business casual events.\n3. **Wingtip shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and French cuffs, often worn with a tuxedo or dinner jacket.\n4. **Cutaway shirt**: A formal shirt with a cutaway collar and French cuffs, often worn with a morning coat or a formal suit.\n\n**Colors and Patterns:**\n\n1. **White**: A classic choice for formal shirts, white is a timeless and versatile option.\n2. **Light blue**: A light blue shirt is a popular choice for business and formal events.\n3. **Pastel colors**: Soft pastel colors, such as pale pink or baby blue, can add a touch of elegance to a formal outfit.\n4. **Stripes and checks**: Subtle stripes or checks can add texture and interest to a formal shirt.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: A British brand known for its high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand that offers exquisite, handmade formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: An American brand that offers classic, timeless formal shirts.\n4. **Ted Baker**: A British brand that offers stylish, modern formal shirts with a twist.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Choose a shirt that fits well**: A well-fitting shirt is essential for a polished, formal look.\n2. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a shirt that is suitable for the occasion, taking into account the dress code and the level of formality.\n3. **Pay attention to details**: Details such as cuff links, collar stays, and a well-pressed shirt can make a big difference in the overall look.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-22 12:56:00', '2026-04-22 12:56:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-04-22 12:56:21', '2026-04-22 12:56:21');
