(2446, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:33', 'Football is a popular sport played by two teams of 11 players using a round ball with the objective of scoring more goals than the opposing team by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent\'s goal. It is also known as soccer in some countries, particularly in the United States and Canada, to distinguish it from other sports with similar names, such as American football.\n\nHere are some key aspects of football:\n\n1. **Objective**: The objective of football is to score more goals than the opposing team by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent\'s goal.\n2. **Players**: Each team has 11 players on the field, including a goalkeeper.\n3. **Gameplay**: Players can use any part of their body except their hands and arms to control and move the ball. Only the goalkeeper is allowed to use their hands and arms to touch the ball.\n4. **Scoring**: A goal is scored when the ball passes completely over the goal line between the goal posts and under the crossbar.\n5. **Game duration**: A standard football game is divided into two 45-minute halves, with a 15-minute halftime break in between.\n6. **Rules**: The game is governed by a set of rules, including offside, fouls, and free kicks.\n\nSome popular football competitions include:\n\n1. **FIFA World Cup**: The most widely viewed and followed sporting event in the world, held every four years.\n2. **UEFA Champions League**: An annual club competition featuring top teams from Europe.\n3. **English Premier League**: A professional league in England, considered one of the most competitive and popular leagues in the world.\n4. **La Liga**: A professional league in Spain, featuring top teams like Barcelona and Real Madrid.\n\nFootball is a global sport with a massive following, and its popularity continues to grow with each passing year.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-25 16:33:00', '2026-04-25 16:33:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/bicycle_kick_hitting_the_top_right_corner?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 53, '2026-04-25 16:33:23', '2026-04-25 16:33:23'),
(2447, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:42', 'The R1 bike. You\'re likely referring to the Yamaha YZF-R1, a legendary sports bike produced by Yamaha. Here are some key features and facts about the R1:\n\n**Overview**\nThe Yamaha YZF-R1 is a high-performance sports bike that was first introduced in 1998. It\'s known for its powerful engine, agile handling, and sleek design.\n\n**Key Features**\n\n* **Engine**: 998cc, liquid-cooled, 4-stroke, DOHC, 16-valve, in-line 4-cylinder engine\n* **Power**: 200 horsepower (147.9 kW) @ 13,500 rpm\n* **Torque**: 82.6 lb-ft (112 Nm) @ 11,500 rpm\n* **Transmission**: 6-speed, multi-plate clutch\n* **Brakes**: Dual 320mm discs with 4-piston calipers (front), 220mm disc with 2-piston caliper (rear)\n* **Suspension**: 43mm inverted fork (front), monoshock with linkage (rear)\n* **Weight**: 439 pounds (199 kg) wet\n\n**Riding Experience**\nThe R1 is designed for experienced riders who crave high-performance and agility. It features a compact, aerodynamic body and a low-slung seat, which provides an aggressive riding position. The bike\'s powerful engine and responsive handling make it a thrill to ride on twisty roads or track days.\n\n**Models and Updates**\nOver the years, Yamaha has released several updates and special editions of the R1, including:\n\n* R1 (1998-2002): The original model\n* R1 (2002-2006): Updated with a new engine and chassis\n* R1 (2007-2008): Featured a new, more compact engine and improved suspension\n* R1 (2009-2014): Introduced a new, more aerodynamic body and updated electronics\n* R1 (2015-present): Features a new, crossplane crankshaft engine and advanced electronics, including traction control and ABS\n\n**Conclusion**\nThe Yamaha YZF-R1 is a high-performance sports bike that\'s designed for experienced riders who demand the best. With its powerful engine, agile handling, and sleek design, it\'s a legendary bike that\'s sure to provide an exhilarating riding experience.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-25 16:42:00', '2026-04-25 16:42:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/r1_bike?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 54, '2026-04-25 16:42:23', '2026-04-25 16:42:23'),
(2448, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:30', 'Iron Man is a iconic superhero from the Marvel Comics universe. Created by Stan Lee, Larry Lieber, and Don Heck, Iron Man first appeared in comic books in 1963.\n\n**Origin Story:**\nTony Stark, a billionaire inventor and industrialist, is kidnapped by a group of terrorists who demand that he build a powerful missile system for them. Instead, Tony uses his genius-level intellect to create a suit of armor, which he uses to escape from his captors. He later refines the suit and becomes the superhero known as Iron Man.\n\n**Powers and Abilities:**\nIron Man\'s suit is a advanced technological marvel, providing him with a range of powers and abilities, including:\n\n1. **Superhuman Strength**: The suit\'s advanced robotics and actuators give Tony enhanced strength, allowing him to lift and throw objects that would be impossible for a human to handle.\n2. **Flight**: The suit\'s repulsor technology enables Iron Man to fly, making him a highly mobile and versatile hero.\n3. **Energy Projection**: The suit\'s repulsor technology also allows Iron Man to project energy blasts, which he can use to attack his enemies or blast through obstacles.\n4. **Advanced Sensors**: The suit\'s advanced sensors and scanning technology give Tony real-time feedback on his surroundings, allowing him to detect and respond to threats more effectively.\n5. **Artificial Intelligence**: The suit\'s AI system, JARVIS (later replaced by FRIDAY), provides Tony with strategic support, tactical analysis, and control over the suit\'s systems.\n\n**Movie Franchise:**\nThe Iron Man movie franchise, starring Robert Downey Jr. as Tony Stark/Iron Man, has been a massive success, with three solo films:\n\n1. **Iron Man (2008)**\n2. **Iron Man 2 (2010)**\n3. **Iron Man 3 (2013)**\n\nThe character has also appeared in several other Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU) movies, including:\n\n1. **The Avengers (2012)**\n2. **Avengers: Age of Ultron (2015)**\n3. **Captain America: Civil War (2016)**\n4. **Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017)**\n5. **Avengers: Infinity War (2018)**\n6. **Avengers: Endgame (2019)**\n\n**Legacy:**\nIron Man has become an iconic character in popular culture, inspiring countless fans around the world with his intelligence, wit, and courage. The character\'s legacy continues to evolve, with new comic book series, animated TV shows, and video games being released regularly.\n\nWhat aspect of Iron Man would you like to know more about? The comics, the movies, or something else?', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-25 17:30:00', '2026-04-25 17:30:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/iron_man?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 55, '2026-04-25 17:30:16', '2026-04-25 17:30:16'),
