(2514, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:33', 'Football, also known as soccer in some countries, is a popular team sport played between two teams of 11 players using a round ball with the objective of scoring more goals than the opposing team by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent\'s goal.\n\nHere are some key aspects of football:\n\n1. **Objective**: The main objective of football is to score more goals than the opposing team within the 90-minute game duration.\n2. **Players**: Each team has 11 players, including a goalkeeper, defenders, midfielders, and forwards.\n3. **Equipment**: The game is played with a round ball, and players can use any part of their body except their hands and arms to control and move the ball.\n4. **Gameplay**: The game starts with a kickoff, and players can use various techniques such as dribbling, passing, and shooting to move the ball and score goals.\n5. **Scoring**: A goal is scored when the ball passes the goal line between the goal posts and under the crossbar.\n6. **Fouls**: If a player commits a foul, such as tripping or pushing an opponent, the opposing team is awarded a free kick or penalty kick.\n7. **Tactics**: Teams employ various tactics, such as formations, strategies, and player positions, to outmaneuver their opponents and score goals.\n\nSome popular football competitions include:\n\n1. **FIFA World Cup**: The most widely viewed and followed sporting event in the world, held every four years.\n2. **UEFA Champions League**: An annual club competition featuring top European teams.\n3. **English Premier League**: A professional league in England, considered one of the most competitive and popular leagues in the world.\n4. **La Liga**: A professional league in Spain, known for its technical and attacking style of play.\n5. **Copa America**: A tournament featuring national teams from South America.\n\nFootball has a massive global following, with millions of fans attending matches, watching games on TV, and playing the sport at various levels, from amateur to professional.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-27 16:33:00', '2026-04-27 16:33:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/bicycle_kick_hitting_the_top_right_corner?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 53, '2026-04-27 16:33:19', '2026-04-27 16:33:19'),
(2515, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:42', 'The R1 bike. You\'re likely referring to the Yamaha YZF-R1, a high-performance sport bike manufactured by Yamaha Motor Company. Here are some key features and specs:\n\n**Overview**\nThe Yamaha YZF-R1 is a flagship sport bike that has been in production since 1998. It\'s known for its exceptional handling, powerful engine, and aerodynamic design.\n\n**Key Features**\n\n1. **Engine**: 998cc, liquid-cooled, 4-stroke, DOHC, 16-valve, inline-four cylinder engine.\n2. **Power**: 200 horsepower (147.9 kW) at 13,500 rpm.\n3. **Torque**: 82.6 lb-ft (112 Nm) at 11,500 rpm.\n4. **Transmission**: 6-speed, constant mesh, with a multi-plate wet clutch.\n5. **Brakes**: Dual 320mm hydraulic disc brakes with 4-piston calipers (front), and a single 220mm hydraulic disc brake with a 2-piston caliper (rear).\n6. **Suspension**: 43mm inverted fork (front), and a monoshock with a piggyback reservoir (rear).\n7. **Weight**: 443 pounds (201 kg) wet weight.\n\n**Variants**\nOver the years, Yamaha has released several variants of the R1, including:\n\n1. **R1M**: A limited-edition, high-performance version with advanced electronics and suspension.\n2. **R1S**: A more affordable, entry-level version with a lower price point.\n3. **R1 60th Anniversary**: A special edition model celebrating Yamaha\'s 60th anniversary.\n\n**Riding Experience**\nThe Yamaha R1 is known for its exceptional handling, stability, and acceleration. It\'s a popular choice among track enthusiasts and experienced riders who demand a high level of performance from their bike.\n\nKeep in mind that the R1 is a high-performance bike, and it\'s not suitable for beginners. If you\'re new to motorcycling, it\'s essential to consider your skill level and experience before choosing a bike like the R1.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-27 16:42:00', '2026-04-27 16:42:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/r1_bike?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 54, '2026-04-27 16:42:22', '2026-04-27 16:42:22'),
(2516, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:30', 'Iron Man is a fictional superhero appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The character was created by writer and editor Stan Lee, and designed by artists Don Heck and Jack Kirby.\n\n**Origin Story:**\nTony Stark, a billionaire inventor and industrialist, is the alter ego of Iron Man. After being kidnapped and held captive, Stark is forced to create a powerful suit of armor to escape. He later perfects the design and uses it to fight crime and protect the world as the superhero Iron Man.\n\n**Powers and Abilities:**\nIron Man\'s powers come from his advanced suit of armor, which provides:\n\n1. **Superhuman Strength**: The suit amplifies Stark\'s physical strength, allowing him to lift and throw objects that would be impossible for a human.\n2. **Flight**: The suit is equipped with repulsor technology, which allows Iron Man to fly.\n3. **Energy Projection**: The suit can project energy blasts from its hands, known as repulsor rays.\n4. **Advanced Sensors**: The suit has advanced sensors and scanners, which provide Iron Man with real-time data and enhance his perception.\n5. **Artificial Intelligence**: The suit\'s AI, known as JARVIS (later replaced by FRIDAY), assists Iron Man in various tasks and provides strategic support.\n\n**Movie Franchise:**\nThe Iron Man character has been featured in several movies, including:\n\n1. **Iron Man (2008)**: The first film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), starring Robert Downey Jr. as Tony Stark/Iron Man.\n2. **Iron Man 2 (2010)**: The sequel to the first film, with Downey Jr. reprising his role.\n3. **Iron Man 3 (2013)**: The third installment in the Iron Man series, with Downey Jr. again starring as Tony Stark/Iron Man.\n4. **The Avengers (2012)**: Iron Man joins the Avengers team, consisting of other Marvel superheroes, to save the world from an alien invasion.\n5. **Avengers: Age of Ultron (2015)**: Iron Man and the Avengers face off against the artificial intelligence Ultron.\n6. **Captain America: Civil War (2016)**: Iron Man and Captain America clash over the Sokovia Accords, leading to a rift in the Avengers team.\n7. **Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017)**: Iron Man appears as a mentor to Peter Parker/Spider-Man.\n8. **Avengers: Infinity War (2018)**: Iron Man plays a key role in the battle against Thanos.\n9. **Avengers: Endgame (2019)**: Iron Man makes the ultimate sacrifice to save the world from Thanos.\n\n**Impact and Legacy:**\nIron Man has become an iconic character in popular culture, inspiring numerous adaptations, including video games, TV shows, and merchandise. The character\'s legacy extends beyond the Marvel Cinematic Universe, with Tony Stark\'s entrepreneurial spirit and innovative genius influencing real-world technological advancements.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-04-27 17:30:00', '2026-04-27 17:30:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/iron_man?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 55, '2026-04-27 17:30:20', '2026-04-27 17:30:20'),
