(2636, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious cartels in the world. He is widely considered to be one of the most infamous and successful criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, and his father, Abel. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was often involved in street fights and petty crime.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to build his career as a cocaine smuggler. He started by smuggling small quantities of cocaine from Colombia to the United States, but soon expanded his operations to become one of the largest and most successful cocaine traffickers in the world. He built a vast network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers, and became known for his ruthless tactics and his ability to bribe and intimidate law enforcement officials.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín Cartel, which quickly became one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world. The cartel\'s main business was cocaine trafficking, but it also engaged in other illicit activities, such as extortion, kidnapping, and murder. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and its willingness to use violence to achieve its goals.\n\n**Notorious Acts**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious acts, including:\n\n* The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989\n* The bombing of Avianca Flight 203 in 1989, which killed 110 people\n* The murder of hundreds of police officers, judges, and politicians who opposed him\n* The establishment of a network of cocaine smuggling routes and distribution networks in the United States and other countries\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, began to crack down on the Medellín Cartel. Escobar\'s organization was weakened by internal conflicts and by the loss of key leaders, and he was eventually forced to go into hiding. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. On the one hand, he was a ruthless and brutal criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. On the other hand, he was a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization, and who became a folk hero to many in Colombia and other countries. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a lavish mansion.\n* He was a skilled businessman and investor, and he invested in a number of legitimate businesses, including real estate and construction companies.\n* Escobar was a devoted family man, and he was particularly close to his mother and his daughter, Manuela.\n* He was a prolific donor to charity, and he gave millions of dollars to poor communities in Colombia and other countries.\n* Escobar\'s net worth at the time of his death was estimated to be around $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 10:45:00', '2026-05-01 10:45:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-01 10:45:23', '2026-05-01 10:45:23'),
(2637, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious organized crime groups in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and dropped out of school in the seventh grade. Escobar began his career in crime at a young age, selling stolen cars and engaging in other petty crimes.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, becoming one of its top leaders. Escobar\'s success was due in part to his ruthless tactics, including the use of violence and intimidation to eliminate competitors and maintain control over the cartel\'s operations.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and profitable organized crime groups in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and Escobar\'s wealth and influence grew exponentially. He was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning numerous properties, cars, and other luxury items.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, and civilians. Escobar also ordered the assassination of several high-profile targets, including Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility, known as La Catedral. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt ensued, with Colombian and American authorities working together to track down Escobar.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was responsible for unimaginable violence and suffering, he also became a folk hero of sorts in Colombia, particularly among the poor and marginalized communities. His rags-to-riches story and his ability to outsmart and outmaneuver his enemies captivated many people, and his legend has endured long after his death.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and career have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite the controversy surrounding his life and legacy, Pablo Escobar remains one of the most fascinating and infamous figures of the 20th century.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 10:50:00', '2026-05-01 10:50:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-01 10:50:21', '2026-05-01 10:50:21'),
(2638, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he quickly became involved in petty crime to support his family.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s entry into the world of organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started working as a smuggler and a thief. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by his mentor, Carlos Lehder. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness made him a natural leader, and he soon became one of the most powerful figures in the cartel.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most dominant and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world. The cartel\'s main product was cocaine, which was smuggled into the United States and other countries through a network of routes and distributors. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and violence, and he was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including rival gang members, police officers, and innocent civilians.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nSome of Escobar\'s most notorious crimes include:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: Escobar ordered the murder of Galán, who was a strong opponent of the Medellín cartel, in 1989.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: Escobar\'s organization planted a bomb on a commercial airliner, which exploded mid-air, killing 110 people, in 1989.\n3. **The massacre of the Colombian police**: Escobar\'s men killed over 200 police officers in a series of attacks in the late 1980s and early 1990s.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nEscobar\'s reign of terror eventually came to an end in 1993, when he was killed in a shootout with Colombian police. The police had been tracking Escobar for months, and they finally cornered him in a rooftop in Medellín. Escobar was shot and killed, and his body was later identified through fingerprint analysis.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and brutal leader who was responsible for thousands of deaths and untold suffering. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the failures of the war on drugs and the corrupting influence of power and wealth. Escobar\'s life and death have been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n1. **Escobar\'s wealth**: At the height of his power, Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be over $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world.\n2. **Escobar\'s private zoo**: Escobar owned a private zoo, which included exotic animals such as lions, tigers, and elephants.\n3. **Escobar\'s philanthropy**: Despite his brutal reputation, Escobar was known to be a generous philanthropist, and he built roads, schools, and hospitals in his hometown of Medellín.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy are a testament to the dangers of the drug trade and the corrupting influence of power and wealth. His story serves as a reminder of the importance of addressing the root causes of poverty and inequality, and of working towards a more just and equitable society.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 10:53:00', '2026-05-01 10:53:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-01 10:53:16', '2026-05-01 10:53:16'),
(2639, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about passion, perseverance, and leadership. Here are some key takeaways:\n\n* **Courage is key**: Don\'t be afraid to take risks and face your fears head-on.\n* **Resilience is essential**: Life can be unpredictable, but it\'s how you respond to challenges that defines you.\n* **Passion drives success**: When you\'re doing something you love, you\'re more likely to put in the effort required to achieve greatness.\n* **Leadership is about empowerment**: As a dragon, I don\'t just lead by brute force - I inspire and empower those around me to reach their full potential.\n\n#DragonsDen #LeadershipLessons #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #BusinessTips #ProfessionalDevelopment #FacebookCommunity #InspirationalQuotes #SuccessStories #EntrepreneurMindset #DragonFire', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 11:18:00', '2026-05-01 11:18:14', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-01 11:18:14', '2026-05-01 11:18:14'),
(2640, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:39', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business/creator on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing my true nature and living my best life. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Be fierce and unapologetic about who you are\n* Never be afraid to show your true colors\n* Surround yourself with people who appreciate your fire\n* Take time to breathe and prioritize self-care\n* Always keep reaching for new heights and never give up on your dreams\n\n#DragonsOfFacebook #TrendingNow #FireBreathingMotivation #DragonSquad #ProfessionalDragon #RelatableContent #FacebookFamous #BusinessOfBeingAFierceDragon\"', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 11:39:00', '2026-05-01 11:39:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 35, '2026-05-01 11:39:18', '2026-05-01 11:39:18'),
(2641, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Tuxedos**: A classic choice for formal parties, tuxedos are sleek, sophisticated, and sure to make a statement.\n2. **Suits**: A well-fitted suit in black, navy, or gray is a timeless choice for formal parties.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A crisp, white dress shirt with a slim tie and cufflinks adds a touch of elegance to any formal outfit.\n4. **Cocktail Attire**: A navy or charcoal gray suit with a patterned dress shirt and a slim tie is a great option for cocktail parties.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Dress Pants**: Dark-washed dress pants with a button-down shirt and a blazer is a stylish and comfortable option for casual parties.\n2. **Jeans and a Button-Down**: A pair of dark-washed jeans with a button-down shirt and a leather jacket is a great casual party look.\n3. **Polos and Chinos**: A polo shirt with chino pants and loafers is a classic casual party outfit.\n4. **Hoodies and Sneakers**: For a more relaxed party, a hoodie with sneakers and distressed denim is a comfortable and stylish option.\n\n**Trendy Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Patterned Shirts**: Bold, patterned shirts with slim-fit pants and sneakers are a trendy and stylish option for parties.\n2. **Velvet Blazers**: A velvet blazer with a dress shirt and dark-washed pants is a stylish and sophisticated option for formal parties.\n3. **Monochromatic Outfits**: Wearing different shades of the same color can create a stylish and cohesive look for parties.\n4. **Accessories**: Adding accessories like pocket squares, cufflinks, and watches can elevate any party outfit.\n\n**Seasonal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Summer**: Lightweight, pastel-colored shirts with linen pants and sandals are perfect for summer parties.\n2. **Winter**: Thick, woolen sweaters with dark-washed jeans and boots are a great option for winter parties.\n3. **Spring**: Lightweight, neutral-colored shirts with chino pants and loafers are a stylish option for spring parties.\n4. **Fall**: Earthy-toned shirts with dark-washed pants and boots are a great option for fall parties.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to be confident, comfortable, and true to your personal style.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 12:40:00', '2026-05-01 12:40:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-01 12:40:21', '2026-05-01 12:40:21'),
(2642, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is designed to be worn in formal or business settings. It is typically made of high-quality fabric, such as cotton or linen, and is characterized by a number of features that distinguish it from more casual shirts.\n\n**Key Features of a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Collar Style:** Formal shirts usually have a point collar or a spread collar, which is a type of collar that is designed to accommodate a tie.\n2. **Cuff Style:** Formal shirts often have French cuffs, which are cuffs that are closed with cufflinks, or button cuffs, which are cuffs that are closed with buttons.\n3. **Fabric:** Formal shirts are typically made of high-quality fabric, such as cotton or linen, that is smooth, crisp, and durable.\n4. **Fit:** Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the torso and sleeves.\n5. **Button Front:** Formal shirts usually have a button front, with a row of buttons that extend from the top of the shirt to the bottom.\n6. **Pockets:** Formal shirts often do not have pockets, or may have a small breast pocket.\n\n**Types of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress Shirt:** A classic formal shirt that is designed to be worn with a suit and tie.\n2. **Business Shirt:** A type of formal shirt that is designed to be worn in a business setting, often with a more relaxed fit than a dress shirt.\n3. **Evening Shirt:** A type of formal shirt that is designed to be worn in the evening, often with a more formal style, such as a wingtip collar and French cuffs.\n\n**Popular Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink:** A British brand that is known for its high-quality formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet:** A French brand that is known for its luxurious formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers:** An American brand that is known for its classic, high-quality formal shirts.\n4. **Armani:** An Italian brand that is known for its stylish and sophisticated formal shirts.\n5. **Hugo Boss:** A German brand that is known for its high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n\n**How to Choose a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the Occasion:** Choose a formal shirt that is appropriate for the occasion, such as a dress shirt for a formal event or a business shirt for a work setting.\n2. **Think About the Color:** Choose a color that complements your skin tone and the occasion, such as white, light blue, or pale pink.\n3. **Consider the Fabric:** Choose a fabric that is comfortable and suitable for the occasion, such as cotton or linen.\n4. **Look for Quality:** Choose a shirt that is made from high-quality materials and construction, such as a shirt with a sturdy collar and cuffs.\n5. **Try it On:** Make sure to try on the shirt before buying it to ensure a good fit.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 12:56:00', '2026-05-01 12:56:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-01 12:56:24', '2026-05-01 12:56:24'),
