g, the man seems utterly at home, his presence commanding and authoritative. He is a true leader, a champion in every sense of the word, and the image seems to capture the very essence of his success mindset.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 17:47:00', '2026-05-01 17:47:27', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/%E2%80%9CPlan_your_business_like_a_play_%E2%80%94_strategy_first%2C_execution_next.%E2%80%9D?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 27, '2026-05-01 17:47:27', '2026-05-01 17:47:27'),
(2663, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:49', 'Wooden craft refers to the art of creating decorative or functional items using wood as the primary material. It involves various techniques, such as carving, cutting, shaping, and assembling, to create unique and beautiful pieces. Here are some popular types of wooden crafts:\n\n1. **Wood Carving**: This involves cutting and shaping wood to create intricate designs, patterns, or figurines. Wood carvings can be used to create decorative items, such as wall hangings, sculptures, or figurines.\n2. **Woodworking**: This involves using various tools and techniques to create functional items, such as furniture, cabinets, or other household items.\n3. **Wood Burning**: This involves using a heated tool to burn designs or patterns onto wooden surfaces. Wood burning can be used to create decorative items, such as coasters, signs, or wall art.\n4. **Wood Turning**: This involves using a lathe to shape and turn wood into symmetrical or rounded shapes, such as bowls, vases, or candlesticks.\n5. **Marquetry**: This involves creating intricate designs or patterns by inlaying small pieces of wood into a larger wooden surface.\n6. **Pyrography**: This involves using a heated tool to burn designs or patterns onto wooden surfaces, similar to wood burning.\n7. **Wood Inlay**: This involves creating intricate designs or patterns by inlaying small pieces of wood into a larger wooden surface.\n\nSome popular wooden craft projects include:\n\n1. **Birdhouses**: Building birdhouses using wood and other materials to create a safe and cozy home for birds.\n2. **Picture Frames**: Creating picture frames using wood and other materials to display favorite photos or artwork.\n3. **Coasters**: Making coasters using wood and other materials to protect surfaces from water marks and spills.\n4. **Candle Holders**: Creating candle holders using wood and other materials to add a touch of warmth and ambiance to any room.\n5. **Custom Signs**: Making custom signs using wood and other materials to display names, messages, or logos.\n\nWooden crafts can be a fun and rewarding hobby, allowing individuals to express their creativity and create unique and functional items for their homes or as gifts.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 17:49:00', '2026-05-01 17:49:13', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/wood_spoon?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 10, '2026-05-01 17:49:13', '2026-05-01 17:49:13'),
(2664, 'Auto Post for facebook at 18:07', 'A flower pot is a container used to hold soil and plants, typically made of materials such as ceramic, clay, plastic, or wood. Flower pots come in a wide range of shapes, sizes, and designs, and can be used to add a decorative touch to indoor or outdoor spaces.\n\nSome common types of flower pots include:\n\n1. Terracotta pots: Made from natural clay, these pots are breathable and allow for good drainage.\n2. Ceramic pots: Made from clay and other materials, these pots are often glazed and can be decorative.\n3. Plastic pots: Lightweight and inexpensive, plastic pots are often used for outdoor plants.\n4. Wooden pots: Made from natural wood, these pots can add a rustic touch to outdoor spaces.\n5. Self-watering pots: These pots have a built-in water reservoir that allows plants to draw water as needed.\n\nFlower pots can be used to plant a variety of plants, including:\n\n1. Flowers: Annuals and perennials, such as roses, daisies, and petunias.\n2. Herbs: Basil, mint, and rosemary are popular herbs to plant in pots.\n3. Vegetables: Tomatoes, peppers, and cucumbers can be grown in large pots.\n4. Succulents: These low-maintenance plants are perfect for indoor pots.\n\nWhen choosing a flower pot, consider the following factors:\n\n1. Size: Choose a pot that is large enough to hold the plant\'s roots and soil.\n2. Material: Consider the durability and breathability of the pot material.\n3. Drainage: Make sure the pot has good drainage holes to prevent waterlogged soil.\n4. Style: Choose a pot that fits your decor and personal style.\n\nOverall, flower pots are a great way to add some greenery to your space and can be a fun and creative way to express your personality.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-01 18:07:00', '2026-05-01 18:07:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Flower_pot?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 33, '2026-05-01 18:07:17', '2026-05-01 18:07:17'),
