(2668, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a symbol of strength, courage, and resilience, dragons have long been a source of fascination and inspiration. Here are some key takeaways from the dragon\'s world that can be applied to our personal and professional lives:\n\n* **Set goals and pursue them with passion**: Just like a dragon guarding its treasure, we must be fierce and dedicated in our pursuit of success.\n* **Be adaptable and open to change**: Dragons are known for their ability to thrive in different environments, reminding us to be flexible and resilient in the face of challenges.\n* **Protect and nurture your inner fire**: A dragon\'s flame is its most valuable asset, and we must prioritize our own well-being and creativity to achieve our full potential.\n* **Surround yourself with a supportive community**: Dragons often live in close-knit groups, highlighting the importance of building strong relationships and networks.\n\n#DragonInspiration #MotivationMonday #ProfessionalGrowth #Resilience #GoalSetting #Adaptability #SelfCare #CommunityFirst #TrendingNow #FacebookInspiration #BusinessTips #PersonalDevelopment', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 10:35:00', '2026-05-02 10:35:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-02 10:35:18', '2026-05-02 10:35:18'),
(2669, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Dari Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and motivations.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by his cousin, Gustavo Gaviria. In the early 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the cartel, and his empire expanded rapidly.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel\'s main business was cocaine trafficking, and Escobar\'s network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers spanned the globe. At the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar\'s success was built on a foundation of violence and intimidation. He was known for his ruthlessness and willingness to use murder, torture, and bribery to eliminate his enemies and maintain control. The Medellín cartel was responsible for thousands of deaths, including politicians, police officers, and civilians.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped in 1992. A massive manhunt ensued, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord, but also as a charismatic and calculating leader who was able to build a vast empire through a combination of intelligence, strategic planning, and violence. His story has been immortalized in numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate called Hacienda Nápoles.\n* He was a skilled politician and was able to manipulate the Colombian government and media to further his interests.\n* Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for the deaths of over 4,000 people, including politicians, police officers, and civilians.\n* He was a devout Catholic and often attended church services, despite his involvement in organized crime.\n* Escobar\'s death was a major blow to the Medellín cartel, and the organization was eventually dismantled by the Colombian government.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 10:45:00', '2026-05-02 10:45:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-02 10:45:21', '2026-05-02 10:45:21'),
(2670, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned the family. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he began his involvement in crime at a young age, selling stolen cars and other goods on the black market.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia at the time. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, becoming one of its top leaders and eventually taking control of the organization.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a vast network of cocaine production, smuggling, and distribution, and its tentacles reached into every level of Colombian society, including politics, law enforcement, and the military.\n\nEscobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and ruthlessness, and he was feared by his enemies and respected by his allies. He was also known for his cunning and strategic thinking, and he was able to evade capture for many years despite the efforts of Colombian and international authorities.\n\n**The Cocaine Empire**\n\nAt the height of its power, the Medellín Cartel was producing and smuggling hundreds of tons of cocaine into the United States and other countries. The cartel\'s profits were enormous, and Escobar became one of the richest men in the world, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion.\n\nEscobar\'s cocaine empire was built on a complex network of relationships with other cartels, smugglers, and distributors. He was able to corrupt and intimidate many officials and law enforcement officers, and he used violence and intimidation to maintain control over his organization and eliminate his enemies.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government and international authorities launched a series of operations aimed at capturing or killing Escobar. The hunt for Escobar became a major priority for law enforcement agencies around the world, and he was eventually placed on the FBI\'s Ten Most Wanted Fugitives list.\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral, which was designed to be escape-proof. However, Escobar was able to escape from the prison in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\nEscobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including law enforcement officers, politicians, and innocent civilians. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and intelligent leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization from scratch.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which tells the story of his rise and fall.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of luxury and extravagance, and he owned a number of expensive cars, homes, and other properties.\n* He was a fan of soccer and owned a team called Atlético Nacional, which won several championships during his ownership.\n* Escobar was married to María Victoria Henao, and the couple had two children together.\n* He was known for his philanthropy and built a number of schools, hospitals, and other infrastructure projects in his hometown of Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s death was seen as a major victory for law enforcement agencies around the world, and it marked the beginning of the end of the Medellín Cartel\'s dominance of the global cocaine trade.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 10:50:00', '2026-05-02 10:50:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-02 10:50:20', '2026-05-02 10:50:20'),
(2671, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his actions and decisions.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a teenager, selling cigarettes and other contraband on the streets of Medellín. He quickly moved on to more lucrative crimes, such as car theft and robbery. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia.\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was swift and ruthless. He eliminated his competitors, bribed officials, and formed alliances with other powerful crime lords. By the early 1980s, he had become one of the most prominent figures in the Medellín cartel, which controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became a multibillion-dollar empire, with operations in Colombia, the United States, Mexico, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s innovative tactics, including the use of small planes to transport cocaine from Colombia to the United States.\n\nEscobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and violence. He ordered the assassination of countless rivals, politicians, and law enforcement officials who stood in his way. He also used terrorism and intimidation to maintain control over his organization and the communities in which he operated.\n\n**War on Drugs**\n\nThe United States government, led by President Ronald Reagan, launched a \"War on Drugs\" in the 1980s, which targeted Escobar and the Medellín cartel. The U.S. government worked closely with the Colombian government to dismantle the cartel and capture Escobar.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, he continued to run his organization from behind bars and eventually escaped in 1992.\n\nA massive manhunt ensued, with the Colombian and U.S. governments working together to capture Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought wealth and power to his family and community. However, his actions also brought devastating violence and destruction to countless people and communities.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been immortalized in numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His life and death continue to fascinate people around the world, serving as a cautionary tale about the dangers of crime and the corrupting influence of power.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a mansion with a private airport.\n* He was estimated to have earned over $30 billion during his lifetime, making him one of the wealthiest people in the world.\n* Escobar was a skilled politician and formed alliances with Colombian politicians and military officials to further his interests.\n* He was a prolific philanthropist, donating to local charities and building infrastructure projects in Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s death was celebrated by many Colombians, who saw him as a symbol of the country\'s violent and corrupt past.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 10:53:00', '2026-05-02 10:53:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-02 10:53:19', '2026-05-02 10:53:19'),
(2672, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business/creator on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing my true self and living life to the fullest. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Believe in yourself and your abilities, just like I believe in my fire-breathing skills\n* Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things - it\'s how I discovered my love for flying\n* Surround yourself with people who support and encourage you, just like my dragon friends do\n* Remember to take care of yourself, both physically and mentally - a happy dragon is a healthy dragon\n\n#DragonsOfFacebook #MotivationMonday #SelfCare #MentalHealthMatters #BelieveInYourself #FireBreathingFrenzy #DragonSquad #TrendingNow\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, including #MotivationMonday, #SelfCare, and #MentalHealthMatters, to reach a wider audience. The brand voice is professional and relatable, making it suitable for a Facebook post.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 11:18:00', '2026-05-02 11:18:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-02 11:18:20', '2026-05-02 11:18:20'),
(2673, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Tuxedos**: A classic choice for formal events, tuxedos are sleek, sophisticated, and sure to make a statement.\n2. **Suits**: A well-fitted suit in a neutral color like black, navy, or gray is a versatile option for formal parties.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: Pair a dress shirt with a suit or tuxedo for a polished look.\n4. **Bow Ties**: Add a touch of elegance with a bow tie in a bold color or pattern.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A blazer can dress up a simple outfit and add a touch of sophistication.\n2. **Dress Pants**: Pair dress pants with a button-down shirt and blazer for a stylish look.\n3. **Polo Shirts**: Polo shirts are a great option for semi-formal parties, especially in bright colors or bold patterns.\n4. **Loafers**: Slip-on loafers or dress shoes can complete a semi-formal outfit.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Jeans**: A pair of dark-washed jeans can be dressed up or down for a casual party.\n2. **Graphic T-Shirts**: Bold graphic tees are perfect for casual parties, especially in bright colors or fun designs.\n3. **Hoodies**: A hoodie can add a relaxed touch to a casual outfit.\n4. **Sneakers**: Sneakers are a great option for casual parties, especially in bold colors or statement designs.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Watches**: A stylish watch can add a touch of sophistication to any outfit.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to a dress shirt.\n3. **Pocket Squares**: A pocket square can add a pop of color and texture to a suit or blazer.\n4. **Hats**: A fedora or panama hat can add a stylish touch to a casual outfit.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Dress according to the theme**: If the party has a specific theme, dress accordingly to show your enthusiasm and creativity.\n2. **Pay attention to fit**: Make sure your clothes fit well to avoid looking sloppy or uncomfortable.\n3. **Accessories matter**: Add a few statement accessories to elevate your outfit and show your personality.\n4. **Be confident**: Own your look and have fun!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 12:40:00', '2026-05-02 12:40:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-02 12:40:19', '2026-05-02 12:40:19'),
(2674, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is designed to be worn for business, formal events, and other professional occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts typically have a point collar, spread collar, or cutaway collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or barrel cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are usually made from high-quality cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely, with a slim silhouette and a fitted waist.\n5. **Buttons**: Formal shirts typically have mother-of-pearl or plastic buttons.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a point collar and French cuffs.\n2. **Business shirt**: A more relaxed formal shirt with a spread collar and barrel cuffs.\n3. **Wingtip shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and French cuffs.\n4. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt designed to be worn with a tuxedo, typically with a wingtip collar and studs.\n\n** Colors and Patterns:**\n\n1. **White**: A classic choice for formal shirts, suitable for business and formal events.\n2. **Light blue**: A popular choice for formal shirts, suitable for business and formal events.\n3. **Pastel colors**: Soft pink, baby blue, and mint green are popular colors for formal shirts.\n4. **Stripes and checks**: Subtle stripes and checks are common patterns for formal shirts.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: A British brand known for its high-quality formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand known for its luxurious formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: An American brand known for its classic formal shirts.\n4. **Hugo Boss**: A German brand known for its stylish and modern formal shirts.\n\n**Tips for Wearing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Pair with a suit**: A formal shirt is typically worn with a suit and tie.\n2. **Choose the right collar style**: Choose a collar style that complements your face shape and the occasion.\n3. **Pay attention to fit**: Make sure the shirt fits well and is not too tight or too loose.\n4. **Accessories**: Add a tie, cufflinks, and a watch to complete the formal look.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 12:56:00', '2026-05-02 12:56:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-02 12:56:17', '2026-05-02 12:56:17'),
(2675, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', '**\"Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Den\"**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about passion, perseverance, and success. Here are some key takeaways:\n\n* **Set your goals ablaze**: Don\'t be afraid to dream big and chase your ambitions with fierce determination.\n* **Protect your treasure**: Invest in yourself and your business, and guard your assets with wisdom and strategic planning.\n* **Breathe fire into your marketing**: Create content that ignites excitement and sparks engagement, leaving a lasting impression on your audience.\n* **Soar to new heights**: Stay adaptable, innovative, and open to new opportunities, always striving to improve and evolve.\n\n#DragonEnergy #BusinessTips #EntrepreneurMindset #MarketingStrategy #SuccessMindset #TrendingNow #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalAdvice #MotivationMonday #BusinessInspiration #DragonDen', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-02 13:03:00', '2026-05-02 13:03:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Women_Sandel?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-05-02 13:03:17', '2026-05-02 13:03:17'),
