(2700, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Unlocking the Power of Dragons in Business**\n\nAs a symbol of strength, courage, and resilience, dragons have long been a source of inspiration for entrepreneurs and creators alike. Here are some key takeaways on what we can learn from these mythical creatures:\n\n* **Embracing innovation**: Just like dragons are known for their fiery breath, businesses can ignite their own spark by embracing new ideas and technologies.\n* **Building strong foundations**: A dragon\'s lair is often hidden deep within a mountain, symbolizing the importance of building a solid foundation for long-term success.\n* **Adapting to change**: Dragons are known for their ability to navigate through treacherous terrain, teaching us the value of being agile and adaptable in an ever-changing business landscape.\n* **Fostering community**: In many mythologies, dragons are depicted as guardians of treasure, highlighting the importance of building strong relationships and nurturing a sense of community.\n\n#DragonInspiration #BusinessTips #InnovationNation #EntrepreneurMindset #ResilienceMatters #TrendingNow #FacebookForBusiness #SmallBusinessTips #MarketingMotivation #CreativityUnleashed', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 10:35:00', '2026-05-03 10:35:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-03 10:35:18', '2026-05-03 10:35:18'),
(2701, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and feared criminal organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Career**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. He was the third of seven children, and his family was considered to be of modest means. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and limited opportunities, which would later drive his desire for wealth and power.\n\nEscobar began his career in crime at a young age, starting with small-time smuggling and theft. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Colombian underworld, becoming a key player in the country\'s burgeoning cocaine trade. In the 1970s, Escobar joined forces with other prominent drug traffickers, including Carlos Lehder and Gustavo Gaviria, to form the Medellín cartel.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel\'s main business was cocaine production and distribution, with Escobar controlling a significant portion of the global market. At the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be earning over $20 billion per year, making him one of the richest men in the world.\n\nThe Medellín cartel\'s success was due in part to Escobar\'s ruthless tactics and his ability to corrupt and intimidate law enforcement officials. He was known for his use of violence and intimidation to eliminate rivals and maintain control over his territory. Escobar\'s organization was also notorious for its use of \"plata o plomo\" (silver or lead), a phrase that referred to the cartel\'s practice of offering bribes or bullets to those who stood in their way.\n\n**Personal Life and Excesses**\n\nEscobar was known for his flamboyant and extravagant lifestyle. He owned numerous mansions, cars, and airplanes, and was said to have a private zoo and a collection of exotic animals. He was also a fan of soccer and owned a team, Atlético Nacional, which won several championships during his ownership.\n\nDespite his wealth and power, Escobar\'s personal life was marked by turmoil and violence. He was married to María Victoria Henao, and the couple had two children together. However, Escobar\'s infidelity and womanizing were well-documented, and he had numerous mistresses and children outside of his marriage.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nEscobar\'s reign as the \"King of Cocaine\" came to an end in 1993, when he was killed in a shootout with Colombian police. The operation, code-named \"Operation Search Bloc,\" was carried out by a team of elite police officers who had been tracking Escobar for months.\n\nEscobar\'s death marked the beginning of the end of the Medellín cartel, and many of his top lieutenants were either killed or captured in the following years. The cartel\'s assets were seized, and its operations were dismantled.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. On the one hand, he is remembered as a ruthless and brutal criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. On the other hand, he is also seen as a symbol of Colombian culture and a representation of the country\'s struggles with poverty and inequality.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story has captivated audiences around the world, and he remains one of the most fascinating and infamous figures in modern history.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his generosity and philanthropy, particularly in his hometown of Medellín. He built roads, schools, and hospitals, and was seen as a hero by many poor Colombians.\n* Escobar\'s favorite car was the Mercedes-Benz 600, which he owned several of.\n* Escobar was a fan of the Colombian soccer team, Atlético Nacional, and owned the team for several years.\n* Escobar\'s net worth at the time of his death was estimated to be over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world.\n* Escobar\'s grave is located in the Itagüí cemetery in Medellín, Colombia, and has become a popular tourist attraction.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 10:45:00', '2026-05-03 10:45:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-03 10:45:23', '2026-05-03 10:45:23'),
(2702, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and feared organized crime groups in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and influential criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned them. Escobar was a bright student and attended the Universidad Autónoma Latinoamericana in Medellín, but he dropped out to pursue a life of crime.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a car thief and a smuggler of small amounts of marijuana. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia. He partnered with other smugglers and dealers, including Carlos Lehder, and together they formed the Medellín cartel.\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was swift and brutal. He used violence, intimidation, and bribery to eliminate his competitors and consolidate his control over the cocaine trade. He became known as \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) and was feared by his enemies and admired by his followers.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, led by Escobar, became one of the most powerful and lucrative organized crime groups in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and its profits were estimated to be in the billions of dollars.\n\nEscobar\'s organization was known for its ruthlessness and brutality. He ordered the killings of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and rival gang members. He also bribed and corrupted government officials, including politicians and military personnel, to ensure his organization\'s protection and impunity.\n\n**Personal Life**\n\nEscobar was known for his flamboyant and extravagant lifestyle. He owned numerous mansions, cars, and airplanes, and he loved to flaunt his wealth. He was also a family man and was married to María Victoria Henao, with whom he had two children.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, Escobar\'s empire began to crumble. The Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The manhunt was one of the most extensive and intense in history, with thousands of police and military personnel involved.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old. The killing of Escobar marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror, but it also led to a power vacuum that was filled by other organized crime groups.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and brutal crime lord who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and lucrative empire.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV series, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story has captivated audiences around the world, and he remains one of the most fascinating and infamous figures in modern history.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of soccer and owned a team called Atlético Nacional.\n* He was a fan of the Colombian singer and songwriter, vallenato musician Andrés Calamaro.\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power.\n* He was responsible for the deaths of over 4,000 people, including politicians, police officers, and rival gang members.\n* Escobar\'s grave is located in Itagüí, Colombia, and has become a tourist attraction.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 10:50:00', '2026-05-03 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-03 10:50:18', '2026-05-03 10:50:18'),
(2703, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious cocaine trafficking organizations in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned them. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he quickly became involved in petty crime to support himself and his family.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working for various cocaine traffickers in Medellín, eventually becoming a key player in the city\'s burgeoning cocaine trade. He quickly rose through the ranks, earning a reputation for his ruthlessness, intelligence, and business acumen.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar co-founded the Medellín cartel with his partners, including Carlos Lehder and Gustavo Gaviria. The cartel quickly became one of the most powerful and profitable cocaine trafficking organizations in the world, with Escobar at its helm.\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel expanded its operations to include smuggling, extortion, and murder. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s innovative tactics, including the use of small planes to transport cocaine and the creation of a network of hidden laboratories and distribution centers.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Feuds**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: Escobar ordered the murder of Galán, who was a vocal opponent of the cartel, in 1989.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: Escobar\'s cartel planted a bomb on a commercial airliner, killing 110 people, in an attempt to intimidate the Colombian government.\n3. **The murder of police officers and judges**: Escobar\'s cartel targeted and killed numerous law enforcement officials and judges who were investigating or prosecuting cartel members.\n\nEscobar was also involved in several high-profile feuds, including a bitter rivalry with the Cali cartel, which was led by the Rodríguez Orejuela brothers.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped from prison in 1992.\n\nA massive manhunt ensued, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. His death marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror and paved the way for the rise of new cocaine trafficking organizations in Colombia.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering, but he is also revered by some as a folk hero who brought wealth and prosperity to his community.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and exploits have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which chronicles the rise and fall of the Medellín cartel.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s story serves as a cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime and the corrupting influence of power and wealth.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 10:53:00', '2026-05-03 10:53:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-03 10:53:19', '2026-05-03 10:53:19'),
(2704, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Key Takeaways for Success**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned valuable lessons that can be applied to both personal and professional growth. Here are some key points to consider:\n\n* **Set ambitious goals**: Just like a dragon sets its sights on a treasure hoard, you should strive for greatness and aim high.\n* **Develop a strong sense of self**: Understand your strengths, weaknesses, and passions to unlock your full potential.\n* **Cultivate resilience**: Life can be unpredictable, but with perseverance and determination, you can overcome any obstacle.\n* **Surround yourself with supportive allies**: A strong network of friends, family, or colleagues can make all the difference in achieving success.\n* **Continuously learn and adapt**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new knowledge, skills, and experiences.\n\n#Trending #Motivation #SuccessTips #PersonalGrowth #ProfessionalDevelopment #DragonInspiration #FireWithin #GoalSetting #Resilience #Networking #LifelongLearning\n\nShare your thoughts and experiences in the comments below! What inspires you to reach new heights?', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 11:18:00', '2026-05-03 11:18:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-03 11:18:21', '2026-05-03 11:18:21'),
(2705, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', '**Men\'s Party Wear: A Guide to Stylish and Fashionable Options**\n\nWhen it comes to party wear for men, there are numerous options to choose from, depending on the occasion, theme, and personal style. Here are some popular and stylish options:\n\n### Formal Party Wear\n\n1. **Suit and Tie**: A classic combination that exudes elegance and sophistication. Choose from a variety of colors, patterns, and fabrics, such as navy blue, black, gray, or charcoal.\n2. **Tuxedo**: Perfect for black-tie events, a tuxedo is a timeless and stylish option. Pair it with a bow tie, cummerbund, and patent leather shoes.\n3. **Dinner Jacket**: A dinner jacket is a versatile and stylish option for formal parties. It can be paired with a dress shirt, trousers, and a tie.\n\n### Semi-Formal Party Wear\n\n1. **Blazer and Jeans**: A blazer can add a touch of sophistication to a pair of jeans and a dress shirt. Choose from a variety of colors and patterns, such as navy blue, gray, or brown.\n2. **Dress Shirt and Trousers**: A dress shirt and trousers are a classic combination that can be dressed up or down, depending on the occasion.\n3. **Chinos and a Button-Down Shirt**: Chinos and a button-down shirt are a stylish and comfortable option for semi-formal parties.\n\n### Casual Party Wear\n\n1. **Graphic T-Shirt and Jeans**: A graphic t-shirt and jeans are a casual and stylish option for parties.\n2. **Hoodie and Sweatpants**: A hoodie and sweatpants are a comfortable and relaxed option for casual parties.\n3. **Shorts and a T-Shirt**: Shorts and a t-shirt are a great option for summer parties or outdoor events.\n\n### Accessories\n\n1. **Watch**: A watch can add a touch of elegance and sophistication to any outfit.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks can add a touch of personality and style to a dress shirt.\n3. **Shoes**: Choose from a variety of shoes, such as dress shoes, boots, or sneakers, depending on the occasion and outfit.\n\n### Tips and Tricks\n\n1. **Dress according to the occasion**: Make sure to dress according to the theme and occasion of the party.\n2. **Accessories can make or break an outfit**: Choose accessories that complement your outfit and add a touch of personality.\n3. **Be confident**: Confidence is key to pulling off any outfit. Own your look and have fun!\n\nBy following these guidelines, you\'ll be sure to make a stylish and fashionable impression at any party. Remember to have fun and express your personal style!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 12:40:00', '2026-05-03 12:40:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-03 12:40:24', '2026-05-03 12:40:24'),
(2706, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is designed to be worn on formal occasions, such as business meetings, job interviews, weddings, and other special events. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts typically have a point collar or a spread collar, which is a type of collar that is designed to accommodate a tie.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or barrel cuffs, which are designed to be worn with cufflinks.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are usually made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the chest and waist.\n5. **Buttons**: Formal shirts often have mother-of-pearl or plastic buttons, which are designed to be durable and long-lasting.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Classic fit**: A classic fit formal shirt is a traditional style that is designed to fit comfortably through the chest and waist.\n2. **Slim fit**: A slim fit formal shirt is designed to fit closely to the body, with a modern and streamlined silhouette.\n3. **Cutaway collar**: A cutaway collar formal shirt has a collar that is cut away from the face, creating a more relaxed and casual look.\n4. **Wingtip collar**: A wingtip collar formal shirt has a collar that is shaped like a wing, with a more formal and elegant look.\n5. **Tuxedo shirt**: A tuxedo shirt is a type of formal shirt that is designed to be worn with a tuxedo, with a wingtip collar and French cuffs.\n\n**Colors:**\n\n1. **White**: White is a classic color for formal shirts, and is often worn with a black tie or a suit.\n2. **Light blue**: Light blue is a popular color for formal shirts, and is often worn with a navy blue suit or a gray suit.\n3. **Pastel colors**: Pastel colors such as pale pink, baby blue, and mint green are popular for formal shirts, and can add a touch of elegance to a outfit.\n4. **Stripes**: Striped formal shirts are a classic style, and can add a touch of personality to a outfit.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: Thomas Pink is a luxury brand that offers high-quality formal shirts with a classic and elegant design.\n2. **Charvet**: Charvet is a luxury brand that offers high-quality formal shirts with a modern and sophisticated design.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: Brooks Brothers is a classic American brand that offers high-quality formal shirts with a traditional and elegant design.\n4. **Ted Baker**: Ted Baker is a British brand that offers high-quality formal shirts with a modern and stylish design.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Choose a shirt that fits well**: A well-fitting shirt is essential for a formal outfit, so make sure to choose a shirt that fits closely to the body.\n2. **Consider the occasion**: Consider the occasion and the dress code when choosing a formal shirt, and make sure to choose a shirt that is appropriate for the event.\n3. **Pay attention to details**: Pay attention to details such as the collar style, cuff style, and fabric, and make sure to choose a shirt that meets your needs and preferences.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 12:56:00', '2026-05-03 12:56:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-03 12:56:20', '2026-05-03 12:56:20'),
(2707, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', '**Empowering Your Business with a Roar**\n\nAs a dragon in the business world, we understand the importance of being relatable and connecting with our audience. Here are some key points to consider:\n\n* **Authenticity is key**: Be true to your brand and values to build trust with your customers\n* **Emotional connection**: Share your story and show your human side to create a lasting impression\n* **Consistency is crucial**: Maintain a consistent tone and voice across all platforms to reinforce your brand identity\n* **Engage with your audience**: Respond to comments and messages promptly to show you care about their feedback and concerns\n* **Stay up-to-date with trends**: Keep an eye on industry trends and adapt to changes to stay ahead of the competition\n\n#BusinessTips #MarketingStrategy #BrandIdentity #RelatableContent #TrendingNow #FacebookMarketing #DragonApproved #ProfessionalVoice #BusinessGrowth #Innovation #Leadership #Entrepreneurship #SmallBusiness #StartupLife #DigitalMarketing #SocialMediaMarketing #ContentCreation #EngagementMatters #CustomerFirst #BrandStorytelling', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-03 13:03:00', '2026-05-03 13:03:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Women_Sandel?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-05-03 13:03:15', '2026-05-03 13:03:15');
