(2731, 'Auto Post for facebook at 03:29', 'It seems like you didn\'t provide a prompt. Please go ahead and ask a question, provide a topic, or request assistance with something, and I\'ll do my best to help. I\'m here to provide information, answer questions, and engage in conversation. What\'s on your mind?', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-04 03:29:00', '2026-05-04 03:29:14', 76, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/prompt?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 49, '2026-05-04 03:29:14', '2026-05-04 03:29:14'),
(2732, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Empowering Your Business with a Roar**\n\nAs a dragon in the business world, we understand the importance of staying ahead of the curve. Here are some key points to consider:\n\n* **Innovate and Adapt**: Stay up-to-date with the latest trends and technologies to stay competitive.\n* **Build a Strong Team**: Surround yourself with talented and dedicated individuals who share your vision.\n* **Take Calculated Risks**: Don\'t be afraid to take bold steps to achieve your goals.\n* **Focus on Customer Satisfaction**: Prioritize the needs and expectations of your customers to build a loyal client base.\n\n#BusinessSuccess #Entrepreneurship #Innovation #Teamwork #RiskManagement #CustomerSatisfaction #TrendingNow #BusinessTips #DragonApproved #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalAdvice', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-04 10:35:00', '2026-05-04 10:35:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-04 10:35:20', '2026-05-04 10:35:20'),
(2733, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious organized crime groups in history. Here\'s a brief overview of his life and career:\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned them. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and inform his actions.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a small-time smuggler and thief, but he quickly rose through the ranks of the Colombian underworld. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was then a relatively new and lucrative market. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him build a network of loyal associates and establish himself as a major player in the Medellín cartel.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, led by Escobar, became one of the most powerful and feared organized crime groups in the world. At its peak, the cartel controlled up to 80% of the global cocaine market, with annual revenues estimated to be around $20 billion. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality, using violence and intimidation to maintain control over its territory and eliminate rivals.\n\n**Notorious Acts**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious acts, including:\n\n1. **The Palace of Justice siege**: In 1985, Escobar\'s henchmen stormed the Palace of Justice in Bogotá, taking hundreds of hostages and killing over 100 people.\n2. **The assassination of Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the murder of presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán, who had vowed to crack down on the cartel.\n3. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s men bombed a commercial airliner, killing 110 people, in an attempt to kill a potential witness against him.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned, but he continued to run his empire from behind bars. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt ensued, with the Colombian government and the US DEA working together to track him down.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era for the Medellín cartel, and it had a significant impact on the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was a ruthless and violent individual, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite his notoriety, Escobar remains a fascinating and intriguing figure, and his impact on the world of organized crime continues to be felt today.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-04 10:45:00', '2026-05-04 10:45:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-04 10:45:26', '2026-05-04 10:45:26');
