(2768, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Empowering Your Business with Dragon\'s Expertise**\n\nAs a seasoned entrepreneur and business leader, I\'d like to share with you the key points to consider when taking your business to the next level:\n\n* **Set clear goals**: Establish a strong vision and mission statement to guide your decision-making process.\n* **Develop a unique value proposition**: Identify what sets your business apart from the competition and communicate it effectively to your target audience.\n* **Build a strong team**: Surround yourself with talented and dedicated individuals who share your passion and commitment to excellence.\n* **Stay adaptable**: Remain flexible and open to new ideas, technologies, and market trends to stay ahead of the curve.\n* **Foster a positive company culture**: Encourage collaboration, innovation, and continuous learning to drive growth and success.\n\n#BusinessSuccess #Entrepreneurship #Leadership #Innovation #GrowthMindset #TrendingNow #BusinessTips #SuccessStory #DragonApproved #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalDevelopment #BusinessGrowth #MarketingStrategy', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-05 10:35:00', '2026-05-05 10:35:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-05 10:35:17', '2026-05-05 10:35:17'),
(2769, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and one of the most infamous criminals of the 20th century. He was the founder and leader of the Medellín cartel, which became one of the most powerful and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda Gaviria, after his father abandoned the family. Escobar began his criminal career at a young age, selling stolen cars and cigarettes on the black market. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which was becoming increasingly lucrative in Colombia.\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was rapid. He formed alliances with other drug traffickers and used violence and intimidation to eliminate his competitors. He also bribed and corrupted government officials, police, and military personnel to ensure his operations went undisturbed.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the 1980s, Escobar\'s organization, the Medellín cartel, became the dominant force in the global cocaine trade. The cartel\'s operations were highly organized and sophisticated, with a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. Escobar\'s organization was responsible for smuggling hundreds of tons of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other countries, generating billions of dollars in revenue.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and journalists. He also ordered the bombing of airplanes, buses, and other public places, causing widespread fear and destruction.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a massive manhunt for Escobar. The search was led by Colonel Hugo Martínez, a Colombian police officer who had dedicated his life to capturing Escobar.\n\n**Death**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. The police had tracked him down to a safe house in the city, and after a brief shootout, Escobar was fatally wounded. He died shortly after being shot, bringing an end to his reign of terror.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal criminal who caused immense harm and suffering to countless people. However, he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a mansion with a private golf course.\n* He was also known for his generosity to the poor, and he built roads, schools, and hospitals in Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for the murder of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n* Escobar\'s brother, Roberto Escobar, was also involved in the cartel and was arrested in 1990.\n* The Medellín cartel\'s operations were so sophisticated that they even had their own airline, which was used to smuggle cocaine into the United States.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-05 10:45:00', '2026-05-05 10:45:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-05 10:45:24', '2026-05-05 10:45:24'),
(2770, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and feared criminal organizations in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He dropped out of school at a young age and began his life of crime, starting with small-time thefts and eventually moving on to more serious crimes, such as smuggling and kidnapping. In the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia.\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was swift and brutal. He formed the Medellín cartel with his cousins and other associates, and they quickly established themselves as major players in the cocaine trade. Escobar\'s organization was known for its ruthlessness and efficiency, and he became one of the wealthiest and most feared men in Colombia.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, under Escobar\'s leadership, dominated the global cocaine trade in the 1980s. The organization was responsible for smuggling massive quantities of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other parts of the world. Escobar\'s cartel was also involved in other crimes, such as money laundering, extortion, and murder.\n\nEscobar\'s success was due in part to his ability to corrupt and intimidate government officials, law enforcement, and other organized crime groups. He was known for his cunning and ruthlessness, and his organization was feared by many.\n\n**The War on Drugs and the Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the 1980s, the United States government, under the leadership of President Ronald Reagan, launched a \"War on Drugs\" aimed at reducing the flow of cocaine into the country. The Colombian government, with the support of the US, began to crack down on the Medellín cartel and other organized crime groups.\n\nEscobar became a target of the authorities, and a massive manhunt was launched to capture him. The Colombian police, with the help of the US DEA and other international law enforcement agencies, pursued Escobar relentlessly.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death. Escobar\'s death marked the end of an era for the Medellín cartel, and his legacy continues to be felt today.\n\nEscobar\'s impact on Colombia and the world was significant. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including innocent civilians, police officers, and rival gang members. His organization also contributed to the corruption and instability of the Colombian government and economy.\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a fascinating and complex figure, and his story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries. The Netflix series \"Narcos\" (2015-2017) is a dramatized account of Escobar\'s life and the rise and fall of the Medellín cartel.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his flamboyant lifestyle, which included owning exotic animals, luxury cars, and a private zoo.\n* He was a skilled soccer player and even owned a professional soccer team in Colombia.\n* Escobar was a devoted family man and was known to be fiercely protective of his loved ones.\n* He was responsible for the construction of many infrastructure projects in Medellín, including roads, schools, and hospitals.\n* Escobar\'s net worth at the time of his death was estimated to be around $30 billion, making him one of the wealthiest people in the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-05 10:50:00', '2026-05-05 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-05 10:50:18', '2026-05-05 10:50:18'),
(2771, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious criminal organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most successful and infamous drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was exposed to crime and corruption from a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a teenager, smuggling cigarettes and other contraband. He quickly moved on to more lucrative crimes, including car theft and robbery. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which would eventually make him a billionaire.\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was facilitated by his cunning, ruthlessness, and ability to build a vast network of loyal associates and corrupt officials. He established a sophisticated smuggling operation, using planes, boats, and trucks to transport cocaine from Colombia to the United States and other countries.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the 1980s, Escobar became the leader of the Medellín cartel, which dominated the global cocaine trade. The cartel\'s success was due in part to Escobar\'s innovative tactics, including the use of submarines and other advanced smuggling techniques.\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be earning over $420 million per week, making him one of the richest men in the world. He invested his wealth in real estate, businesses, and other ventures, and he became a prominent figure in Colombian society.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, politicians, and rival gang members. He also ordered the bombing of airplanes, buildings, and other targets, including the Avianca Flight 203, which was blown up in mid-air in 1989, killing 110 people.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and a massive manhunt was launched to capture him.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord, but also as a charismatic and generous figure who was loved by many in Colombia. His story has inspired numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar\'s impact on Colombian society and politics cannot be denied. He was a product of the country\'s poverty, corruption, and violence, and his rise to power was facilitated by the weaknesses of the Colombian state.\n\nToday, Escobar\'s legacy serves as a reminder of the dangers of organized crime and the importance of addressing the root causes of poverty and inequality. His story also highlights the need for effective law enforcement and international cooperation to combat the global threat of drug trafficking and terrorism.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-05 10:53:00', '2026-05-05 10:53:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-05 10:53:20', '2026-05-05 10:53:20'),
(2772, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing Your Inner Strength**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned that success is not just about breathing fire, but about staying focused and driven. Here are some key takeaways to help you unleash your inner power:\n\n* Set clear goals and priorities to achieve your vision\n* Stay adaptable and resilient in the face of challenges\n* Surround yourself with a supportive community that believes in you\n* Continuously learn and improve to stay ahead of the curve\n* Believe in yourself and your abilities, just like a dragon believes in its fire\n\n#MotivationMonday #DragonEnergy #InnerStrength #GoalSetting #Resilience #CommunitySupport #LifelongLearning #SelfBelief #TrendingNow #FacebookInspiration #BusinessTips #PersonalGrowth #SuccessMindset', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-05 11:18:00', '2026-05-05 11:18:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-05 11:18:20', '2026-05-05 11:18:20'),
(2773, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:57', 'A pen is a writing instrument used to apply ink to a surface, typically paper, in order to write or draw. It is a common tool used for everyday tasks such as writing notes, signing documents, and creating artwork.\n\nThere are several types of pens, including:\n\n1. Ballpoint pens: These are the most common type of pen and use a small metal ball to dispense ink onto the paper.\n2. Rollerball pens: These pens use a small metal ball to dispense liquid ink onto the paper, creating a smooth and fluid writing experience.\n3. Fountain pens: These pens use a nib to deliver ink onto the paper and are often used for calligraphy and other forms of artistic writing.\n4. Gel pens: These pens use a water-based ink that is suspended in a gel-like substance, creating a vibrant and colorful writing experience.\n5. Fineliners: These pens use a fine tip to create precise lines and are often used for technical drawing and illustration.\n\nPens have been used for thousands of years, with early versions made from reeds and papyrus. The modern pen as we know it today was developed in the 19th century, with the invention of the ballpoint pen in the 1940s.\n\nSome interesting facts about pens include:\n\n* The first pen was made from a reed, with the ink being made from soot and gum.\n* The word \"pen\" comes from the Latin word \"penna,\" meaning \"feather.\"\n* The average person uses around 4-6 pens per year.\n* The longest pen in the world was over 10 feet long and was made in 2018.\n\nOverall, pens are a ubiquitous tool that have been used for centuries to create written communication and artistic expression.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-05 11:57:00', '2026-05-05 11:57:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 16, '2026-05-05 11:57:18', '2026-05-05 11:57:18'),
