(2811, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He was the third of seven children to Abel de Jesús Dari Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. Escobar\'s family was of modest means, and he grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in crime began at a young age. He started by selling stolen cars and eventually moved on to more serious crimes, such as kidnapping and robbery. In the 1970s, he became involved in the cocaine trade, which would eventually become the source of his vast wealth and power.\n\nIn 1976, Escobar founded the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world. He quickly rose to prominence, earning the nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) for his ruthless and efficient leadership.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel dominated the global cocaine trade. The cartel\'s operations were characterized by brutal violence, intimidation, and corruption. Escobar was known for his cunning and strategic thinking, and he was able to outmaneuver his competitors and law enforcement agencies.\n\nThe Medellín Cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s ability to establish a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. He also invested heavily in legitimate businesses, such as real estate and construction, to launder his profits and legitimize his wealth.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, politicians, and innocent civilians. His cartel was known for its use of car bombs, assassinations, and massacres to intimidate and eliminate rivals and opponents.\n\nIn 1989, Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people. The bombing was intended to kill a presidential candidate, César Gaviria, who was a vocal opponent of Escobar.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially designed prison, known as La Catedral. However, he continued to run his cartel from behind bars and eventually escaped in 1992.\n\nA massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down and killed in a shootout with Colombian police on December 1, 1993, his 44th birthday.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord, but also as a charismatic and generous figure who was loved by many in his community. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar\'s impact on Colombian society and politics cannot be overstated. His cartel\'s violence and corruption contributed to a period of instability and chaos in Colombia, and his legacy continues to be felt today.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate, known as Hacienda Napoles.\n* He was a skilled soccer player and was known to have played in local tournaments.\n* Escobar was a devout Catholic and was known to have made significant donations to the Catholic Church.\n* His cartel was responsible for the assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n* Escobar\'s death was mourned by many in Medellín, who saw him as a folk hero and a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-06 10:50:00', '2026-05-06 10:50:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-06 10:50:21', '2026-05-06 10:50:21'),
(2812, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, narco-terrorist, and leader of the Medellín cartel, which was one of the most powerful and feared criminal organizations in the world during the 1980s and early 1990s. He is often referred to as the \"King of Cocaine\" due to his dominance of the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. He grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in small-time crime at a young age. Escobar\'s early crimes included selling stolen cars, robbing banks, and smuggling cigarettes.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to focus on the cocaine trade, which was becoming increasingly lucrative due to the growing demand for the drug in the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by his cousin, Gustavo Gaviria. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him to build a network of loyal associates and to expand the cartel\'s operations.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and Escobar\'s personal wealth was estimated to be over $30 billion.\n\nThe Medellín cartel was known for its brutality and violence. Escobar and his associates used murder, intimidation, and bribery to maintain control and eliminate rivals. They also used their wealth and influence to corrupt government officials and law enforcement agencies.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Events**\n\nSome of the most notable crimes and events associated with Pablo Escobar include:\n\n1. **The Assassination of Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Luis Carlos Galán, a Colombian presidential candidate who had vowed to crack down on the Medellín cartel.\n2. **The Bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people. The bombing was intended to kill Galán, who was not on the flight.\n3. **The Siege of the Palace of Justice**: In 1985, Escobar\'s associates, including his brother Roberto, took hundreds of hostages at the Palace of Justice in Bogotá. The siege ended in a bloodbath, with over 100 people killed.\n4. **The Murder of Rodrigo Lara Bonilla**: In 1984, Escobar ordered the murder of Rodrigo Lara Bonilla, the Colombian justice minister, who had been cracking down on the Medellín cartel.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major campaign against the Medellín cartel. Escobar\'s empire began to crumble, and many of his associates were arrested or killed.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and brutal leader who was responsible for thousands of deaths and suffering. However, he was also a charismatic figure who was able to build a vast and powerful organization, and who became a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a fascinating and intriguing figure, and his story continues to captivate audiences around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-06 10:53:00', '2026-05-06 10:53:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-06 10:53:23', '2026-05-06 10:53:23'),
(2813, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon business/creator on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing my true self and living my best life. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Being different is what makes me special\n* My fiery personality is an asset, not a liability\n* I don\'t have to hide my true nature to fit in\n* My scales may be tough, but they also shine like diamonds\n* I\'m not just a creature, I\'m a symbol of power and strength\n\n#DragonPride #EmbracingMyTrueSelf #FireAndIce #TrendingNow #DragonSquad #MythicalCreatures #FantasyBeings #Legendary #FacebookFamous #DragonLove\"', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-06 11:18:00', '2026-05-06 11:18:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-06 11:18:21', '2026-05-06 11:18:21'),
(2814, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:00', 'Happy Birthday Komal. May your special day be filled with love, laughter, and all your favorite things. Wishing you a year ahead that\'s bright, happy, and fulfilling.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-06 12:00:00', '2026-05-06 12:00:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Happy_Birthday_Komal?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 29, '2026-05-06 12:00:25', '2026-05-06 12:00:25'),
(2815, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-tailored suit in black, navy, or gray is a classic choice for formal parties.\n2. **Tuxedos**: For black-tie events, a tuxedo is a must-have. Choose from single-breasted or double-breasted styles.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: Pair a dress shirt with a suit or tuxedo for a sharp, formal look.\n4. **Bow Ties**: Add a touch of elegance with a bow tie in a variety of patterns and colors.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A blazer with a dress shirt and trousers is a versatile and stylish option.\n2. **Dress Pants**: Choose from a range of colors and fabrics, such as wool or cotton.\n3. **Button-Down Shirts**: A button-down shirt with a blazer or dress pants is a great semi-formal look.\n4. **Loafers**: Slip-on loafers or dress shoes add a touch of sophistication.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans with a dress shirt or a casual button-down shirt is a great casual party look.\n2. **Polos**: A polo shirt with jeans or dress pants is a classic casual option.\n3. **Hoodies**: For a more relaxed party, a hoodie with jeans or sweatpants is a comfortable choice.\n4. **Sneakers**: Pair sneakers with jeans or dress pants for a casual, stylish look.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Watches**: A leather-strapped watch or a metal watch adds a touch of elegance.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Add a personal touch with cufflinks in a variety of designs and materials.\n3. **Pocket Squares**: A pocket square in a contrasting color adds a pop of color to a suit or blazer.\n4. **Belt**: A leather belt in a neutral color complements a suit or dress pants.\n\n**Grooming:**\n\n1. **Hairstyle**: Style your hair with a bit of product for a sleek, polished look.\n2. **Beard**: Trim your beard to add a touch of sophistication.\n3. **Fragrance**: Wear a subtle, elegant fragrance to complete your party look.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Choose an outfit that reflects your personal style and the occasion, and don\'t forget to add a few accessories to complete your look!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-06 12:40:00', '2026-05-06 12:40:27', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-06 12:40:27', '2026-05-06 12:40:27'),
(2816, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is designed to be worn on formal occasions, such as business meetings, job interviews, weddings, and other special events. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts typically have a point collar, spread collar, or wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or barrel cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are usually made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the chest and waist.\n5. **Button-front**: Formal shirts typically have a button-front closure.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Classic fit**: A classic fit formal shirt is a traditional style that is loose-fitting and comfortable.\n2. **Slim fit**: A slim fit formal shirt is a more modern style that is designed to fit closely to the body.\n3. **Tailored fit**: A tailored fit formal shirt is a custom-made style that is designed to fit the individual\'s body perfectly.\n4. **Dress shirt**: A dress shirt is a type of formal shirt that is designed to be worn with a suit and tie.\n5. **Business casual**: A business casual formal shirt is a style that is designed to be worn in a more relaxed business setting.\n\n**Popular Colors:**\n\n1. **White**: A classic choice for formal shirts, white is a timeless and versatile color.\n2. **Light blue**: A light blue formal shirt is a popular choice for business and formal events.\n3. **Pastel colors**: Pastel colors such as pale pink, baby blue, and mint green are popular for formal shirts.\n4. **Stripes**: Striped formal shirts are a classic style that can add visual interest to an outfit.\n5. **Checks**: Checked formal shirts are a popular choice for business casual events.\n\n**Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: A luxury brand that offers high-quality formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand that offers bespoke formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: A classic American brand that offers traditional formal shirts.\n4. **Armani**: A luxury brand that offers stylish and modern formal shirts.\n5. **Hugo Boss**: A German brand that offers high-quality formal shirts with a modern twist.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Choose a fit that flatters your body**: Make sure to choose a formal shirt that fits your body well, as a poor fit can ruin the overall look.\n2. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a formal shirt that is appropriate for the occasion, such as a white shirt for a wedding or a light blue shirt for a business meeting.\n3. **Pay attention to details**: Look for high-quality details such as stitching, buttons, and cuffs to ensure that your formal shirt looks professional and polished.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-06 12:56:00', '2026-05-06 12:56:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-06 12:56:23', '2026-05-06 12:56:23'),
(2817, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a symbol of strength, courage, and resilience, dragons have long fascinated human imagination. Here are a few key takeaways from the dragon\'s perspective:\n\n* **Courage in the face of adversity**: Just like a dragon faces its challenges head-on, we too can learn to be brave and overcome obstacles in our own lives.\n* **Passion and drive**: A dragon\'s fiery spirit can teach us about the importance of pursuing our passions and staying motivated.\n* **Protection and care**: Dragons are often depicted as guardians of treasure and wisdom, reminding us of the value of safeguarding our own resources and knowledge.\n\n#DragonEnergy #MotivationMonday #CourageOverFear #ResilienceMatters #TrendingNow #Inspiration #ProfessionalGrowth #FacebookCommunity #LessonsFromMythology #DragonSlayingGoals #FireUpYourPassion', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-06 13:03:00', '2026-05-06 13:03:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Women_Sandel?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-05-06 13:03:18', '2026-05-06 13:03:18'),
