(2846, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a powerful and majestic creature, I\'ve learned a thing or two about what it takes to succeed. Here are a few key takeaways:\n\n* **Embracing your inner fire**: Don\'t be afraid to let your passions burn bright and drive you forward.\n* **Soaring to new heights**: Set ambitious goals and work tirelessly to achieve them.\n* **Protecting your treasure**: Prioritize what\'s truly important to you and defend it with courage and determination.\n* **Breathing life into your community**: Use your unique gifts and talents to make a positive impact on those around you.\n\n#DragonsOfFacebook #MotivationMonday #BusinessTips #SuccessMindset #TrendingNow #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalDevelopment #MajesticCreatures #FireBreathingInspiration\"', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-07 10:35:00', '2026-05-07 10:35:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-07 10:35:20', '2026-05-07 10:35:20'),
(2847, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious organized crime groups in history. He is often referred to as the \"King of Cocaine\" due to his dominance of the global cocaine trade during the 1980s.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He grew up in a rough neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in petty crime and eventually graduated to more serious offenses, such as car theft and robbery. In the 1970s, Escobar began to focus on the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia.\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was swift and ruthless. He formed alliances with other traffickers, including Carlos Lehder, and began to expand his operations, using violence and intimidation to eliminate competitors and consolidate his control over the cocaine trade. By the early 1980s, Escobar had become one of the most powerful men in Colombia, with a vast network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers at his disposal.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, which Escobar led, was a highly organized and efficient operation that controlled every aspect of the cocaine trade, from production to distribution. The cartel\'s smugglers used a variety of methods to transport cocaine into the United States, including planes, boats, and even submarines. Once in the US, the cocaine was distributed to a network of dealers and wholesalers, who sold it to consumers.\n\nAt the height of its power, the Medellín cartel was estimated to be earning over $20 billion per year, making it one of the most profitable organized crime groups in history. Escobar\'s personal wealth was estimated to be over $30 billion, which is equivalent to over $60 billion today.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by extreme violence and terror. He and his associates were responsible for numerous bombings, assassinations, and massacres, including the killing of politicians, judges, and police officers. Escobar also ordered the murder of thousands of innocent people, including civilians, who were caught in the crossfire of his battles with rival cartels and law enforcement.\n\nIn 1989, Escobar\'s men bombed a commercial airliner, killing 110 people, in an attempt to intimidate the Colombian government into granting him amnesty. The bombing was one of the deadliest terrorist attacks in Colombian history, and it marked a turning point in the government\'s efforts to capture Escobar.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the US, launched a major operation to capture Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he continued to run his empire from behind bars. In 1992, he escaped from prison and went into hiding, sparking a massive manhunt.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death. Escobar\'s death marked the end of an era in the cocaine trade, and it paved the way for the rise of other cartels, including the Cali cartel.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. On the one hand, he was a ruthless and violent individual who was responsible for thousands of deaths and untold suffering. On the other hand, he was a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization from scratch.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" While these depictions often romanticize Escobar\'s life and exploits, they also serve as a reminder of the devastating impact of the cocaine trade on individuals, communities, and societies around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-07 10:45:00', '2026-05-07 10:45:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-07 10:45:25', '2026-05-07 10:45:25'),
(2848, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. He grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in crime at a young age. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working as a car thief and smuggler.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working for the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder. He quickly rose through the ranks, becoming a key player in the organization. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness made him a natural leader, and he eventually took over the cartel.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and profitable drug trafficking organizations in the world. The cartel smuggled vast quantities of cocaine into the United States, earning Escobar an estimated $30 billion per year. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality, and he was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including law enforcement officials, politicians, and rival gang members.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for several high-profile crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Galán, a Colombian presidential candidate who had vowed to crack down on the Medellín cartel.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s organization bombed a commercial airliner, killing 110 people.\n3. **The assassination of Judge Carlos Valencia**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Valencia, a judge who had been investigating the Medellín cartel.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down by Colombian police on December 1, 1993. He was shot and killed in a shootout with police in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime boss who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people. However, he is also remembered as a folk hero in some parts of Colombia, where he was seen as a champion of the poor and a symbol of resistance against the government.\n\n**Popular Culture**\n\nEscobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including:\n\n1. **Narcos**: A Netflix series that dramatizes Escobar\'s life and the rise of the Medellín cartel.\n2. **Escobar: Paradise Lost**: A film that tells the story of Escobar\'s life and death.\n3. **Killing Pablo**: A book by Mark Bowden that chronicles the hunt for Escobar and his eventual death.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy are a testament to the enduring power of crime and corruption, and the devastating consequences of the drug trade.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-07 10:50:00', '2026-05-07 10:50:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-07 10:50:18', '2026-05-07 10:50:18'),
(2849, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and infamous drug trafficking organizations in history. He was born in Rionegro, Colombia, and rose to prominence in the 1970s and 1980s as a major player in the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a small-time smuggler and thief, but he quickly gained notoriety and wealth through his involvement in the cocaine trade. He formed the Medellín cartel, which became one of the largest and most powerful drug trafficking organizations in the world. At the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest people in the world.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his ruthless tactics and his willingness to use violence to eliminate his enemies and maintain control over his empire. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, politicians, and rival drug traffickers. His organization was also responsible for numerous bombings, kidnappings, and assassinations.\n\n**The \"King of Cocaine\"**\n\nEscobar\'s success in the cocaine trade earned him the nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) or \"The King of Cocaine.\" He was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning numerous properties, cars, and airplanes. He also invested heavily in sports teams, including the Atlético Nacional soccer team, and was a major supporter of the Colombian national soccer team.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral, which he had designed himself. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and brutal crime lord who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and cunning figure who was able to build a vast empire and evade capture for many years. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which chronicles his rise and fall.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of animals and had a private zoo at his estate, Hacienda Napoles, which included giraffes, elephants, and hippos.\n* He was a major supporter of the poor and was known for his charitable donations to local communities.\n* Escobar was a skilled businessman and invested in numerous legitimate businesses, including real estate, construction, and agriculture.\n* He was a skilled pilot and owned several airplanes, including a Learjet and a helicopter.\n* Escobar\'s death was celebrated by many Colombians, who saw him as a symbol of the country\'s corruption and violence. However, his legacy continues to be felt in Colombia, and his story remains a fascinating and complex chapter in the country\'s history.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-07 10:53:00', '2026-05-07 10:53:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-07 10:53:20', '2026-05-07 10:53:20'),
(2850, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon**\n\nAs a symbol of power, strength, and resilience, the dragon has long been a fascinating creature. Here are a few key takeaways from the dragon\'s approach to life:\n\n* **Courage in the face of adversity**: Dragons are known for their fearlessness and bravery, reminding us to stand up for ourselves and face challenges head-on.\n* **Passion and drive**: With a fiery spirit, dragons embody the importance of pursuing our passions and staying motivated.\n* **Protection and loyalty**: As guardians of treasure and territory, dragons demonstrate the value of defending what\'s important to us and being loyal to those we care about.\n* **Adaptability and growth**: From sea serpents to sky-dwelling beasts, dragons have evolved over time, teaching us to be flexible and open to change.\n\n#DragonsOfFacebook #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #BusinessLessons #MythicalCreatures #ProfessionalDevelopment #Inspiration #CourageOverFear #PassionDriven #LoyaltyMatters #GrowthMindset #FacebookBusiness', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-07 11:18:00', '2026-05-07 11:18:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-07 11:18:21', '2026-05-07 11:18:21'),
(2851, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'When it comes to party wear for men, there are many stylish and fashionable options to choose from. Here are some popular and trendy ideas:\n\n**Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Suits:** A well-fitted suit in black, navy, or gray is a classic choice for formal parties. Pair it with a crisp white shirt, a slim tie, and polished dress shoes.\n2. **Tuxedos:** A tuxedo is perfect for black-tie events or luxurious parties. Opt for a classic black tuxedo with a white shirt, black bow tie, and patent leather shoes.\n3. **Dress Shirts:** A dress shirt with a slim collar and cuffs is a great option for formal parties. Choose from a variety of colors and patterns, such as stripes or checks.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Blazers:** A blazer with a dress shirt and dark jeans is a stylish and versatile option for semi-formal parties.\n2. **Dress Pants:** Dress pants in gray, navy, or beige are a great alternative to jeans. Pair them with a dress shirt and a blazer or a leather jacket.\n3. **Polos:** A polo shirt with dress pants or dark jeans is a great option for a more casual party.\n\n**Casual Party Wear:**\n\n1. **Graphic T-Shirts:** A graphic t-shirt with distressed denim jeans and sneakers is a great option for a casual party.\n2. **Hoodies:** A hoodie with sweatpants or joggers is perfect for a relaxed and casual party.\n3. **Leather Jackets:** A leather jacket with a t-shirt and jeans is a stylish and edgy option for a casual party.\n\n**Accessories:**\n\n1. **Watches:** A leather strap watch or a metal watch is a great accessory to add a touch of sophistication to your outfit.\n2. **Cufflinks:** Cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to your dress shirt.\n3. **Sunglasses:** Sunglasses can add a cool and stylish touch to your outfit.\n4. **Hats:** A fedora or a panama hat can add a stylish touch to your outfit.\n\n**Grooming:**\n\n1. **Hair:** Style your hair with a pomade or a hair wax to add a touch of sophistication.\n2. **Beard:** Trim your beard to add a touch of elegance to your outfit.\n3. **Fragrance:** Wear a fragrance that complements your outfit and personality.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to be confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Experiment with different styles and find what works best for you!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-07 12:40:00', '2026-05-07 12:40:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-07 12:40:23', '2026-05-07 12:40:23'),
(2852, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of dress shirt that is typically worn for business or formal occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Types of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress Shirt:** A classic, collared shirt with a button-front closure, typically made of cotton or a cotton-blend fabric.\n2. **Business Shirt:** A slightly more casual version of the dress shirt, often with a relaxed fit and a softer collar.\n3. **Tuxedo Shirt:** A formal, black-tie shirt with a wingtip collar and French cuffs, typically worn with a tuxedo or dinner jacket.\n4. **Dress Shirt with Contrast Cuffs:** A dress shirt with contrasting cuffs and collar, often in a bold color or pattern.\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar Style:** Formal shirts often have a point collar, spread collar, or wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff Style:** Formal shirts may have French cuffs, button cuffs, or barrel cuffs.\n3. **Fabric:** Formal shirts are typically made of high-quality cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit:** Formal shirts are usually tailored to fit closely, with a slim cut through the body and sleeves.\n5. **Button-Down or Button-Front:** Formal shirts may have a button-down collar or a button-front closure.\n\n**Popular Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink:** Known for their high-quality, classic dress shirts.\n2. **Charvet:** A French luxury brand offering exquisite, handmade dress shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers:** An American brand famous for their classic, two-button dress shirts.\n4. **Ted Baker:** A British brand offering stylish, high-quality dress shirts with a twist.\n5. **Armani:** An Italian luxury brand providing sleek, modern dress shirts.\n\n**Tips for Choosing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the occasion:** Choose a shirt that matches the formality of the event.\n2. **Think about your skin tone:** Select a shirt color that complements your skin tone.\n3. **Pay attention to fit:** Ensure the shirt fits well, with a slim cut through the body and sleeves.\n4. **Accessories matter:** Pair your shirt with a quality tie, cufflinks, and shoes to complete the look.\n\nRemember, a formal shirt is an essential component of a man\'s wardrobe, and choosing the right one can make a significant difference in his overall appearance and confidence.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-07 12:56:00', '2026-05-07 12:56:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-07 12:56:21', '2026-05-07 12:56:21'),
