(2943, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a powerful dragon, I understand the importance of staying on top of your game. Here are a few key takeaways to help you soar to new heights:\n\n* Set clear goals and priorities to focus your energy\n* Surround yourself with a supportive community that encourages growth\n* Continuously learn and adapt to stay ahead of the curve\n* Take calculated risks to challenge yourself and achieve greatness\n* Remember to take breaks and practice self-care to maintain your inner fire\n\nBy following these principles, you\'ll be unstoppable! #DragonMode #BusinessTips #ProductivityHacks #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #SuccessStory #EntrepreneurLife #LeadershipGoals #InspirationalQuotes\"', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-10 10:35:00', '2026-05-10 10:35:17', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-10 10:35:17', '2026-05-10 10:35:17'),
(2944, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most successful and infamous criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life and Career:**\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began his life of crime on the streets of Medellín, selling stolen cars and other contraband. In the 1970s, he started working for a local cocaine smuggler, eventually becoming a key player in the Medellín cartel.\n\n**Rise to Power:**\nEscobar\'s success in the cocaine trade was swift and dramatic. He built a vast network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers, and his cartel became one of the largest and most powerful in the world. At the height of his power, Escobar was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation:**\nEscobar was known for his ruthless tactics and brutal violence. He ordered the murders of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, judges, and rival gang members. He also used intimidation and bribery to maintain control over his empire.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel:**\nThe Medellín cartel, led by Escobar, dominated the global cocaine trade in the 1980s. The cartel\'s operations were highly organized and sophisticated, with a complex network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine supply.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar:**\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a massive manhunt for Escobar. The search was led by the Colombian police, with support from the US DEA and other international agencies.\n\n**Death:**\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old. The killing of Escobar marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror and had a significant impact on the global cocaine trade.\n\n**Legacy:**\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was a brutal and ruthless criminal, he was also a charismatic leader and a shrewd businessman. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts:**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a mansion with a private airport.\n* He was a skilled politician and was elected to the Colombian Congress in 1982.\n* Escobar was a devout Catholic and built a church in Medellín, which still stands today.\n* He was known for his generosity to the poor and was often referred to as \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) by the people of Medellín.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy are a fascinating and disturbing reminder of the power and brutality of organized crime.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-10 10:45:00', '2026-05-10 10:45:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-10 10:45:25', '2026-05-10 10:45:25'),
(2945, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He grew up in a rough neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and violence at a young age. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working as a car thief and smuggler.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to build his drug empire, initially smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose to prominence in the Medellín cartel, which was founded by his cousin, Gustavo Gaviria. Escobar\'s charisma, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him to consolidate power and eventually become the leader of the cartel.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, with Escobar estimated to be earning over $420 million per week at the height of his power. The cartel\'s operations were characterized by brutality, violence, and corruption, with Escobar using intimidation, murder, and bribery to maintain control.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the murder of Galán, who was a leading candidate in the Colombian presidential election.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s henchmen planted a bomb on an Avianca airliner, killing 110 people.\n3. **The murder of Colombian police officers**: Escobar\'s cartel was responsible for the murder of hundreds of Colombian police officers, who were seen as a threat to the cartel\'s operations.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, he continued to run his empire from behind bars and eventually escaped in 1992. A massive manhunt was launched, with Colombian and American authorities working together to capture Escobar.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the global cocaine trade, and his legacy continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the failures of the war on drugs and the corrupting influence of power and wealth. His story has been immortalized in numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-10 10:50:00', '2026-05-10 10:50:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-10 10:50:24', '2026-05-10 10:50:24'),
(2946, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He was the third of seven children, and his family was considered lower-middle-class. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and a lack of opportunities, which may have contributed to his later involvement in crime.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s entry into the world of crime began in the 1970s, when he started selling cocaine on the streets of Medellín. He quickly rose through the ranks of the local underworld, becoming a key player in the city\'s burgeoning cocaine trade. In the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín cartel, which would go on to become one of the most powerful and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, with estimated annual revenues of over $20 billion. The cartel\'s operations were characterized by brutal violence, intimidation, and corruption, with Escobar and his associates using any means necessary to eliminate rivals, law enforcement, and anyone else who stood in their way.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: Escobar ordered the murder of Galán, a leading candidate in the 1989 presidential election, in an effort to prevent him from cracking down on the cartel.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s henchmen planted a bomb on an Avianca flight, killing 110 people, in an attempt to kill a key witness against the cartel.\n3. **The murder of Colombian police chief Colonel Jaime Ramírez Gómez**: Escobar ordered the assassination of Ramírez, who had been leading the effort to capture him.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a luxurious private prison, which he had built himself. However, he escaped in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, with the Colombian government and the US Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) working together to capture him.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of an era in the global cocaine trade, and his legacy continues to be felt in Colombia and around the world.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord, responsible for countless deaths and suffering. However, he is also seen as a folk hero by some in Colombia, who view him as a symbol of resistance against the government and the establishment. His life and times have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-10 10:53:00', '2026-05-10 10:53:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-10 10:53:18', '2026-05-10 10:53:18'),
(2947, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Journey**\n\nAs a symbol of strength, courage, and resilience, I, a dragon, have learned valuable lessons that can be applied to our personal and professional lives. Here are a few key takeaways:\n\n* **Believe in yourself**: Just like a dragon\'s roar can be heard from miles away, our confidence and self-belief can make a lasting impact on those around us.\n* **Protect and nurture**: Dragons are known to fiercely protect their treasure and loved ones. Similarly, we should prioritize our well-being, relationships, and passions.\n* **Evolve and adapt**: As a mythical creature, I\'ve had to adapt to changing environments and circumstances. This ability to evolve is crucial in today\'s fast-paced world.\n* **Leave a legacy**: A dragon\'s legacy can be seen in the stories and legends that live on long after they\'re gone. What will your legacy be?\n\n#DragonInspiration #MotivationMonday #PersonalGrowth #ProfessionalDevelopment #ConfidenceIsKey #WellnessWednesday #AdaptabilityMatters #LegacyBuilding #TrendingNow #FacebookInspiration #MythicalMotivation #BusinessLessonsFromADragon', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-10 11:18:00', '2026-05-10 11:18:15', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-10 11:18:15', '2026-05-10 11:18:15'),
(2948, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', '**Party Wear for Men: A Guide to Dressing Up**\n\nWhen it comes to party wear for men, the options are endless. From formal suits to stylish casual wear, there\'s a wide range of choices to suit every taste and occasion. Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n### Formal Party Wear\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-tailored suit is a classic choice for formal parties. You can opt for a black, navy, or gray suit, and pair it with a crisp white shirt and a tie.\n2. **Tuxedos**: If you want to make a statement, a tuxedo is the way to go. It\'s perfect for black-tie events and can be paired with a bow tie and a cummerbund.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A dress shirt with a slim fit and a wingtip collar is a great option for formal parties. You can pair it with a suit or a blazer.\n\n### Casual Party Wear\n\n1. **Dress Pants**: Dress pants in bold colors or patterns can add a touch of elegance to your outfit. You can pair them with a casual shirt and a blazer.\n2. **Button-Down Shirts**: A button-down shirt in a bold color or pattern is a great option for casual parties. You can pair it with jeans or dress pants.\n3. **Blazers**: A blazer can instantly elevate your outfit and make you look stylish. You can pair it with a dress shirt and jeans or dress pants.\n\n### Accessories\n\n1. **Watches**: A watch can add a touch of sophistication to your outfit. Opt for a leather strap or a metal band.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks can add a touch of elegance to your shirt. Opt for simple or patterned cufflinks.\n3. **Shoes**: Shoes can make or break your outfit. Opt for dress shoes, loafers, or boots, depending on the occasion.\n\n### Tips\n\n1. **Dress according to the occasion**: Make sure you dress according to the occasion. If it\'s a formal party, opt for a suit or a tuxedo. If it\'s a casual party, opt for dress pants and a casual shirt.\n2. **Pay attention to fit**: Make sure your clothes fit well. A well-tailored outfit can make you look stylish and confident.\n3. **Accessories can make a difference**: Accessories like watches, cufflinks, and shoes can add a touch of elegance to your outfit.\n\n**Some popular party wear styles for men include:**\n\n1. **Slim Fit**: Slim fit clothes are a popular choice for men. They create a streamlined look and can make you look stylish and confident.\n2. **Streetwear**: Streetwear is a popular choice for casual parties. It includes clothes like graphic t-shirts, jeans, and sneakers.\n3. **Luxury**: Luxury party wear includes high-end suits, tuxedos, and accessories. It\'s perfect for formal events and can make you look sophisticated and elegant.\n\nRemember, party wear for men is all about expressing your personal style and having fun. Experiment with different styles, accessories, and colors to find what works best for you.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-10 12:40:00', '2026-05-10 12:40:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-10 12:40:24', '2026-05-10 12:40:24'),
(2949, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, or special occasions. Here are some key characteristics of a formal shirt for men:\n\n**Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a point collar, spread collar, or a wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or button cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality cotton or cotton-blend fabrics, such as Oxford cloth, pinpoint, or twill.\n4. **Weave**: The weave of the fabric is usually tight and smooth, giving the shirt a crisp and formal appearance.\n5. **Color**: Formal shirts are often white, light blue, or pale pink, although other colors like lavender or yellow can also be suitable for formal events.\n6. **Pockets**: Formal shirts usually do not have pockets, or have a small breast pocket.\n7. **Buttons**: Formal shirts often have mother-of-pearl or plastic buttons.\n\n**Types of formal shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a point collar and French cuffs.\n2. **Business shirt**: A formal shirt with a spread collar and button cuffs.\n3. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and French cuffs, designed to be worn with a tuxedo.\n4. **Dinner shirt**: A formal shirt with a detachable collar and cuffs, often worn for formal dinners.\n\n**How to wear a formal shirt:**\n\n1. **Pair with a suit**: A formal shirt is typically worn with a suit and tie for business or formal events.\n2. **Choose the right tie**: Select a tie that complements the color and pattern of the shirt.\n3. **Add a pocket square**: A pocket square can add a touch of elegance to a formal outfit.\n4. **Ensure a good fit**: Make sure the shirt fits well and is not too loose or too tight.\n\n**Brands:**\n\nSome popular brands that offer high-quality formal shirts for men include:\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**\n2. **Charvet**\n3. **Brooks Brothers**\n4. **Ralph Lauren**\n5. **Armani**\n\nRemember, a formal shirt is a versatile and essential item in a man\'s wardrobe, and can be dressed up or down depending on the occasion.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-10 12:56:00', '2026-05-10 12:56:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-10 12:56:22', '2026-05-10 12:56:22'),
