(3000, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:33', 'Football, also known as soccer in some countries, is a sport played between two teams of 11 players using a round ball with the objective of scoring more goals than the opposing team by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent\'s goal.\n\nHere are some key aspects of football:\n\n1. **Objective**: The objective of football is to score more goals than the opposing team within the 90-minute playing time.\n2. **Gameplay**: The game starts with a kick-off, where one team kicks the ball to the other team. Players can use any part of their body except their hands and arms to control and move the ball. Only the goalkeeper is allowed to use their hands and arms to touch the ball.\n3. **Scoring**: A goal is scored when the ball passes the goal line between the goal posts and under the crossbar.\n4. **Positions**: Each team has 11 players with different positions:\n	* Goalkeeper (GK): protects the goal\n	* Defenders (DF): defend the goal and support the goalkeeper\n	* Midfielders (MF): support both the defenders and the forwards\n	* Forwards (FW): score goals\n5. **Tactics**: Teams use various tactics to outmaneuver their opponents, such as formations, passing, dribbling, and shooting.\n6. **Rules**: The game is governed by a set of rules, including offside, fouls, and penalties.\n\nSome of the most popular football competitions include:\n\n1. **FIFA World Cup**: an international tournament held every four years\n2. **UEFA Champions League**: a European club competition\n3. **English Premier League**: a professional league in England\n4. **La Liga**: a professional league in Spain\n5. **Copa America**: a South American international tournament\n\nFootball is a popular sport with a massive global following, and its popularity continues to grow.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-11 16:33:00', '2026-05-11 16:33:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/bicycle_kick_hitting_the_top_right_corner?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 53, '2026-05-11 16:33:16', '2026-05-11 16:33:16'),
(3001, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:42', 'The Yamaha R1 is a high-performance sport bike produced by Yamaha Motor Company. It was first introduced in 1998 and has since become one of the most popular and iconic sport bikes on the market.\n\nHere are some key features and specs of the Yamaha R1:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Engine:** 998cc, liquid-cooled, 4-stroke, DOHC, 16-valve, in-line four-cylinder engine.\n2. **Power:** 200 horsepower (147.9 kW) at 13,500 rpm.\n3. **Torque:** 82.6 lb-ft (112 Nm) at 11,500 rpm.\n4. **Transmission:** 6-speed, constant mesh.\n5. **Brakes:** Dual 320mm discs with 4-piston calipers (front), 220mm disc with 2-piston caliper (rear).\n6. **Suspension:** 43mm inverted fork (front), link-type monoshock (rear).\n7. **Weight:** 439 lbs (199 kg) wet weight.\n8. **Seat Height:** 32.7 inches (831 mm).\n\n**Riding Modes:**\n\nThe Yamaha R1 features several riding modes, including:\n\n1. **Track Mode:** Designed for track use, this mode provides maximum power and minimal electronic intervention.\n2. **Street Mode:** Suitable for everyday riding, this mode provides a balance of power and traction control.\n3. **Rain Mode:** Designed for low-traction conditions, this mode reduces power and increases traction control.\n\n**Electronic Features:**\n\nThe R1 features a range of electronic rider aids, including:\n\n1. **Traction Control:** Helps prevent wheelspin and loss of traction.\n2. **Slide Control:** Helps prevent excessive wheelspin and slide.\n3. **Lift Control:** Helps prevent wheelies and loss of traction.\n4. **Brake Control:** Helps prevent wheel lockup and loss of traction during braking.\n5. **Quick Shift:** Allows for clutchless upshifts and downshifts.\n\n**Design and Styling:**\n\nThe Yamaha R1 has a sleek and aggressive design, with a focus on aerodynamics and ergonomics. The bike features a compact, lightweight chassis and a range of styling elements, including:\n\n1. **Aerodynamic Fairing:** Designed to reduce wind resistance and improve airflow.\n2. **LED Headlights:** Provide improved visibility and a distinctive look.\n3. **Digital Instrumentation:** Features a range of displays, including speed, rpm, gear position, and more.\n\nOverall, the Yamaha R1 is a high-performance sport bike that is designed for experienced riders who demand the best in terms of power, handling, and technology.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-11 16:42:00', '2026-05-11 16:42:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/r1_bike?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 54, '2026-05-11 16:42:20', '2026-05-11 16:42:20'),
(3002, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:30', 'Iron Man is a fictional superhero appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The character was created by writer and editor Stan Lee, and artists Don Heck and Jack Kirby.\n\n**Origin Story:**\nTony Stark, a billionaire inventor and industrialist, is the alter ego of Iron Man. After being kidnapped and held captive by a terrorist group, Stark is forced to build a powerful suit of armor to escape. He uses this technology to create a more advanced suit, which he wears to fight crime and protect the world as Iron Man.\n\n**Powers and Abilities:**\nIron Man\'s powers come from his advanced suit of armor, which provides him with:\n\n1. Superhuman strength and durability\n2. Flight capabilities\n3. Energy projection and repulsor technology\n4. Advanced sensors and tracking systems\n5. Enhanced cognitive abilities through his AI assistant, JARVIS (later replaced by FRIDAY)\n\n**Personality:**\nTony Stark, aka Iron Man, is a complex and charismatic character. He is:\n\n1. Highly intelligent and resourceful\n2. Confident and arrogant, often to a fault\n3. A self-proclaimed genius and billionaire playboy\n4. Haunted by his past mistakes and struggles with anxiety and PTSD\n\n**Movie Franchise:**\nThe Iron Man movie franchise, starring Robert Downey Jr. as Tony Stark/Iron Man, has been incredibly successful. The films include:\n\n1. Iron Man (2008)\n2. Iron Man 2 (2010)\n3. Iron Man 3 (2013)\n4. Avengers: Age of Ultron (2015)\n5. Captain America: Civil War (2016)\n6. Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017)\n7. Avengers: Infinity War (2018)\n8. Avengers: Endgame (2019)\n\n**Legacy:**\nIron Man has become an iconic superhero, inspiring countless fans around the world. The character\'s legacy extends beyond the comics and movies, with themes of innovation, perseverance, and redemption resonating with audiences of all ages.\n\nWhat aspect of Iron Man would you like to know more about? The comics, the movies, or something else?', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-11 17:30:00', '2026-05-11 17:30:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/iron_man?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 55, '2026-05-11 17:30:19', '2026-05-11 17:30:19'),
