(3011, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Unlock the Fire Within: 5 Key Takeaways from a Dragon\'s Perspective**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about resilience, adaptability, and passion. Here are some relatable points to help you unleash your inner fire:\n\n* **Embracing challenges**: Just like how I face fierce storms and treacherous landscapes, you too can overcome obstacles by staying focused and determined.\n* **Protecting your treasure**: Whether it\'s your time, energy, or resources, learn to prioritize and safeguard what\'s truly important to you.\n* **Breathing fire**: Don\'t be afraid to speak your mind and express yourself authentically – it\'s a powerful way to connect with others and leave a lasting impact.\n* **Soaring to new heights**: Continuously strive for growth and improvement, just as I do when I take to the skies and explore new territories.\n* **Hoarding knowledge**: Stay curious, keep learning, and accumulate wisdom – it\'s a treasure that will serve you well throughout your journey.\n\n#DragonInspiration #MotivationMonday #FireWithin #Resilience #GrowthMindset #ProductivityHacks #SelfImprovement #TrendingNow #FacebookMotivation #InspirationalQuotes #PersonalGrowth #ProfessionalDevelopment #SuccessTips', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-12 10:35:00', '2026-05-12 10:35:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-12 10:35:20', '2026-05-12 10:35:20'),
(3012, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful criminals in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. He grew up in a humble household with his parents and siblings. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and limited opportunities, which may have contributed to his involvement in crime.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his criminal career in the 1970s, initially involved in car theft and smuggling. He eventually turned to cocaine trafficking, which would become his main source of income. In the early 1980s, Escobar partnered with other Colombian traffickers to form the Medellín cartel, which quickly became one of the largest and most powerful cocaine cartels in the world.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, smuggling massive quantities of the drug into the United States, Europe, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s cunning, ruthlessness, and strategic thinking. He established a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers, and used violence and intimidation to maintain control over his empire.\n\n**Notorious Crimes**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán** (1989): Escobar ordered the killing of Galán, who had vowed to crack down on the Medellín cartel.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203** (1989): Escobar\'s cartel planted a bomb on the plane, killing 110 people, in an attempt to kill a potential witness against him.\n3. **The murder of Colombian police officers and judges**: Escobar\'s cartel targeted and killed numerous law enforcement officials and judges who were investigating or prosecuting his organization.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility, known as the \"Cathedral.\" However, he continued to run his cartel from behind bars and eventually escaped in 1992. A massive manhunt ensued, with Colombian and American authorities working together to capture Escobar.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in Medellín, during a rooftop shootout. His death marked the end of an era for the Medellín cartel, and his legacy continues to fascinate and horrify people around the world.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s life and crimes have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story serves as a cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime and the devastating consequences of the drug trade. Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a complex and intriguing figure, symbolizing both the darker aspects of human nature and the enduring power of ambition and greed.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-12 10:45:00', '2026-05-12 10:45:28', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-12 10:45:28', '2026-05-12 10:45:28'),
(3013, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious cartels in the history of organized crime. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a poor family and was raised in the city of Medellín, where he became involved in street crime at a young age. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty, violence, and a lack of opportunities, which would later shape his motivations and actions.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power began in the 1970s, when he started working as a small-time smuggler and thief. He quickly gained a reputation for his cunning, ruthlessness, and ability to evade law enforcement. In the early 1980s, Escobar partnered with other Colombian traffickers to form the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared cartels in the world.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, smuggling massive quantities of the drug into the United States, Europe, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s innovative tactics, including the use of airplanes, submarines, and other sophisticated smuggling methods.\n\nEscobar\'s organization was also known for its brutality and violence. He ordered the murders of countless people, including rival traffickers, law enforcement officials, politicians, and innocent civilians. The Medellín Cartel\'s reign of terror was marked by bombings, assassinations, and kidnappings, which created a climate of fear and intimidation in Colombia and beyond.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The pursuit of Escobar became a national obsession in Colombia, with the government offering large rewards for information leading to his capture.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death. The circumstances surrounding his death are still disputed, with some claiming that he was executed by the police, while others believe that he took his own life to avoid capture.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. At the same time, he is also seen as a symbol of the country\'s struggles with poverty, inequality, and corruption.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story has captivated audiences around the world, offering a glimpse into the dark and fascinating world of organized crime.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included owning a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a sprawling estate in Medellín.\n* He was a skilled politician and strategist, who used his charisma and wealth to build alliances and manipulate others.\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power, making him one of the richest people in the world.\n* He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including law enforcement officials, politicians, and innocent civilians.\n* Escobar\'s death marked the beginning of the end of the Medellín Cartel, which was eventually dismantled by the Colombian government and international law enforcement agencies.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-12 10:50:00', '2026-05-12 10:50:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-12 10:50:19', '2026-05-12 10:50:19'),
(3014, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and powerful crime lords of all time.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and behavior.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his criminal career in the 1970s, initially as a car thief and a smuggler of goods. He quickly moved into the cocaine trade, which was booming in Colombia at the time. In the early 1980s, Escobar partnered with other Colombian traffickers to form the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, smuggling massive quantities of the drug into the United States, Europe, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s innovative and ruthless business tactics, including the use of violence and intimidation to eliminate competitors and law enforcement officials.\n\n**Violence and Terror**\n\nEscobar was known for his brutal tactics, including the use of bombings, assassinations, and kidnappings. He was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, politicians, and civilians. In 1989, Escobar\'s henchmen bombed an Avianca Airlines plane, killing 110 people, in an attempt to kill a Colombian presidential candidate.\n\n**Personal Life**\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar was a complex and charismatic figure. He was known for his love of luxury and extravagance, and he built a lavish mansion, Hacienda Napoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars. Escobar was also a devoted family man and was particularly close to his mother, Hermilda.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and his empire began to crumble. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the country\'s struggle against poverty and inequality, and his story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known as \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) or \"Don Pablo\" by his associates and admirers.\n* He was a prolific builder and invested heavily in real estate, including the construction of homes, roads, and sports facilities in Medellín.\n* Escobar was a fan of soccer and owned a team, Atlético Nacional, which won several championships during his ownership.\n* He was known for his love of animals and kept a private zoo at Hacienda Napoles, which featured exotic animals such as hippos, giraffes, and elephants.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-12 10:53:00', '2026-05-12 10:53:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-12 10:53:23', '2026-05-12 10:53:23'),
(3015, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon business/creator on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing our true selves and living our best lives. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Be fearless and take risks - whether it\'s exploring new lands or trying new things, don\'t be afraid to step out of your comfort zone\n* Protect your treasure - whether it\'s your time, energy, or resources, make sure you\'re prioritizing what\'s truly important to you\n* Breathe fire into your passions - don\'t let your dreams and desires simmer, fan the flames and make them a reality\n* Surround yourself with a supportive tribe - having a community of like-minded individuals can make all the difference in your journey\n\n#DragonSquad #FireBreathingMotivation #TreasureYourTime #FearlessLiving #TrendingNow #DragonInspiration #ProfessionalDragon #BusinessOfBeingABoss #DragonLife\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of niche-specific (dragon-related) and trending hashtags to increase visibility and reach a wider audience.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-12 11:18:00', '2026-05-12 11:18:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-12 11:18:26', '2026-05-12 11:18:26'),
(3016, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:57', 'A pen is a writing instrument used to apply ink to a surface, typically paper, in order to write or draw. It consists of a nib or tip that delivers the ink, a reservoir to hold the ink, and a handle or body to hold the pen. Pens have been used for thousands of years and have evolved over time to include various types, such as:\n\n1. Ballpoint pens: These use a small rotating ball to dispense ink onto the paper.\n2. Rollerball pens: These use a small metal ball to dispense liquid ink onto the paper.\n3. Fountain pens: These use a nib to deliver ink from an internal reservoir to the paper.\n4. Gel pens: These use a water-based ink that is suspended in a gel-like substance.\n5. Felt-tip pens: These use a porous tip to absorb and release ink onto the paper.\n\nPens are commonly used for everyday writing, drawing, and signing documents. They come in a wide range of styles, sizes, and colors, and can be made from various materials, such as plastic, metal, or wood.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-12 11:57:00', '2026-05-12 11:57:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 16, '2026-05-12 11:57:21', '2026-05-12 11:57:21'),
(3017, 'Auto Post for instagram at 11:59', 'A \"pen packet\" is a small package or envelope that contains a set of pens, often with a specific theme or design. These packets usually include a variety of pens, such as ballpoint pens, gel pens, or rollerball pens, and may also include other stationery items like pencils, highlighters, or stickers.\n\nPen packets can be found in office supply stores, online marketplaces, or specialty stationery shops. They\'re often marketed as a convenient and portable way to carry a set of writing utensils, making them perfect for students, office workers, or artists on-the-go.\n\nSome common types of pen packets include:\n\n1. Variety packs: These packets contain a mix of different pen types, such as ballpoint, gel, and rollerball pens.\n2. Color packs: These packets feature pens in a range of colors, often with matching ink colors.\n3. Theme packs: These packets are designed around a specific theme, such as animals, flowers, or abstract designs.\n4. Brand packs: These packets feature pens from a particular brand, such as Pilot, Uni-ball, or Faber-Castell.\n\nOverall, pen packets are a fun and convenient way to collect and carry a set of pens, and they make great gifts for stationery enthusiasts or anyone who loves to write or draw.', '[\"instagram\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-12 11:59:00', '2026-05-12 11:59:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen_Packet?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 17, '2026-05-12 11:59:25', '2026-05-12 11:59:25'),
