(3074, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:33', 'Football, also known as soccer in some countries, is a popular team sport played between two teams of 11 players using a round ball with the objective of scoring more goals than the opposing team by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent\'s goal.\n\nHere are some key aspects of football:\n\n1. **Objective**: The primary objective of football is to score more goals than the opposing team within the allotted time (90 minutes, divided into two 45-minute halves).\n2. **Players**: Each team consists of 11 players, including a goalkeeper and 10 outfield players.\n3. **Equipment**: The game is played with a round ball, and players can use any part of their body except their hands and arms to control and move the ball.\n4. **Rules**: The game is governed by a set of rules, which include offside, fouls, free kicks, penalty kicks, and corner kicks.\n5. **Positions**: Players can be categorized into different positions, such as:\n	* Goalkeeper (GK)\n	* Defenders (DF)\n	* Midfielders (MF)\n	* Forwards (FW)\n6. **Tactics**: Teams employ various tactics, such as formations, strategies, and player movements, to outmaneuver their opponents and create scoring opportunities.\n7. **Competitions**: Football is played at various levels, including:\n	* Professional leagues (e.g., English Premier League, La Liga, Bundesliga)\n	* International tournaments (e.g., FIFA World Cup, UEFA European Championship)\n	* Club competitions (e.g., UEFA Champions League, Copa Libertadores)\n\nSome of the most popular football leagues and competitions include:\n\n1. **English Premier League** (EPL)\n2. **La Liga** (Spanish league)\n3. **Bundesliga** (German league)\n4. **Serie A** (Italian league)\n5. **FIFA World Cup**\n6. **UEFA Champions League**\n7. **Copa America**\n\nFootball is a widely popular sport, enjoyed by millions of fans worldwide, and is often considered a cultural phenomenon, with a significant impact on society, economy, and politics.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-13 16:33:00', '2026-05-13 16:33:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/bicycle_kick_hitting_the_top_right_corner?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 53, '2026-05-13 16:33:20', '2026-05-13 16:33:20'),
(3075, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:42', 'The R1 bike, also known as the Yamaha YZF-R1, is a high-performance sport bike produced by the Japanese manufacturer Yamaha. \n\nHere are some key features of the Yamaha R1:\n\n1. **Engine**: The R1 is powered by a 998cc, inline-four cylinder engine that produces around 200 horsepower.\n2. **Transmission**: The bike features a six-speed manual transmission with a multi-plate slipper clutch.\n3. **Chassis**: The R1 has a lightweight aluminum frame, with a swingarm and a fully adjustable suspension system.\n4. **Brakes**: The bike is equipped with dual 320mm front disc brakes and a 220mm rear disc brake, both with ABS (Anti-lock Braking System).\n5. **Electronics**: The R1 features advanced electronic systems, including traction control, wheelie control, and multiple ride modes (e.g., Sport, Standard, and Rain).\n6. **Design**: The bike has a sleek and aerodynamic design, with a distinctive Yamaha styling and a range of color options.\n\nThe Yamaha R1 is known for its exceptional performance, handling, and features, making it a popular choice among sport bike enthusiasts and professional racers. However, please note that the specifications and features may vary depending on the model year and region.\n\nWould you like to know more about the Yamaha R1 or is there something specific you\'d like to ask about this bike?', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-13 16:42:00', '2026-05-13 16:42:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/r1_bike?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 54, '2026-05-13 16:42:24', '2026-05-13 16:42:24'),
(3076, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:30', 'Iron Man is a fictional superhero appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The character was created by writer and editor Stan Lee, and artists Don Heck and Jack Kirby. He first appeared in the comic book \"Tales of Suspense #39\" in March 1963.\n\n**Origin Story:**\nTony Stark, a billionaire inventor and industrialist, is the founder of Stark Industries, a cutting-edge technology company. While on a business trip in Afghanistan, Tony is kidnapped by a group of terrorists who demand that he build a powerful missile system for them. Instead, Tony uses his intelligence and resources to create a suit of armor, which he uses to escape from his captors.\n\n**The Iron Man Suit:**\nThe Iron Man suit is a powered exoskeleton that provides Tony with superhuman strength, speed, and agility. The suit is also equipped with advanced technology, including repulsor technology, which allows Tony to fly and project energy blasts. Over the years, Tony has upgraded and modified the suit numerous times, adding new features and capabilities.\n\n**Personality:**\nTony Stark, aka Iron Man, is a confident and charismatic character. He is a self-proclaimed genius and a master strategist, often using his intelligence and wit to outmaneuver his enemies. Tony is also a bit of a narcissist and can come across as arrogant, but he is ultimately driven by a desire to protect the world from threats both human and supernatural.\n\n**Movie Franchise:**\nThe Iron Man character has been featured in several movies, including:\n\n1. Iron Man (2008) - The first movie in the franchise, starring Robert Downey Jr. as Tony Stark/Iron Man.\n2. Iron Man 2 (2010) - The sequel to the first movie, with Tony facing off against a new villain, Whiplash.\n3. The Avengers (2012) - A team-up movie featuring Iron Man, Captain America, Thor, and other Marvel heroes.\n4. Iron Man 3 (2013) - The third movie in the franchise, with Tony facing off against a terrorist known as the Mandarin.\n5. Avengers: Age of Ultron (2015) - The second team-up movie, with Iron Man and the Avengers facing off against an artificial intelligence known as Ultron.\n6. Captain America: Civil War (2016) - A movie that features Iron Man and Captain America on opposite sides of a conflict over government regulation of superheroes.\n7. Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017) - A movie that features Iron Man as a mentor to the young superhero Spider-Man.\n8. Avengers: Infinity War (2018) - A team-up movie that features Iron Man and the Avengers facing off against the villainous Thanos.\n9. Avengers: Endgame (2019) - The final movie in the franchise, with Iron Man and the Avengers facing off against Thanos in a battle to save the universe.\n\n**Impact and Legacy:**\nIron Man has become one of the most iconic and beloved superheroes in the world. The character has inspired countless fans with his intelligence, wit, and bravery. The Iron Man franchise has also spawned numerous spin-offs, including video games, TV shows, and merchandise. The character\'s legacy continues to grow, with new movies and TV shows in development.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-13 17:30:00', '2026-05-13 17:30:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/iron_man?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 55, '2026-05-13 17:30:22', '2026-05-13 17:30:22'),
