(3090, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious crime organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda Gaviria, after his father abandoned them. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he quickly turned to crime to support himself and his family.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working in the cocaine trade, initially as a small-time smuggler. However, he quickly rose through the ranks and became a key player in the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder and other Colombian traffickers. Escobar\'s cunning, charisma, and ruthlessness helped him to consolidate power and eventually become the leader of the cartel.\n\n**Medellín Cartel and Cocaine Empire**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a vast network of cocaine production, smuggling, and distribution, with tentacles reaching into the United States, Europe, and other parts of the world.\n\nEscobar\'s empire was built on violence, intimidation, and corruption. He used murder, torture, and bribery to eliminate rivals, silence informants, and manipulate government officials. His cartel was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, and politicians.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Feats**\n\nSome of Escobar\'s most notorious crimes and feats include:\n\n* The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989\n* The bombing of Avianca Flight 203 in 1989, which killed 110 people\n* The murder of Colombian police chief Colonel Jaime Ramírez Gómez in 1989\n* The construction of a luxurious mansion, Hacienda Nápoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a manhunt for Escobar. The search was intense, with thousands of soldiers and police officers involved. Escobar went into hiding, but he was eventually tracked down to a rooftop in Medellín on December 1, 1993.\n\nAs police closed in, Escobar was shot and killed in a shootout. His death marked the end of an era for the Medellín cartel, and it paved the way for the rise of other cartels and crime organizations in Colombia.\n\n**Legacy and Impact**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the failures of the war on drugs and the corruption that pervades many Latin American countries.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been immortalized in books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His life and death have also sparked debates about the impact of the drug trade on society and the effectiveness of law enforcement strategies in combating organized crime.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life was marked by violence, corruption, and tragedy. His legacy serves as a reminder of the dangers of the drug trade and the importance of addressing the root causes of crime and violence in our societies.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 10:45:00', '2026-05-14 10:45:37', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-14 10:45:37', '2026-05-14 10:45:37'),
(3091, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious crime organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He grew up in a tough neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in small-time crime at a young age. Escobar\'s rise to power began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States.\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar partnered with other Colombian traffickers to form the Medellín cartel, which quickly became one of the dominant players in the global cocaine trade. Escobar\'s organization was known for its ruthless tactics, including murder, intimidation, and bribery, which allowed it to expand its operations and eliminate competitors.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nAt its peak, the Medellín cartel was responsible for smuggling an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine into the United States. Escobar\'s organization was highly sophisticated, with a complex network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. The cartel\'s profits were staggering, with estimates suggesting that Escobar\'s personal wealth reached $30 billion.\n\nEscobar\'s success was due in part to his ability to corrupt and intimidate government officials, judges, and law enforcement agents. He was known to use violence and intimidation to maintain control over his organization and eliminate any potential threats.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The hunt for Escobar was one of the most extensive and complex manhunts in history, involving thousands of police and military personnel.\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, known as La Catedral. However, Escobar continued to run his organization from behind bars, and in 1992, he escaped from prison and went into hiding.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death. Escobar\'s death marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s dominance in the global cocaine trade, and his legacy has been the subject of much debate and controversy.\n\nSome have portrayed Escobar as a Robin Hood figure, who used his wealth and power to help the poor and marginalized in Colombia. Others have condemned him as a ruthless and brutal criminal, responsible for the deaths of thousands of people.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite the controversy surrounding his life, Pablo Escobar remains one of the most fascinating and complex figures in modern history.\n\n**Key Facts**\n\n* Born: December 1, 1949, Rionegro, Colombia\n* Died: December 1, 1993, Medellín, Colombia\n* Leader of the Medellín cartel\n* Estimated personal wealth: $30 billion\n* Responsible for smuggling an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine into the United States\n* Killed in a shootout with Colombian police on December 1, 1993\n\n**Sources**\n\n* \"Pablo Escobar: The Life and Legacy of the World\'s Most Notorious Drug Lord\" by Shaun Attwood\n* \"The Medellín Cartel: The Inside Story of the World\'s Most Powerful Crime Organization\" by Hernando Calvo Ospina\n* \"Narcos\" (Netflix series, 2015-2017)\n* \"Pablo Escobar: El Patrón del Mal\" (Colombian TV series, 2012)', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 10:50:00', '2026-05-14 10:50:28', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-14 10:50:28', '2026-05-14 10:50:28'),
(3092, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious cartels in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most successful and infamous drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his criminal career.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started selling cocaine and other illicit substances in Medellín. He quickly rose through the ranks of the local underworld, becoming a key figure in the city\'s cocaine trade. In the early 1980s, Escobar co-founded the Medellín cartel with his partners, Carlos Lehder and Gustavo Gaviria.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel\'s main business was cocaine trafficking, and it controlled a significant portion of the global market. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality, and he was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including politicians, police officers, and rival gang members.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar\'s reign was marked by violence and intimidation. He used terror tactics to maintain control over his organization and to eliminate his enemies. He was responsible for the assassination of several high-profile targets, including Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989. Escobar also ordered the bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people in 1989.\n\n**Wealth and Excess**\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle. He owned several luxury mansions, including the famous Hacienda Nápoles, which featured a private zoo, a swimming pool, and a collection of exotic cars. Escobar\'s wealth was estimated to be around $30 billion, making him one of the richest men in the world at the time.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially designed facility, known as the Cathedral. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt was launched, and Escobar was eventually tracked down by Colombian police and the US DEA. He was killed in a shootout on December 1, 1993, on the rooftop of a safe house in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a folk hero by some, who view him as a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the US-backed war on drugs. Escobar\'s story has been immortalized in numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 10:53:00', '2026-05-14 10:53:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-14 10:53:26', '2026-05-14 10:53:26'),
(3093, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Key Takeaways for Success**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about perseverance, passion, and drive. Here are some key points to consider on your own journey to success:\n\n* **Set ambitious goals**: Don\'t be afraid to dream big and strive for excellence.\n* **Stay focused and determined**: Overcome obstacles and stay committed to your vision.\n* **Surround yourself with supportive allies**: Build a strong network of like-minded individuals who share your passion.\n* **Continuously learn and adapt**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new knowledge and skills.\n* **Believe in yourself**: Trust your instincts and have confidence in your abilities.\n\n#MotivationMonday #SuccessMindset #DragonInspiration #TrendingNow #BusinessTips #EntrepreneurLife #ProfessionalGrowth #FacebookCommunity #Inspiration #LeadershipQualities #GoalSetting #Determination #Focus #Networking #LifelongLearning #SelfBelief #ConfidenceIsKey', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 11:18:00', '2026-05-14 11:18:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-14 11:18:21', '2026-05-14 11:18:21'),
(3094, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', '**Party Wear for Men: A Guide to Styling and Fashion**\n\nWhen it comes to party wear for men, the options are endless. From formal suits to stylish casual wear, there\'s something for every occasion and personal style. Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n### **Formal Party Wear**\n\n1. **Suits**: A classic choice for formal parties, suits are available in various styles, including black tie, white tie, and business attire.\n2. **Tuxedos**: Perfect for black-tie events, tuxedos are a stylish and sophisticated option.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: Pair a dress shirt with a suit or tuxedo for a formal and elegant look.\n4. **Bow Ties**: Add a touch of sophistication with a bow tie, available in various patterns and colors.\n\n### **Casual Party Wear**\n\n1. **Dress Pants**: A versatile option, dress pants can be paired with a variety of tops, including dress shirts, polo shirts, and blazers.\n2. **Polo Shirts**: A classic choice for casual parties, polo shirts are available in various colors and patterns.\n3. **Blazers**: Add a touch of sophistication to a casual outfit with a blazer, available in various styles and colors.\n4. **Jeans**: A popular choice for casual parties, jeans can be paired with a variety of tops, including dress shirts, polo shirts, and t-shirts.\n\n### **Trendy Party Wear**\n\n1. **Slim-Fit Suits**: A modern twist on the classic suit, slim-fit suits are perfect for fashion-forward men.\n2. **Patterned Shirts**: Add a touch of personality to an outfit with a patterned shirt, available in various styles and colors.\n3. **Statement Accessories**: Make a statement with bold accessories, such as patterned ties, pocket squares, and cufflinks.\n4. **Boots**: Add a touch of edge to an outfit with boots, available in various styles and colors.\n\n### **Tips for Styling Party Wear**\n\n1. **Dress for the Occasion**: Make sure to dress according to the party\'s theme and dress code.\n2. **Accessories Matter**: Add a touch of personality to an outfit with accessories, such as watches, cufflinks, and pocket squares.\n3. **Grooming is Key**: Make sure to groom yourself properly, including trimming your beard, styling your hair, and wearing clean clothes.\n4. **Confidence is Key**: Own your outfit and exude confidence to make a lasting impression.\n\nBy following these tips and guides, you\'ll be sure to make a stylish and memorable impression at your next party. Remember to dress according to the occasion, accessorize wisely, and exude confidence to take your party wear to the next level.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 12:40:00', '2026-05-14 12:40:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-14 12:40:21', '2026-05-14 12:40:21'),
(3095, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key characteristics of a formal shirt for men:\n\n**Types of Formal Shirts:**\n\n1. **Dress Shirt:** A classic dress shirt with a collar and cuffs, usually made of cotton or a cotton-blend fabric.\n2. **Business Shirt:** A slightly more casual version of a dress shirt, often with a spread collar and no cuffs.\n3. **Tuxedo Shirt:** A special type of formal shirt designed to be worn with a tuxedo, typically with a wingtip collar and cuffs.\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar Style:** Formal shirts often have a point collar, spread collar, or wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff Style:** Formal shirts usually have cuffs, which can be button or link cuffs.\n3. **Fabric:** Formal shirts are often made of high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit:** Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the chest and shoulders.\n5. **Color:** Formal shirts are often white, light blue, or other conservative colors.\n6. **Pattern:** Formal shirts may have a subtle pattern such as stripes or checks, but solid colors are more common.\n\n**Popular Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink:** Known for their high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet:** A French luxury brand that offers exquisite formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers:** An American brand that offers classic, high-quality formal shirts.\n4. **Hermès:** A French luxury brand that offers elegant, sophisticated formal shirts.\n5. **Armani:** An Italian luxury brand that offers stylish, high-quality formal shirts.\n\n**Tips for Wearing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Pair with a suit:** A formal shirt is often worn with a suit and tie for a complete, polished look.\n2. **Choose the right collar:** Select a collar style that complements your face shape and the occasion.\n3. **Pay attention to fit:** Make sure the shirt fits well and is not too tight or too loose.\n4. **Accessorize:** Add a tie, pocket square, and cufflinks to complete your formal look.\n5. **Iron your shirt:** Make sure your shirt is crisp and well-ironed to create a sharp, professional impression.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 12:56:00', '2026-05-14 12:56:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-14 12:56:18', '2026-05-14 12:56:18'),
(3096, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of building a strong brand. Here are a few key points to consider:\n\n* **Embracing your unique identity**: Just like my scales shine in the sunlight, your brand should reflect what makes you unique.\n* **Breathing fire into your marketing strategy**: Don\'t be afraid to take risks and try new things to stand out from the crowd.\n* **Hoarding treasure, not clutter**: Keep your brand organized and focused on what\'s truly important.\n* **Soaring to new heights**: Set goals and work towards achieving them, just like I soar through the skies.\n\n#DragonSquad #BusinessTips #MarketingStrategy #BrandIdentity #TrendingNow #FacebookMarketing #ProfessionalAdvice #BusinessGrowth #Entrepreneurship\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, including #TrendingNow to increase visibility. The tone is professional and relatable, making it suitable for a dragon business on Facebook.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 13:03:00', '2026-05-14 13:03:12', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Women_Sandel?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-05-14 13:03:12', '2026-05-14 13:03:12'),
