(3218, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Lessons from a Dragon\'s Den**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned a thing or two about passion, perseverance, and success. Here are some key takeaways:\n\n* **Set your goals ablaze**: Don\'t be afraid to dream big and chase your aspirations with fierce determination.\n* **Hoarding knowledge is key**: Continuously learn and grow, just like a dragon\'s treasure trove of wisdom and experience.\n* **Breathing fire into your passions**: Pursue your interests with unrelenting enthusiasm and energy.\n* **Scales of resilience**: Develop a tough skin and learn to bounce back from setbacks and failures.\n* **Winging it with courage**: Take calculated risks and face your fears head-on, just like a dragon soaring through the skies.\n\n#DragonMotivation #BusinessLessons #SuccessTips #Entrepreneurship #Trending #Facebook #MotivationMonday #Inspiration #GoalSetting #Resilience #Courage #Passion #Determination #GrowthMindset #KnowledgeIsPower #DreamBig', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-18 10:35:00', '2026-05-18 10:35:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-18 10:35:19', '2026-05-18 10:35:19'),
(3219, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a notorious Colombian drug lord, smuggler, and leader of the Medellín cartel. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and powerful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and inform his actions.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling cocaine from Colombia to the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder and others. In 1979, Escobar became a key figure in the cartel, and by the early 1980s, he had become the dominant force in the organization.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world. The cartel\'s success was due in part to Escobar\'s innovative strategies, including the use of small planes to transport cocaine and the creation of a network of informants and assassins.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his ruthless tactics, including murder, intimidation, and bribery. He was responsible for the deaths of hundreds of people, including politicians, judges, police officers, and rival gang members. Escobar\'s organization was also responsible for numerous bombings and assassinations, including the 1989 bombing of Avianca Flight 203, which killed 110 people.\n\n**Personal Life**\n\nDespite his notorious reputation, Escobar was a complex and charismatic figure. He was known for his love of luxury and his flamboyant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of exotic cars, and a sprawling estate in Medellín. Escobar was also a family man, and he was deeply devoted to his wife, María Victoria Henao, and their two children.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the support of the United States, launched a series of operations aimed at capturing or killing Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped from prison in 1992. A massive manhunt ensued, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal, but also as a folk hero and a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the United States. Escobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power.\n* He was known for his love of soccer and was a major supporter of the Atlético Nacional soccer team in Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s private zoo, which included exotic animals such as hippos, giraffes, and elephants, was a popular tourist attraction in Medellín.\n* He was a skilled pilot and owned several planes, including a Learjet and a helicopter.\n* Escobar\'s death was a major blow to the Medellín cartel, and the organization was eventually dismantled by the Colombian authorities.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-18 10:45:00', '2026-05-18 10:45:32', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-18 10:45:32', '2026-05-18 10:45:32'),
(3220, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and infamous criminal organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. His father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. Escobar grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and smuggling at a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began working for a local cocaine smuggler, and quickly rose through the ranks. He became a key player in the Medellín cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder and later led by Escobar. The cartel\'s success was fueled by the growing demand for cocaine in the United States and Europe, and Escobar\'s ability to smuggle large quantities of the drug into these markets.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel\'s operations were highly sophisticated, with a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers. Escobar was known for his cunning and ruthlessness, and was feared by his enemies and respected by his associates.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar\'s rise to power was marked by violence and intimidation. He was responsible for the murders of hundreds of people, including police officers, judges, and politicians. He also ordered the bombing of a commercial airliner, which killed over 100 people. Escobar\'s tactics were designed to intimidate his enemies and maintain control over the cartel\'s operations.\n\n**Pursuit and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped from prison in 1992. A massive manhunt ensued, and on December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for the deaths of hundreds of people, but he was also a charismatic leader who was admired by many in Colombia. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Today, Escobar\'s name is synonymous with the excesses and violence of the drug trade, and his legacy serves as a cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his extravagant lifestyle, which included a private zoo, a collection of luxury cars, and a mansion with a private airport.\n* He was a skilled soccer player and was known to have played in local tournaments.\n* Escobar was a devout Catholic and was known to have made large donations to the Catholic Church.\n* He was a fan of the Colombian soccer team and was known to have sponsored several local teams.\n* Escobar\'s son, Juan Pablo Escobar, has written a book about his father\'s life and has spoken publicly about the difficulties of growing up as the son of a notorious drug lord.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-18 10:50:00', '2026-05-18 10:50:27', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-18 10:50:27', '2026-05-18 10:50:27'),
(3221, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín Cartel. He is widely considered one of the most notorious and influential figures in the history of organized crime.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, to a peasant farmer and a schoolteacher. He grew up in a poor family and was raised in a tough neighborhood in Medellín. Escobar began his career in crime at a young age, starting with small-time theft and smuggling. He eventually moved on to more serious crimes, such as kidnapping and murder.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was booming in Colombia at the time. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, becoming a top lieutenant to the cartel\'s leader, Carlos Lehder. After Lehder\'s arrest in 1981, Escobar took over as the leader of the cartel.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organized crime groups in the world. Escobar\'s organization controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and he became one of the richest men in the world.\n\nThe Medellín Cartel was known for its brutal tactics, including murder, kidnapping, and intimidation. Escobar was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, and politicians. He also ordered the assassinations of several high-profile targets, including Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989.\n\n**The \"King of Cocaine\"**\n\nEscobar\'s success in the cocaine trade earned him the nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) or \"The King of Cocaine.\" He lived a lavish lifestyle, with a large estate in Medellín, known as Hacienda Napoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic animals.\n\nEscobar was also known for his charitable work in Medellín, where he built housing, roads, and other infrastructure for the poor. This earned him a degree of popularity among some segments of the population, who saw him as a folk hero.\n\n**The Hunt for Escobar**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The hunt for Escobar became a major priority for law enforcement agencies around the world.\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to the Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility in Envigado, known as La Catedral. However, Escobar escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\n**Death and Legacy**\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\nEscobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who was responsible for thousands of deaths and untold suffering. However, he is also seen by some as a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the United States, which were perceived as corrupt and oppressive.\n\nToday, Escobar\'s name is still synonymous with the cocaine trade and organized crime. His life and exploits have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which tells the story of his rise and fall.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-18 10:53:00', '2026-05-18 10:53:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-18 10:53:21', '2026-05-18 10:53:21'),
(3222, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Dragon\'s Den: Embracing the Fire Within**\n\nAs a dragon, I\'ve learned to harness my inner strength and passion to drive success. Here are some key takeaways to help you unleash your own potential:\n\n* **Set ambitious goals**: Don\'t be afraid to dream big and aim high.\n* **Stay focused and determined**: Overcome obstacles and stay committed to your vision.\n* **Cultivate a growth mindset**: Continuously learn, adapt, and evolve to stay ahead.\n* **Surround yourself with positivity**: Build a supportive network that fuels your passion and motivation.\n* **Take calculated risks**: Sometimes, you need to take a leap of faith to achieve greatness.\n\n#DragonsDen #MotivationMonday #SuccessTips #GoalSetting #Focus #Determination #GrowthMindset #PositiveVibes #RiskAndReward #TrendingNow #FacebookMotivation #BusinessInspiration #Entrepreneurship #Leadership #PersonalGrowth #SelfImprovement #Innovation #Creativity #ProductivityHacks #SuccessStories #Inspiration #Motivation #FacebookBusiness #SmallBusiness #EntrepreneurTips', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-18 11:18:00', '2026-05-18 11:18:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-18 11:18:21', '2026-05-18 11:18:21'),
(3223, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', '**Men\'s Party Wear: A Guide to Dressing Up**\n\nWhen it comes to party wear for men, the options can be overwhelming. Here are some tips and ideas to help you dress to impress:\n\n**Formal Party Wear**\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-fitted suit is a classic choice for formal parties. Choose from a range of colors, including black, navy, and gray.\n2. **Dress Shirts**: Pair your suit with a dress shirt in a complementary color. Consider a white or light-colored shirt for a classic look.\n3. **Ties**: Add a pop of color with a tie. Opt for a simple pattern or a bold, statement-making design.\n4. **Shoes**: Black or brown leather shoes are a safe choice for formal parties.\n\n**Semi-Formal Party Wear**\n\n1. **Blazers**: A blazer can add a touch of sophistication to a casual outfit. Pair it with a dress shirt and dark jeans.\n2. **Dress Pants**: Dark-washed dress pants are a versatile choice for semi-formal parties.\n3. **Polos**: A polo shirt is a great alternative to a dress shirt. Look for one in a bold color or pattern.\n4. **Loafers**: Slip-on loafers or dress boots can add a stylish touch to your outfit.\n\n**Casual Party Wear**\n\n1. **T-Shirts**: A plain white or black T-shirt is a classic choice for casual parties.\n2. **Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans are a staple for casual parties. Consider a pair with a bit of stretch for comfort.\n3. **Jackets**: Add a denim or leather jacket to your outfit for a cool, casual look.\n4. **Sneakers**: Sneakers are a great choice for casual parties. Opt for a pair in a bold color or with a unique design.\n\n**Accessories**\n\n1. **Watches**: A leather or metal watch can add a touch of sophistication to your outfit.\n2. **Cufflinks**: If you\'re wearing a dress shirt, consider adding a pair of cufflinks for a stylish touch.\n3. **Pocket Squares**: A pocket square can add a pop of color to your suit or blazer.\n4. **Hats**: A fedora or Panama hat can add a stylish touch to your outfit.\n\n**Tips**\n\n1. **Dress for the occasion**: Consider the theme and dress code of the party when choosing your outfit.\n2. **Be confident**: Own your look and feel confident in what you\'re wearing.\n3. **Pay attention to fit**: Make sure your clothes fit well and are comfortable to wear.\n4. **Accessories can make or break an outfit**: Choose accessories that complement your outfit and add a touch of personality.\n\n**Popular Party Wear Styles for Men**\n\n1. **Slim Fit**: A slim-fit suit or dress shirt can create a streamlined, modern look.\n2. **Classic**: A classic two-button suit or a simple white dress shirt is a timeless choice.\n3. **Statement-Making**: Consider a bold, statement-making outfit with a patterned shirt or bold-colored pants.\n4. **Vintage**: A vintage-inspired outfit with a fitted waistcoat or a patterned suit can add a touch of elegance to your look.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Experiment with different styles and find what works best for you.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-18 12:40:00', '2026-05-18 12:40:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-18 12:40:26', '2026-05-18 12:40:26'),
(3224, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, or special occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a point collar or a spread collar, which is a classic and timeless choice.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or button cuffs, which are more formal than barrel cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are usually slim-fit or tailored to fit close to the body, creating a streamlined look.\n5. **Button-front**: Formal shirts usually have a button-front closure, which is a classic and elegant choice.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a point collar and French cuffs.\n2. **Business shirt**: A formal shirt with a spread collar and button cuffs, often worn for business meetings and office work.\n3. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and French cuffs, designed to be worn with a tuxedo.\n4. **Dinner shirt**: A formal shirt with a detachable collar and cuffs, often worn for formal dinners and special occasions.\n\n**Popular Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: Known for their high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French luxury brand that offers exquisite formal shirts with intricate details.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: An American brand that offers classic, timeless formal shirts.\n4. **Armani**: An Italian luxury brand that offers stylish, modern formal shirts.\n\n**Tips for Choosing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a formal shirt that is suitable for the occasion, such as a business meeting or a formal event.\n2. **Choose a comfortable fabric**: Select a fabric that is comfortable and breathable, such as cotton or linen.\n3. **Pay attention to fit**: Make sure the shirt fits well and is not too tight or too loose.\n4. **Accessories**: Consider the accessories you will be wearing with the shirt, such as a tie or cufflinks.\n\nBy following these tips and considering the different styles and brands available, you can find a formal shirt that is both stylish and suitable for your needs.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-18 12:56:00', '2026-05-18 12:56:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-18 12:56:24', '2026-05-18 12:56:24'),
