(3254, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of fiery passion and drive in business. Here are a few key takeaways to help you succeed:\n* Set clear goals and priorities to stay focused\n* Develop a strong support network to help you navigate challenges\n* Continuously learn and adapt to stay ahead of the curve\n* Don\'t be afraid to take calculated risks and try new things\n* Remember to take care of yourself and prioritize self-care\n\nBy following these principles, you can unlock your full potential and achieve greatness. #DragonSizedAmbitions #BusinessTips #ProductivityHacks #EntrepreneurLife #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #SuccessStory #GoalOriented #InnovationNation\"\n\nThis caption is professional, relatable, and uses trending hashtags to increase visibility on Facebook.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-19 10:35:00', '2026-05-19 10:35:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-19 10:35:19', '2026-05-19 10:35:19'),
(3255, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to Abel de Jesús Escobar and Hermilda Gaviria. He was the third of seven children in a lower-middle-class family. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, with his family struggling to make ends meet. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working on the streets, selling fruit and other goods to support his family.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s entry into the world of organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling cigarettes and other contraband into Colombia. He quickly moved into the cocaine trade, which was becoming increasingly lucrative in the 1970s and 1980s. Escobar\'s charisma, business acumen, and ruthlessness helped him build a vast network of smugglers, distributors, and dealers.\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world. He established a sophisticated network of cocaine production, transportation, and distribution, using planes, boats, and other vehicles to smuggle the drug into the United States and other countries.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Feats**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Galán, who was running on an anti-drug platform.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s henchmen planted a bomb on an Avianca flight, killing 110 people.\n3. **The murder of Colombian police officers**: Escobar\'s organization killed hundreds of police officers, judges, and other officials who dared to challenge his empire.\n\nDespite his brutal methods, Escobar was also known for his charitable works and his ability to build loyalty among his associates and the poor communities he supported. He built houses, roads, and other infrastructure in Medellín, earning him the nickname \"El Patrón\" (The Boss).\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a campaign to capture Escobar. In 1991, Escobar surrendered to the authorities and was imprisoned, but he escaped in 1992.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. His death marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror, but it also sparked a wave of violence and instability in Colombia that would last for years to come.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning criminal who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a symbol of the country\'s struggles with poverty, inequality, and corruption.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos,\" which dramatized his rise and fall. Despite the controversy surrounding his legacy, Escobar remains a fascinating and infamous figure, a testament to the enduring power of his myth and the enduring impact of his crimes.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-19 10:45:00', '2026-05-19 10:45:30', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-19 10:45:30', '2026-05-19 10:45:30'),
(3256, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious cartels in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. He dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working on the streets, selling fruit and other items to support his family.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling cocaine from Colombia to the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Medellín Cartel, which was founded by Carlos Lehder and other Colombian traffickers. Escobar\'s charm, intelligence, and ruthlessness helped him become a key player in the cartel, and he eventually took over as its leader.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín Cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel controlled a significant portion of the global cocaine trade, and its profits were estimated to be in the billions of dollars. Escobar\'s organization was known for its brutality and violence, and he was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including rival gang members, police officers, and innocent civilians.\n\n**Notorious Acts**\n\nSome of Escobar\'s most notorious acts include:\n\n* The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán in 1989\n* The bombing of Avianca Flight 203 in 1989, which killed 110 people\n* The murder of dozens of police officers and judges who were investigating his activities\n* The construction of a private zoo and mansion, known as Hacienda Nápoles, which featured exotic animals and a collection of luxury cars\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nEscobar\'s reign of terror eventually came to an end in 1993, when he was killed in a shootout with Colombian police. He was 44 years old at the time of his death. The Colombian government had been working with the United States to track down Escobar, and a special task force was formed to capture or kill him. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was cornered in a rooftop hideout in Medellín, and he was shot and killed by police.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and brutal leader who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering. However, he is also seen as a symbol of Colombian culture and a product of the country\'s tumultuous history. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of luxury cars and owned a collection of vehicles, including a Mercedes-Benz 600 and a Porsche 911.\n* He was a fan of soccer and owned a team called the Atlético Nacional.\n* Escobar was married to María Victoria Henao, and the couple had two children together.\n* He was known for his generosity and philanthropy, and he built roads, schools, and hospitals in his hometown of Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s net worth was estimated to be around $30 billion at the height of his power, making him one of the richest people in the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-19 10:50:00', '2026-05-19 10:50:29', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-19 10:50:29', '2026-05-19 10:50:29'),
(3257, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious crime organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful drug traffickers of all time.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. He grew up in a tumultuous household and was exposed to violence and crime from a young age. Escobar dropped out of school in the seventh grade and began working in the streets, selling cigarettes and other small items.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar became involved in the cocaine trade, which was rapidly expanding in Colombia. He started by smuggling small quantities of cocaine into the United States, but soon expanded his operations to become one of the largest cocaine traffickers in the world.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the late 1970s, Escobar formed the Medellín Cartel, a crime organization that would become synonymous with violence, corruption, and cocaine trafficking. The cartel\'s operations were highly organized and efficient, with a network of smugglers, distributors, and money launderers.\n\nAt the height of its power, the Medellín Cartel was responsible for an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine supply, with revenues exceeding $20 billion per year. Escobar became one of the richest men in the world, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his ruthless tactics and willingness to use violence to maintain control and eliminate rivals. He was responsible for the murders of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, politicians, and journalists.\n\nThe Medellín Cartel\'s violence and intimidation tactics included:\n\n* Assassinations: Escobar ordered the killings of anyone who stood in his way, including government officials, rival gang members, and innocent civilians.\n* Bombings: The cartel carried out numerous bombings, including attacks on government buildings, banks, and other public places.\n* Kidnappings: Escobar\'s men kidnapped and held for ransom numerous prominent Colombians, including politicians, business leaders, and members of the media.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the late 1980s and early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a series of operations to capture or kill Escobar. The pressure on the Medellín Cartel increased, and many of its top leaders were either killed or captured.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a vast and powerful crime organization from scratch.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and television shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a fascinating and intriguing figure, and his story continues to captivate audiences around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-19 10:53:00', '2026-05-19 10:53:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-19 10:53:26', '2026-05-19 10:53:26'),
(3258, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**\"Breathing Fire into Your Business: Key Takeaways\"**\n\nAs a dragon in the business world, I\'ve learned a thing or two about what it takes to succeed. Here are some relatable points to consider:\n\n* **Set clear goals**: Just like a dragon sets its sights on its treasure, you need to define what you want to achieve in your business.\n* **Be adaptable**: The business landscape is constantly changing, and you need to be able to pivot and adjust your strategy to stay ahead.\n* **Build a strong team**: A dragon\'s hoard is only as strong as the dragon guarding it - surround yourself with talented and dedicated individuals.\n* **Take calculated risks**: Don\'t be afraid to take bold action and try new things - it\'s often the key to unlocking new opportunities.\n* **Stay focused**: With so many distractions in the business world, it\'s easy to get sidetracked - stay laser-focused on your goals and keep pushing forward.\n\n#BusinessTips #Entrepreneurship #Dragonapproved #TrendingNow #FacebookBusiness #BusinessInspiration #MotivationMonday #SuccessTips #LeadershipGoals #BusinessStrategy #InnovationNation', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-19 11:18:00', '2026-05-19 11:18:21', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-19 11:18:21', '2026-05-19 11:18:21'),
(3259, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:57', 'A pen is a common writing instrument used to apply ink to a surface, typically paper, in order to write or draw. It consists of a nib or tip that dispenses the ink, and a handle or body that holds the ink reservoir. Pens can be categorized into several types, including:\n\n1. **Ballpoint pens**: These use a small metal ball to dispense ink onto the paper.\n2. **Rollerball pens**: Similar to ballpoint pens, but with a water-based ink that flows more smoothly.\n3. **Fountain pens**: These use a nib to deliver ink to the paper, and are often preferred by those who value handwriting and calligraphy.\n4. **Gel pens**: These use a water-based gel ink that is vibrant and colorful.\n5. **Fineliners**: These are fine-tipped pens used for detailed work, such as drawing and illustration.\n\nPens have been an essential tool for communication and self-expression throughout history, and continue to be an important part of daily life.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-19 11:57:00', '2026-05-19 11:57:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 16, '2026-05-19 11:57:18', '2026-05-19 11:57:18'),
(3260, 'Auto Post for instagram at 11:59', 'A pen packet, also known as a pen pack, is a small collection of pens, usually containing 2-10 pens, that are bundled together and sold as a single unit. These packets often include a variety of pens with different ink colors, tip sizes, or styles.\n\nPen packets are commonly used for:\n\n1. **Office or school supplies**: They provide a convenient way to purchase multiple pens at once, making it easy to stock up on writing utensils.\n2. **Art or design projects**: Pen packets with assorted colors and tip sizes can be useful for artists, designers, or crafters who need a range of pens for their work.\n3. **Travel or on-the-go**: A pen packet can be a handy item to carry in a bag or purse, providing a set of pens that can be used in different situations.\n\nSome common types of pens found in pen packets include:\n\n* Ballpoint pens\n* Rollerball pens\n* Fineliners\n* Highlighters\n* Gel pens\n\nOverall, pen packets offer a convenient and often cost-effective way to purchase multiple pens at once, making them a popular choice for individuals and businesses alike.', '[\"instagram\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-19 11:59:00', '2026-05-19 11:59:16', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Pen_Packet?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 17, '2026-05-19 11:59:16', '2026-05-19 11:59:16');
