(3332, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon business/creator on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of embracing my true self and living my best life. Here are a few things I\'ve learned along the way:\n\n* Self-care is key: taking time to breathe fire and relax is essential for my mental and physical health\n* Don\'t be afraid to stand out: my scales may be a little unconventional, but they\'re what make me unique\n* Networking is important: I\'ve made some great connections with other dragons and creatures in the industry\n* Always be learning: whether it\'s a new way to hoard treasure or a more efficient way to fly, I\'m always looking for ways to improve\n\n#DragonLife #SelfCare #MentalHealthMatters #BeYourself #Networking #ProfessionalGrowth #TrendingNow #FireBreathing #ScaleSquad #DragonSociety\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, as well as some specific to the dragon theme. The brand voice is professional, while still being relatable and engaging.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 10:35:00', '2026-05-21 10:35:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-05-21 10:35:24', '2026-05-21 10:35:24'),
(3333, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and the founder of the Medellín Cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug cartels in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a middle-class family and was the third of seven children. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he was exposed to the harsh realities of Colombia\'s underworld from a young age.\n\nEscobar\'s entry into the world of organized crime began in the 1970s, when he started smuggling marijuana and cocaine into the United States. He quickly rose through the ranks of the Colombian underworld, earning a reputation for his cunning, ruthlessness, and business acumen.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the late 1970s, Escobar co-founded the Medellín Cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug cartels in the world. The cartel\'s success was built on Escobar\'s innovative approach to the drug trade, which included:\n\n1. **Vertical integration**: Escobar controlled every aspect of the drug trade, from production to distribution, ensuring maximum profits and minimizing risks.\n2. **Diversification**: The cartel expanded into other lucrative businesses, such as extortion, kidnapping, and money laundering.\n3. **Violence and intimidation**: Escobar used brutal tactics to eliminate competitors, silence informants, and maintain control over his empire.\n\n**At the Height of Power**\n\nBy the mid-1980s, Escobar had become one of the richest and most powerful men in Colombia. He was estimated to be worth over $30 billion, and his cartel was responsible for supplying an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine.\n\nEscobar\'s lavish lifestyle was legendary, with his Hacienda Napoles estate featuring a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of exotic cars. He was known for his generosity and charisma, earning him a degree of popularity among some Colombians.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nHowever, Escobar\'s reign of terror eventually caught up with him. In 1991, the Colombian government, backed by the United States, launched a major crackdown on the Medellín Cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and his empire began to crumble.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. While he was responsible for immense suffering and violence, he also became a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government and the United States. His life and death have inspired numerous books, films, and TV series, including the popular Netflix show \"Narcos.\"\n\nToday, Escobar\'s name is still synonymous with the darker aspects of the drug trade, and his story serves as a cautionary tale about the dangers of unchecked power and the devastating consequences of organized crime.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 10:45:00', '2026-05-21 10:45:31', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-21 10:45:31', '2026-05-21 10:45:31'),
(3334, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord and one of the most notorious criminals of the 20th century. He was the founder and leader of the Medellín cartel, a powerful and ruthless organization that dominated the global cocaine trade in the 1980s.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda, after his father abandoned them. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, and he quickly turned to crime to survive.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar began his career in crime as a small-time smuggler and thief, but he soon became involved in the cocaine trade. He founded the Medellín cartel in the late 1970s, and through a combination of violence, intimidation, and strategic alliances, he quickly expanded his operation into a global empire.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel was a massive and complex organization that controlled every aspect of the cocaine trade, from production to distribution. Escobar and his associates smuggled tons of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other countries, earning billions of dollars in profits.\n\n**Violence and Intimidation**\n\nEscobar was known for his ruthless tactics and willingness to use violence to achieve his goals. He ordered the murders of thousands of people, including rival gang members, police officers, judges, and politicians. His organization was also responsible for numerous bombings, kidnappings, and other terrorist acts.\n\n**The \"King of Cocaine\"**\n\nAt the height of his power, Escobar was known as the \"King of Cocaine.\" He was one of the richest and most powerful men in the world, with an estimated net worth of over $30 billion. He lived in a lavish mansion in Medellín, surrounded by bodyguards and luxury cars.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn the early 1990s, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major crackdown on the Medellín cartel. Escobar was forced to go into hiding, and his organization began to crumble. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. He was 44 years old.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and violent criminal who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, but he was also a charismatic and cunning leader who was able to build a massive and powerful organization. His story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\"\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known for his love of animals and had a private zoo at his mansion, which included elephants, lions, and other exotic creatures.\n* He was a prolific builder and invested heavily in infrastructure projects, including roads, bridges, and schools.\n* Escobar was a fan of soccer and owned a team in the Colombian league.\n* He was known for his generosity and was said to have given away millions of dollars to poor people in Medellín.\n* Escobar\'s brother, Roberto, was also involved in the cartel and was known as \"El Osito\" (The Little Bear).', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 10:50:00', '2026-05-21 10:50:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-21 10:50:25', '2026-05-21 10:50:25'),
(3335, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Escobar was born in Rionegro, Colombia, on December 1, 1949. He grew up in a poor family and was raised by his mother, Hermilda Gaviria, after his father abandoned the family. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty and violence, which would later shape his worldview and inform his actions as a crime lord.\n\nEscobar began his career in crime at a young age, starting with small-time thefts and scams. He eventually turned to smuggling and trafficking, and by the late 1970s, he had established himself as a major player in the Colombian cocaine trade.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nIn the early 1980s, Escobar founded the Medellín cartel, which would become one of the most powerful and feared drug trafficking organizations in the world. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s ruthless tactics, his ability to bribe and intimidate officials, and his strategic use of violence to eliminate competitors and maintain control.\n\nAt the height of its power, the Medellín cartel was responsible for smuggling an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine into the United States, with revenues exceeding $20 billion per year. Escobar\'s organization was also involved in other crimes, including murder, kidnapping, and extortion.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Feuds**\n\nPablo Escobar was responsible for numerous notorious crimes, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Justice Minister Rodrigo Lara Bonilla**: In 1984, Escobar ordered the murder of Lara Bonilla, who had been cracking down on the Medellín cartel.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s organization bombed a commercial airliner, killing 110 people, in an attempt to kill a presidential candidate who was on board.\n3. **The murder of presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar\'s organization assassinated Galán, who was a leading candidate in the Colombian presidential election.\n\nEscobar was also involved in a series of bloody feuds with rival cartels and crime organizations, including the Cali cartel and the Colombian government.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility, known as the \"Catedral,\" which he had designed himself. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\nA massive manhunt ensued, with the Colombian government and the US Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) working together to track down Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and cunning crime lord who was responsible for countless deaths and suffering, but he was also a charismatic figure who was able to inspire loyalty and devotion in his followers.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life and career have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His story has also been the subject of controversy and debate, with some critics arguing that it glorifies or romanticizes his crimes, while others see it as a cautionary tale about the dangers of organized crime and the corrupting influence of power.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy serve as a reminder of the devastating consequences of organized crime and the importance of addressing the root causes of poverty, inequality, and violence that can drive individuals to engage in such activities.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 10:53:00', '2026-05-21 10:53:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-05-21 10:53:26', '2026-05-21 10:53:26'),
(3336, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**\"Unleashing the Fire Within: A Dragon\'s Guide to Success\"**\n\nAs a symbol of power and strength, dragons have long been revered for their unwavering dedication to their goals. Here are some key takeaways from the dragon\'s playbook:\n\n* **Set ambitious targets**: Don\'t be afraid to aim high and strive for greatness.\n* **Stay focused and resilient**: Overcome obstacles and push through challenges with determination and grit.\n* **Embrace your unique strengths**: Leverage your individual talents and abilities to achieve success.\n* **Continuously learn and adapt**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new knowledge and skills.\n* **Build a strong support network**: Surround yourself with like-minded individuals who share your vision and values.\n\nBy following these principles, you can unlock your full potential and achieve greatness. Remember to stay true to yourself and never give up on your dreams! #DragonInspiration #SuccessMindset #MotivationMonday #TrendingNow #BusinessTips #PersonalGrowth #ProfessionalDevelopment #FacebookBusiness #EntrepreneurLife #InspirationalQuotes', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 11:18:00', '2026-05-21 11:18:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-05-21 11:18:25', '2026-05-21 11:18:25'),
(3337, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', '**Party Wear for Men: A Guide to Stylish and Fashionable Options**\n\nWhen it comes to party wear for men, there are numerous options to choose from, depending on the occasion, theme, and personal style. Here are some popular and stylish party wear options for men:\n\n### Formal Party Wear\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-tailored suit in black, navy, or gray is a classic choice for formal parties.\n2. **Tuxedos**: A tuxedo is perfect for black-tie events, such as weddings, galas, or award shows.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A crisp, white dress shirt with a slim tie or bow tie adds a touch of elegance to any outfit.\n4. **Dress Pants**: Formal dress pants in matching or contrasting colors to the suit or tuxedo complete the look.\n\n### Semi-Formal Party Wear\n\n1. **Blazers**: A blazer in a bold color or pattern adds a stylish touch to a dress shirt and jeans.\n2. **Dress Shoes**: Loafers, brogues, or dress boots elevate a semi-formal outfit.\n3. **Chinos**: Dark-washed chinos or trousers are a versatile choice for semi-formal parties.\n4. **Polo Shirts**: A polo shirt in a bold color or pattern adds a sporty touch to a semi-formal outfit.\n\n### Casual Party Wear\n\n1. **Jeans**: Dark-washed jeans are a staple for casual parties.\n2. **T-Shirts**: Graphic T-shirts or plain T-shirts in bold colors are perfect for casual parties.\n3. **Hoodies**: A hoodie or a sweater adds a laid-back touch to a casual outfit.\n4. **Sneakers**: Sneakers, such as Converse or Vans, complete a casual party look.\n\n### Theme-Based Party Wear\n\n1. **Luau**: Hawaiian shirts, shorts, and flip-flops are perfect for a luau-themed party.\n2. **Retro**: Bell-bottom jeans, platform shoes, and a disco-era-inspired shirt are great for a retro-themed party.\n3. **Western**: A cowboy hat, boots, and a plaid shirt are ideal for a western-themed party.\n\n### Accessories\n\n1. **Watches**: A leather or metal watch adds a touch of sophistication to any outfit.\n2. **Cufflinks**: Cufflinks or a tie bar add a stylish touch to a formal outfit.\n3. **Hats**: A fedora, panama, or baseball cap adds a stylish touch to a casual outfit.\n4. **Jewelry**: A simple necklace or a pair of earrings can add a touch of personality to an outfit.\n\nRemember, the key to stylish party wear is to feel confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Experiment with different styles, colors, and accessories to find what works best for you!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 12:40:00', '2026-05-21 12:40:28', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-05-21 12:40:28', '2026-05-21 12:40:28'),
(3338, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is designed to be worn for formal occasions, such as business meetings, weddings, and other special events. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts typically have a point collar, spread collar, or wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or button cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are usually made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the chest and waist.\n5. **Details**: Formal shirts may feature details such as starched collars, cuffs, and placket fronts.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Classic fit**: A traditional formal shirt with a relaxed fit through the chest and waist.\n2. **Slim fit**: A modern formal shirt with a slim fit through the chest and waist.\n3. **Tailored fit**: A formal shirt with a tailored fit, designed to fit closely to the body.\n4. **Dress shirt**: A formal shirt designed to be worn with a suit and tie.\n5. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt designed to be worn with a tuxedo.\n\n**Popular Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: Known for their high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand that offers luxurious, high-end formal shirts.\n3. **Brooks Brothers**: An American brand that offers classic, traditional formal shirts.\n4. **Burberry**: A British brand that offers stylish, modern formal shirts.\n5. **Armani**: An Italian brand that offers luxurious, high-end formal shirts.\n\n**Tips for Choosing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a formal shirt that is suitable for the occasion.\n2. **Think about the color**: White, light blue, and pink are classic colors for formal shirts.\n3. **Pay attention to the fabric**: Choose a high-quality fabric that is comfortable and durable.\n4. **Get the right fit**: Make sure the shirt fits closely to the body, but is not too tight.\n5. **Accessories**: Consider the tie, cufflinks, and other accessories that will complement the shirt.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 12:56:00', '2026-05-21 12:56:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-05-21 12:56:24', '2026-05-21 12:56:24'),
(3339, 'Auto Post for facebook at 13:03', 'Here\'s a relatable caption in points for a dragon-themed business on Facebook:\n\n\"As a dragon, I understand the importance of being fierce and passionate about what I do. Here are a few things that drive me:\n* Embracing my unique strengths and abilities\n* Continuously learning and growing to stay ahead of the curve\n* Surrounding myself with like-minded individuals who share my vision\n* Taking calculated risks to achieve my goals\n* Staying true to my values and principles, even in the face of adversity\n\nLet\'s connect and see how we can help each other soar to new heights! #DragonSquad #FierceAndFearless #EntrepreneurLife #BusinessTips #TrendingNow #InspirationalQuotes #MotivationMonday #ProfessionalGrowth\"\n\nNote: The hashtags used are a mix of popular and trending ones, as well as some specific to the dragon theme and business/entrepreneurship.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-21 13:03:00', '2026-05-21 13:03:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Women_Sandel?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 3, '2026-05-21 13:03:20', '2026-05-21 13:03:20'),
