(3418, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:33', 'Football, also known as soccer in some countries, is a popular team sport played between two teams of 11 players using a round ball with the objective of scoring more goals than the opposing team by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent\'s goal.\n\nThere are several types of football, including:\n\n1. **Association Football (Soccer)**: This is the most popular type of football, played with a round ball and emphasizing kicking and heading.\n2. **American Football**: This type of football is played with an oval-shaped ball and emphasizes carrying and throwing the ball.\n3. **Rugby Football**: This type of football is a full-contact sport that emphasizes carrying and passing the ball.\n4. **Australian Rules Football**: This type of football is played with an oval-shaped ball and emphasizes kicking, carrying, and tackling.\n\n**Association Football (Soccer)** is the most widely played and watched sport in the world, with top leagues like the English Premier League, La Liga, and the UEFA Champions League. The sport is known for its simplicity, requiring minimal equipment, and its ability to bring people together from different cultures and backgrounds.\n\nSome of the most popular football tournaments include:\n\n1. **FIFA World Cup**: The most widely viewed and followed sporting event in the world, held every four years.\n2. **UEFA Champions League**: The top club competition in European football.\n3. **English Premier League**: One of the most popular and competitive domestic leagues in the world.\n\nFootball has a huge following and is played at various levels, from amateur to professional, with millions of players and fans around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-23 16:33:00', '2026-05-23 16:33:19', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/bicycle_kick_hitting_the_top_right_corner?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 53, '2026-05-23 16:33:19', '2026-05-23 16:33:19'),
(3419, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:42', 'The R1 bike is likely referring to the Yamaha YZF-R1, a high-performance sports motorcycle produced by Yamaha. \n\nHere are some key features of the Yamaha YZF-R1:\n\n1. **Engine**: 998cc, liquid-cooled, inline-four engine producing around 200 horsepower.\n2. **Transmission**: 6-speed manual transmission with a multi-plate clutch.\n3. **Suspension**: Upside-down fork at the front and a monoshock at the rear, both adjustable for preload, compression, and rebound.\n4. **Brakes**: Dual 320mm discs at the front with 4-piston calipers, and a single 220mm disc at the rear with a 2-piston caliper.\n5. **Weight**: Around 443 pounds (201 kg) wet weight.\n6. **Top Speed**: Electronically limited to around 186 mph (300 km/h), but can reach higher speeds with the limiter removed.\n\nThe Yamaha YZF-R1 is known for its exceptional handling, braking, and acceleration, making it a popular choice among track enthusiasts and street riders alike.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-23 16:42:00', '2026-05-23 16:42:23', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/r1_bike?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 54, '2026-05-23 16:42:23', '2026-05-23 16:42:23');
