(3492, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:49', 'Wooden craft, also known as woodcraft or woodworking, is a traditional and popular hobby that involves creating decorative or functional items from wood. Here are some interesting aspects of wooden craft:\n\n**Types of Wooden Crafts:**\n\n1. **Wood Carving:** Creating intricate designs or patterns on wood using hand tools or power tools.\n2. **Wood Turning:** Shaping wood into symmetrical or asymmetrical shapes using a lathe.\n3. **Wood Joinery:** Assembling wood pieces using various joints, such as mortise and tenon or dovetail joints.\n4. **Wood Burning:** Creating designs or patterns on wood using a pyrography tool or a wood burning pen.\n5. **Wood Inlay:** Creating intricate designs or patterns by embedding small pieces of wood into a larger piece.\n\n**Popular Wooden Craft Projects:**\n\n1. **Wooden Furniture:** Building chairs, tables, beds, or other furniture pieces.\n2. **Wooden Decorations:** Creating decorative items, such as wooden signs, wall art, or coasters.\n3. **Wooden Toys:** Building wooden toys, such as cars, trains, or puzzles.\n4. **Wooden Boxes:** Creating wooden boxes or chests for storage or as a decorative piece.\n5. **Wooden Sculptures:** Creating three-dimensional sculptures using wood.\n\n**Tools and Materials:**\n\n1. **Hand Tools:** Chisels, gouges, mallets, and hand saws.\n2. **Power Tools:** Table saws, miter saws, drill presses, and sanders.\n3. **Wood:** Various types of wood, such as oak, maple, cherry, or pine.\n4. **Adhesives:** Glues, such as wood glue or epoxy.\n5. **Finishing Materials:** Stains, varnishes, or polyurethane to protect and enhance the wood.\n\n**Benefits of Wooden Craft:**\n\n1. **Relaxation:** Woodworking can be a calming and meditative activity.\n2. **Creativity:** Wooden craft allows you to express your creativity and bring your ideas to life.\n3. **Skill Building:** Woodworking helps develop problem-solving skills, hand-eye coordination, and fine motor skills.\n4. **Sustainable:** Wooden craft can be a sustainable hobby, as you can use reclaimed or recycled wood.\n5. **Personal Satisfaction:** Creating something with your own hands can give you a sense of pride and accomplishment.\n\n**Tips for Beginners:**\n\n1. **Start with simple projects:** Begin with small, easy projects, such as building a birdhouse or a picture frame.\n2. **Practice safety:** Always wear protective gear, such as safety glasses and a dust mask, when working with power tools.\n3. **Learn from others:** Watch online tutorials, take classes, or join a woodworking community to learn new skills and techniques.\n4. **Be patient:** Woodworking can be a slow and iterative process, so be patient and don\'t be afraid to make mistakes.\n5. **Have fun:** Most importantly, enjoy the process and have fun creating something with your own hands!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-25 17:49:00', '2026-05-25 17:49:29', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/wood_spoon?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 10, '2026-05-25 17:49:29', '2026-05-25 17:49:29'),
(3493, 'Auto Post for facebook at 18:07', 'A flower pot is a container used to hold soil and plants, typically made of materials like ceramic, plastic, or clay. They come in various shapes, sizes, and designs, allowing people to showcase their plants and add a decorative touch to their homes or gardens.\n\nSome common types of flower pots include:\n\n1. Terracotta pots: Made from natural clay, these pots are breathable and suitable for plants that prefer well-draining soil.\n2. Ceramic pots: Often glazed and decorated, ceramic pots are popular for their aesthetic appeal and durability.\n3. Plastic pots: Lightweight and affordable, plastic pots are a practical choice for many gardeners.\n4. Hanging pots: Designed to be suspended from a hook or chain, hanging pots are perfect for adding a decorative touch to patios or balconies.\n5. Self-watering pots: These pots have a built-in water reservoir, allowing plants to draw water as needed, reducing the need for frequent watering.\n\nWhen choosing a flower pot, consider the following factors:\n\n1. Size: Select a pot that is large enough to accommodate the plant\'s roots and provide sufficient drainage.\n2. Material: Choose a pot that suits the plant\'s needs and your personal style.\n3. Drainage: Ensure the pot has adequate drainage holes to prevent waterlogged soil.\n4. Location: Consider the amount of sunlight and wind the pot will be exposed to, and choose a location that suits the plant\'s requirements.\n\nBy selecting the right flower pot and providing proper care, you can create a beautiful and thriving garden or indoor space that showcases your favorite plants.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-25 18:07:00', '2026-05-25 18:07:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Flower_pot?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 33, '2026-05-25 18:07:22', '2026-05-25 18:07:22'),
(3494, 'Auto Post for facebook at 18:26', 'Good morning, here are the weekdays: \n1. Monday\n2. Tuesday\n3. Wednesday\n4. Thursday\n5. Friday \n\nThe weekend days are:\n1. Saturday\n2. Sunday', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-05-25 18:26:00', '2026-05-25 18:26:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Week_days_post-Good_Morning_Like_(Monday%2CTuesday%2CWednesday%2CThursday%2CFriday%2CSaturday%2CSunday).?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 34, '2026-05-25 18:26:20', '2026-05-25 18:26:20'),
