(3704, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:35', '**Embracing the Fire Within: Key Takeaways for Success**\n\nAs a dragon in the business world, I\'ve learned a thing or two about what it takes to thrive. Here are some key points to consider:\n\n* **Set clear goals**: Define your vision and objectives to stay focused and driven.\n* **Develop a strong team**: Surround yourself with talented and dedicated individuals who share your passion.\n* **Innovate and adapt**: Stay ahead of the curve by embracing new ideas and technologies.\n* **Build strong relationships**: Foster trust and loyalty with your customers, partners, and community.\n* **Continuously learn and improve**: Stay humble and committed to ongoing growth and development.\n\nBy following these principles, you\'ll be well on your way to achieving success and making a lasting impact. #DragonSquad #BusinessTips #SuccessMindset #LeadershipGoals #Entrepreneurship #InnovationNation #TrendingNow #FacebookBusiness #ProfessionalDevelopment #GrowthMindset', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 10:35:00', '2026-06-01 10:35:18', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 50, '2026-06-01 10:35:18', '2026-06-01 10:35:18'),
(3705, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:45', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, narco-terrorist, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and infamous drug trafficking organizations in history. Here\'s a brief overview of his life and legacy:\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a middle-class family. He grew up in a neighborhood called Envigado, near Medellín, where he became involved in small-time crime and street violence from an early age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nEscobar\'s involvement in organized crime began in the 1970s, when he worked as a smuggler and a thief. He eventually turned to cocaine trafficking, which became his primary source of income. In the early 1980s, he partnered with other traffickers to form the Medellín cartel, which quickly grew into a massive and ruthless organization.\n\n**Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel dominated the global cocaine trade, smuggling tons of cocaine into the United States, Europe, and other countries. The cartel\'s success was fueled by Escobar\'s cunning, brutality, and strategic thinking. He used violence, intimidation, and bribery to eliminate competitors, silence law enforcement, and manipulate politicians.\n\n**Notorious Acts**\n\nEscobar was responsible for numerous notorious acts, including:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán** in 1989, which was meant to intimidate the government and prevent Galán\'s election.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203** in 1989, which killed 110 people and was intended to kill a Colombian presidential candidate.\n3. **The assassination of Colombian police chief Colonel Jaime Ramírez Gómez** in 1989, which was a revenge killing for the colonel\'s efforts to combat the Medellín cartel.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built facility, known as the \"Cathedral,\" which he had designed himself. However, he escaped from prison in 1992 and went into hiding. A massive manhunt ensued, involving Colombian and American law enforcement agencies.\n\nOn December 1, 1993, Escobar\'s 44th birthday, he was killed in a shootout with Colombian police in Medellín. His death marked the end of the Medellín cartel\'s reign of terror, but it also led to a power vacuum that allowed other cartels to rise to prominence.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a ruthless and cunning criminal who was responsible for thousands of deaths and immeasurable suffering. However, he was also a charismatic figure who was admired by some for his generosity, his love of soccer, and his ability to build a massive business empire.\n\nIn recent years, Escobar\'s life has been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV series, including the popular Netflix show \"Narcos,\" which dramatizes his rise and fall. Despite his notorious reputation, Escobar remains a fascinating and intriguing figure, and his story continues to captivate audiences around the world.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 10:45:00', '2026-06-01 10:45:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-06-01 10:45:25', '2026-06-01 10:45:25'),
(3706, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:50', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and founder of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and feared criminal organizations in the world. He is widely regarded as one of the most notorious and successful cocaine traffickers in history.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a family of modest means. His father was a farmer, and his mother was a schoolteacher. Escobar grew up in a poor neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and gang activity at a young age.\n\n**Rise to Power**\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began building his cocaine empire, initially working as a small-time smuggler and later becoming a key player in the Medellín cartel. He formed alliances with other cartels and bribed government officials to turn a blind eye to his operations. By the early 1980s, Escobar had become one of the richest and most powerful men in Colombia.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nThe Medellín cartel, led by Escobar, dominated the global cocaine trade in the 1980s. The cartel\'s operations were characterized by violence, intimidation, and bribery. Escobar\'s organization was responsible for the murder of thousands of people, including police officers, judges, and politicians who opposed him.\n\n**Notorious Crimes and Escapades**\n\nSome of Escobar\'s most notorious crimes and escapades include:\n\n1. **The assassination of Colombian presidential candidate Luis Carlos Galán**: In 1989, Escobar ordered the assassination of Galán, who was a leading candidate in the Colombian presidential election.\n2. **The bombing of Avianca Flight 203**: In 1989, Escobar\'s cartel bombed a commercial airliner, killing 110 people, in an attempt to kill a key witness against him.\n3. **The escape from La Catedral**: In 1992, Escobar escaped from La Catedral, a luxurious prison he had built for himself in Medellín.\n\n**Downfall and Death**\n\nIn 1991, the Colombian government, with the help of the United States, launched a major operation to capture Escobar. He was eventually tracked down and killed in a shootout with Colombian police on December 1, 1993, in Medellín.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who brought terror and violence to Colombia and beyond. However, he is also seen as a folk hero by some, who view him as a champion of the poor and a symbol of resistance against the Colombian government.\n\n**Popular Culture**\n\nEscobar\'s life and legacy have been the subject of numerous books, films, and TV shows, including:\n\n1. **Narcos** (2015-2017): A Netflix series that tells the story of Escobar\'s rise and fall.\n2. **Escobar: Paradise Lost** (2014): A film that explores the relationship between Escobar and a young surfer who becomes embroiled in his cartel.\n3. **The Two Escobars** (2010): A documentary that examines the intersection of soccer and crime in Colombia during Escobar\'s reign.\n\nOverall, Pablo Escobar\'s life and legacy are a testament to the destructive power of crime and corruption, as well as the enduring fascination with the darker aspects of human nature.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 10:50:00', '2026-06-01 10:50:26', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-06-01 10:50:26', '2026-06-01 10:50:26'),
(3707, 'Auto Post for facebook at 10:53', 'Pablo Escobar (1949-1993) was a Colombian drug lord, crime boss, and leader of the Medellín cartel, one of the most powerful and notorious drug trafficking organizations in history. He is widely regarded as one of the most infamous and successful criminals of the 20th century.\n\n**Early Life and Rise to Power**\n\nPablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria was born on December 1, 1949, in Rionegro, Colombia, to a poor farming family. He grew up in a tough neighborhood in Medellín, where he became involved in street crime and violence at a young age. Escobar\'s early life was marked by poverty, violence, and a strong sense of loyalty to his family and community.\n\nIn the 1970s, Escobar began to build his career as a smuggler and trafficker, initially focusing on small-time operations. He quickly gained a reputation for his cunning, ruthlessness, and ability to evade law enforcement. By the early 1980s, Escobar had become a major player in the Colombian cocaine trade, and his Medellín cartel was making millions of dollars from the lucrative market.\n\n**The Medellín Cartel**\n\nUnder Escobar\'s leadership, the Medellín cartel became one of the most powerful and feared organizations in the world. The cartel\'s operations were characterized by brutal violence, intimidation, and corruption. Escobar and his associates used murder, torture, and bribery to eliminate competitors, silence informants, and influence government officials.\n\nAt the height of its power, the Medellín cartel was responsible for an estimated 80% of the world\'s cocaine supply. Escobar\'s organization was known for its sophisticated smuggling networks, which included the use of submarines, planes, and other advanced transportation methods.\n\n**Personal Life and Excesses**\n\nEscobar\'s personal life was marked by excess and extravagance. He built a luxurious mansion, Hacienda Napoles, which featured a private zoo, a lake, and a collection of rare and exotic animals. He also owned a fleet of cars, including a Mercedes-Benz 600, and was known to have spent millions of dollars on lavish parties and gifts.\n\nEscobar was also a devoted family man and was particularly close to his wife, María Victoria Henao, and their two children. However, his family life was also marked by violence and tragedy, including the assassination of his brother, Roberto, and the kidnapping of his son, Juan Pablo.\n\n**Manhunt and Death**\n\nIn 1991, Escobar surrendered to Colombian authorities and was imprisoned in a specially built prison, La Catedral, which he had designed himself. However, he escaped from the prison in 1992 and went into hiding.\n\nThe Colombian government, with the help of the US DEA and other international agencies, launched a massive manhunt for Escobar. On December 1, 1993, Escobar was shot and killed by Colombian police in a rooftop shootout in Medellín. He was 44 years old at the time of his death.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nPablo Escobar\'s legacy is complex and multifaceted. He is remembered as a ruthless and cunning crime lord who was responsible for the deaths of thousands of people, including innocent civilians, police officers, and rival gang members. However, he is also remembered as a charismatic and calculating leader who was able to build a vast and powerful organization from scratch.\n\nEscobar\'s story has been the subject of numerous books, films, and documentaries, including the popular Netflix series \"Narcos.\" His life and death have also had a lasting impact on Colombian politics and society, and his legacy continues to be felt in the country today.\n\n**Interesting Facts**\n\n* Escobar was known as \"El Patrón\" (The Boss) or \"El Señor\" (The Lord) by his associates and admirers.\n* He was estimated to be worth over $30 billion at the height of his power, making him one of the richest men in the world.\n* Escobar was a fan of soccer and owned a soccer team, Atlético Nacional, which won several championships during his ownership.\n* He was known for his love of animals and had a private zoo at his Hacienda Napoles estate, which featured exotic animals such as lions, tigers, and elephants.\n* Escobar\'s death was celebrated by many Colombians, who saw him as a symbol of violence and corruption. However, others mourned his passing, seeing him as a folk hero and a symbol of resistance against the government and the establishment.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 10:53:00', '2026-06-01 10:53:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/pablo_escobar?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 52, '2026-06-01 10:53:20', '2026-06-01 10:53:20'),
(3708, 'Auto Post for facebook at 11:18', '**Introduction to Dragon Business**\n\nAs a professional dragon business, we strive to provide the best services to our clients. Here are some key points about our business:\n\n* We offer a wide range of services, including fire-breathing performances, treasure hoarding, and medieval-themed events.\n* Our team of experienced dragons is dedicated to providing exceptional customer service and ensuring that our clients are completely satisfied.\n* We take pride in our ability to adapt to any situation and provide customized solutions to meet the unique needs of our clients.\n* At Dragon Business, we value professionalism, integrity, and respect for our clients and the community.\n\n**Follow us on Facebook for updates and behind-the-scenes insights into the world of dragon business!**\n\n#DragonBusiness #ProfessionalServices #FireBreathing #TreasureHoarder #MedievalTheme #CustomerSatisfaction #TrendingNow #BusinessOfTheDay #DragonSquad #FireAndIce #MythicalCreatures #LegendaryBeings #FantasyWorld #AdventureAwaits #DragonFire #BreathingFire #TrendingTopics #FacebookPage #FollowUs #LikeAndShare', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 11:18:00', '2026-06-01 11:18:24', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/A_highly_detailed_fantasy_dragon_flying_over_a_medieval_castle_during_sunset_with_cinematic_lighting_and_dramatic_clouds?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 42, '2026-06-01 11:18:24', '2026-06-01 11:18:24'),
(3709, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:40', 'When it comes to party wear for men, there are many options to choose from, depending on the type of party, the dress code, and personal style. Here are some popular party wear options for men:\n\n1. **Suits**: A well-tailored suit is a classic choice for formal parties. You can opt for a black, navy, or gray suit, and pair it with a crisp white shirt and a tie.\n2. **Blazers**: A blazer can add a touch of sophistication to any outfit. You can wear it with a dress shirt, trousers, and dress shoes for a stylish look.\n3. **Dress Shirts**: A dress shirt is a versatile option that can be dressed up or down. You can pair it with trousers, jeans, or even shorts, depending on the occasion.\n4. **Tuxedos**: If you\'re attending a black-tie event, a tuxedo is a must. Make sure it\'s well-fitted and paired with a bow tie and cummerbund.\n5. **Jeans and a Nice Top**: For a more casual party, you can wear a pair of dark-washed jeans with a nice top, such as a button-down shirt or a polo shirt.\n6. **Jackets and Coats**: A leather jacket or a coat can add an edgy touch to your outfit. You can wear it over a dress shirt and trousers for a stylish look.\n7. **Accessories**: Don\'t forget to add some accessories to complete your outfit. A watch, a pocket square, and a quality belt can make a big difference.\n\nSome popular party wear styles for men include:\n\n1. **Formal**: Suits, tuxedos, and dress shirts are great for formal parties.\n2. **Semi-Formal**: Blazers, dress shirts, and trousers are perfect for semi-formal parties.\n3. **Casual**: Jeans, polo shirts, and sneakers are great for casual parties.\n4. **Smart Casual**: A combination of dressy and casual pieces, such as a blazer with jeans and a dress shirt.\n\nSome popular party wear colors for men include:\n\n1. **Black**: A classic choice for formal parties.\n2. **Navy**: A versatile color that works well for both formal and semi-formal parties.\n3. **Gray**: A great choice for formal and business casual parties.\n4. **White**: A crisp white shirt is a must-have for formal parties.\n5. **Earth Tones**: Brown, beige, and olive green are great for casual and smart casual parties.\n\nRemember, the key to dressing well for a party is to be confident and comfortable in what you\'re wearing. Experiment with different styles and find what works best for you!', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 12:40:00', '2026-06-01 12:40:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Party_Wear_for_Mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 38, '2026-06-01 12:40:22', '2026-06-01 12:40:22'),
(3710, 'Auto Post for facebook at 12:56', 'A formal shirt for men is a type of shirt that is typically worn for business, formal events, and special occasions. Here are some key features and styles of formal shirts for men:\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **Collar style**: Formal shirts usually have a point collar, spread collar, or wingtip collar.\n2. **Cuff style**: Formal shirts often have French cuffs or barrel cuffs.\n3. **Fabric**: Formal shirts are typically made from high-quality fabrics such as cotton, linen, or silk.\n4. **Weave**: Formal shirts often have a tight weave, such as pinpoint or twill.\n5. **Color**: Formal shirts are often white, light blue, or other muted colors.\n6. **Fit**: Formal shirts are designed to fit closely to the body, with a slim fit through the chest and shoulders.\n\n**Styles:**\n\n1. **Dress shirt**: A classic formal shirt with a point collar and French cuffs.\n2. **Business shirt**: A formal shirt with a spread collar and barrel cuffs.\n3. **Tuxedo shirt**: A formal shirt with a wingtip collar and studs.\n4. **Dinner shirt**: A formal shirt with a detachable collar and cuffs.\n5. **Oxford shirt**: A formal shirt with a button-down collar and button cuffs.\n\n**Popular Brands:**\n\n1. **Thomas Pink**: Known for their high-quality, stylish formal shirts.\n2. **Charvet**: A French brand that offers luxurious, bespoke formal shirts.\n3. **Burberry**: A British brand that offers classic, elegant formal shirts.\n4. **Brooks Brothers**: An American brand that offers traditional, high-quality formal shirts.\n5. **Armani**: An Italian brand that offers stylish, modern formal shirts.\n\n**Tips for Choosing a Formal Shirt:**\n\n1. **Consider the occasion**: Choose a shirt that is appropriate for the occasion, such as a white shirt for a wedding or a light blue shirt for a business meeting.\n2. **Think about the fit**: Make sure the shirt fits well, with a slim fit through the chest and shoulders.\n3. **Pay attention to the fabric**: Choose a high-quality fabric that is comfortable and durable.\n4. **Accessories matter**: Consider the type of tie, cufflinks, and other accessories that will complement the shirt.\n5. **Personal style**: Choose a shirt that reflects your personal style and complements your suit and other clothing items.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 12:56:00', '2026-06-01 12:56:25', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/Formal_shirt_for_mens?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 39, '2026-06-01 12:56:25', '2026-06-01 12:56:25'),
