(3729, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:33', 'Football, also known as American football in some countries, is a popular contact team sport played between two teams of eleven players using an oval-shaped ball with pointed ends. The objective is to score points by carrying or throwing the ball into the end zone of the opponent\'s field.\n\nThere are several types of football, including:\n\n1. **American Football**: Played in the United States and Canada, this version is known for its physicality, stoppages in play, and strategic team management.\n2. **Association Football** (or Soccer): Played globally, this version emphasizes speed, agility, and ball control, with an emphasis on scoring goals by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent\'s goal.\n3. **Rugby Football**: A full-contact team sport that originated in the UK, played with an oval-shaped ball and emphasizing physical tackling and territorial gain.\n4. **Australian Rules Football**: A fast-paced, contact team sport played in Australia, with an emphasis on speed, agility, and scoring goals by carrying or kicking the ball through the opponent\'s goalposts.\n\nSome popular football competitions include:\n\n* **National Football League (NFL)**: The top-level American football league in the United States.\n* **FIFA World Cup**: The premier international soccer competition, held every four years.\n* **English Premier League**: A top-tier association football league in England.\n* **Super Bowl**: The annual championship game of the NFL.\n\nFootball is a sport that requires strength, speed, agility, and strategy, with a rich history, diverse rules, and a massive global following. Which type of football are you interested in?', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 16:33:00', '2026-06-01 16:33:30', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/bicycle_kick_hitting_the_top_right_corner?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 53, '2026-06-01 16:33:30', '2026-06-01 16:33:30'),
(3730, 'Auto Post for facebook at 16:42', 'The Yamaha YZF-R1 is a high-performance sport bike produced by Yamaha since 1998. It is known for its impressive power output, agile handling, and sleek design. Here are some key features of the Yamaha R1:\n\n**Engine:**\n- 998cc, liquid-cooled, 4-stroke, DOHC, 16-valve, inline-four engine\n- Produces 200 horsepower (147.9 kW) at 13,500 rpm\n- 82.9 lb-ft (112.4 Nm) of torque at 11,500 rpm\n\n**Transmission:**\n- 6-speed manual transmission with a multi-plate clutch\n\n**Chassis and Suspension:**\n- Aluminum Deltabox frame\n- 43mm inverted fork with 4.7 inches (120mm) of travel\n- Swingarm with 4.7 inches (120mm) of travel, monoshock suspension\n\n**Brakes:**\n- Dual 320mm discs with 4-piston calipers (front)\n- 220mm disc with single-piston caliper (rear)\n\n**Electronics:**\n- 6-axis Inertial Measurement Unit (IMU)\n- Yamaha Ride Control (YRC) with traction control, slide control, lift control, and brake control\n- Cornering ABS\n\n**Other Features:**\n- LED headlights and taillights\n- Digital instrument cluster with color TFT display\n- Cruise control\n\nThe Yamaha R1 is a highly-regarded sport bike that offers exceptional performance, handling, and technology. It is a popular choice among track enthusiasts and street riders alike.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 16:42:00', '2026-06-01 16:42:20', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/r1_bike?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 54, '2026-06-01 16:42:20', '2026-06-01 16:42:20'),
(3731, 'Auto Post for facebook at 17:30', 'Iron Man is a fictional superhero appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by writer and editor Stan Lee, along with artists Don Heck and Jack Kirby, he first appeared in the comic book \"Tales of Suspense #39\" in March 1963.\n\n**Origin Story:**\nTony Stark, a billionaire inventor and industrialist, is kidnapped by a group of terrorists who demand that he build a powerful weapon for them. Instead, Stark uses his intelligence and resources to create a suit of armor, which he uses to escape and later becomes the superhero known as Iron Man.\n\n**Powers and Abilities:**\nIron Man\'s powers come from his advanced suit of armor, which is powered by a high-tech propulsion system and equipped with a range of advanced technologies, including:\n\n* Superhuman strength and durability\n* Flight capabilities\n* Energy projection and repulsor technology\n* Enhanced sensory capabilities, including infrared and X-ray vision\n* Advanced computer systems and artificial intelligence\n\n**Personality:**\nTony Stark, aka Iron Man, is a confident, charismatic, and often arrogant character. He is a self-proclaimed genius and a master strategist, but also has a tendency to be reckless and impulsive. Despite his flaws, he is a deeply committed hero who will stop at nothing to protect the world from threats both human and supernatural.\n\n**Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU):**\nIron Man has been featured in numerous movies and TV shows as part of the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), including:\n\n* Iron Man (2008)\n* The Incredible Hulk (2008)\n* Iron Man 2 (2010)\n* The Avengers (2012)\n* Iron Man 3 (2013)\n* Avengers: Age of Ultron (2015)\n* Captain America: Civil War (2016)\n* Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017)\n* Avengers: Infinity War (2018)\n* Avengers: Endgame (2019)\n\nIn the MCU, Iron Man is played by actor Robert Downey Jr., who has become closely associated with the character and has received widespread critical acclaim for his portrayal.\n\n**Legacy:**\nIron Man has had a significant impact on popular culture, inspiring countless fans around the world with his intelligence, courage, and determination. He has also spawned numerous spin-offs, including video games, animated TV shows, and comic book series, cementing his place as one of the most iconic and beloved superheroes of all time.', '[\"facebook\"]', 'published', 1, NULL, '2026-06-01 17:30:00', '2026-06-01 17:30:22', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/iron_man?width=1024&height=1024&nologo=true', NULL, 'pending', 55, '2026-06-01 17:30:22', '2026-06-01 17:30:22'),
